a lot that could benefit from significant overhaul. A few presentation points like the &quot;storyteller's wall&quot; enforcing a separation of knowledge from the players in <i>and</i> out of character are entirely sensible to throw out.<br /> <br /> The existing fluff fantastic and I expect it will be conserved as something that's unlike anything else in the CofD, but things such as the very specific prerequisites of Utterance tiers and the differentiation of pillars as technically different resources that are only interchangeable sometimes seem like logical points to simplify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 08-18-2017, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:54:22-07:00","id":1130459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130343#post1130343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait until you hear who's developing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo! Who's developing it? Very excited! Enjoyed the 1st edition greatly and am eager to see the transition into 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:55:14-07:00","id":1130461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130459#post1130459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ooo! Who's developing it? Very excited! Enjoyed the 1st edition greatly and am eager to see the transition into 2nd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not my place to say, but I geeked out when I found out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:01:22-07:00","id":1130464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130461#post1130461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not my place to say, but I geeked out when I found out.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> this brings a grin of anticipated geeking out ! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:47:37-07:00","id":1130501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130343#post1130343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait until you hear who's developing it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd guess Malcolm Sheppard, but I think he's busy with Green Ronin now. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130390#post1130390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A teensy bit sad I won't have a chance to work on this, but I'm glad it's actually happening. So I have to ask: <b>what's everyone hoping for out of a new edition?</b><br /> <br /> I'm personally hoping for more support for troupe play right out of the box.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like more emphasis on player cultists. It's a great opportunity for lesser template characters. Mechanically, I'd like to see an update to the Deceived powers that were based on the fixed list of virtues and vices. I'd like to see Memory reworked as its own stat separate from Morality the way Humanity, Wisdom, and so many others were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:53:53-07:00","id":1130508,"title":"","content":"Do you think Utterances will be more freeform and loose, as is the trend for most 2e updates, or will they stay stricter defined abilities like what we got?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:10:12-07:00","id":1130565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130390#post1130390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have to ask: <b>what's everyone hoping for out of a new edition?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a bit of trepidation, honestly. Even mechanically, Mummy remains one of my favourite games in spite of using first edition rules. Coming in at the tail end of the system, it really felt like it made perfect use of the established mechanics and Utterances in particular were exquisitely well balanced. It really struck me going from Mummy to Demon just how slipshod a lot of Demon's mechanics (particularly powers) were by comparison. Sybaris could use some tidying up, but beyond changing the Morality element of Memory to better match second edition and integrating Conditions and Tilts into the mechanics there isn't a huge amount I would change. Maybe raising Mummies' power level in the same manner as most second edition splats, I guess?<br /> <br /> And of course, in terms of the game's world and story I wouldn't change a thing. If Mummy gets a reworking on the same scale as, say, Changeling, I'm going to be real worried.<br /> <br /> But if I had one major point on my wishlist it would be Apotheosis. I hope that the game &quot;taking place&quot; 5-6 years after first edition means that Apotheosis will be a more established element of the setting (going by the release of Rio and the existence of post-Apotheosis Mummies there, that's already first edition's own take on the matter), so more detail on the mechanics of both reaching it and playing as a post-Apotheosis Mummy would be good. I'd even be intrigued by the prospect of making playing post-Apotheosis Mummies be the default and casting regular Mummies as antagonists, but on reflection that strips Mummy of everything that makes it unique in the first place so... better not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:20:25-07:00","id":1130569,"title":"","content":"It would be great if some of the straggling mechanics were consolidated into the core--neithan architecture, talismans, mortal sorcerers, the merits from dark eras that would still apply to modern times, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> It feels like the 1e core's ''storyteller's section'' caused me more confusion in regards to the meta story than clarification. While the Death Cycle was golden, a lot of the extraneous details were so light that they were barely secrets. Plus, some of it implied secrets that later books deny. There are lots of ideas present in the core that felt unnecessary to the game (apotheosis mechanics, details about Anpu besides his silent presence) right out of the gate that could've easily been saved for a supplement, while certain ideas in the supplements change the game setting so thoroughly (talismans, city-wide modifications from architecture or guildmasters) that they were hard to introduce to an ongoing game without a lot of awkwardness (oh... yeah, the temple of sutek ALWAYS doubled your life span.. what, you didn't notice?). I'd be happy if 2e compiles all of the ''need to know'' stuff into the core, shifts all the ''big dirty secrets mummies won't find out until memory 7+ endgame'' stuff into a supplement ... book of going westward maybe? a mechanical and fluff book to portray the judges' dirty secrets and flashbacks in Dust, with a chapter on Iremite history and settings? Yas pleeeease. It took me months to realize I shouldn't be doing pretty much any Irem flashbacks until higher memory kicks in, so having all the secrets and stuff in the core is a bit too tempting. So many other things need to be in the core more than details we won't need till tier 4 endgame anyway.<br /> <br /> I do hope they hring some of the utterances up a notch. The ''life'' focused ones (golden ankh, notably) can be somewhat underwhelming. And while I do love the Guild utterances, they're fairly ''stereotypical'' and one-note, which meant many guildmasters seemed identical to one another. I wouldn't mind there being an easy way to track which Utterances get turned off at what Sekhem. But I don't want to see that mechanic lost.<br /> <br /> Good gravy, please give shuanksen some love! With so few Bane Affinities ever given, that relies far too heavily on home brewing. The Bane Mummies are such compelling antagonists, and the concept of arisen being tainted by them is so juicy, that we NEED more bane affinities. I like amkhata as much as the next guy, but they got more overall love in the gameline than necessary, next to shuanksen. While they definitely made up for the Deceived in the end (more of my players side with them and prefer their storyline), shuanksen never got their own chapter of a book even. Bane mummies need love too, hehe.<br /> <br /> Rather like shuanksen, there were lots of things that got a mention as if there would be more coming later (cosmic utterances, unison utterances). I don't need them in the core, but I'd love to see more of them later, especially unusual ones (non-guild unison, ammut-empowered cosmic , etc ). The corebook needs to have all the bases covered so that any and all supplements can reference them. Variety is the spice of life and all.<br /> <br /> I can't think of much that I'd like to see changed, though, more just updated, reorganized, and streamlined. Mummies could benefit from promethean and vampire style undead body benefits, for example. It probably wouldn't need too much work, hopefully. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T16:50:31-07:00","id":1130592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130569#post1130569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope they hring some of the utterances up a notch. The ''life'' focused ones (golden ankh, notably) can be somewhat underwhelming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeds of Life and Waters of Life and Death were the problem Utterances for me. Golden Ankh got a lot of use from the player who took it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130569#post1130569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bane mummies need love too, hehe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, wait, I ran that game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T19:51:34-07:00","id":1130659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130565#post1130565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And of course, in terms of the game's world and story I wouldn't change a thing. If Mummy gets a reworking on the same scale as, say, Changeling, I'm going to be real worried.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, to me it should be more like Promethean where it's essentially a systems update and not a setting overhaul like Werewolf. Here are some things I've thought about, though:<ul><li>A &quot;Storyteller's Wall&quot; was really unnecessary. For a section claiming to reveal all the secrets we still had to wait for, arguably, two or three future supplements to <i>actually</i> have those secrets revealed. More practically, they hid the relics in this section, too, which is really confounding given that those are clearly character sheet choices.</li> <li>We all know Integrity replaced Morality, but I still like the idea of mummies have dual traits that play into each other. Pretty much every game has its spin on traits and I think this is fine for Mummy, too.</li> <li>A lot of people want all the extra stuff from supplements in the core, but I think a lot of those rules are <i>extra</i> and don't need to be in the baseline core. However, Promethean did a good job of consolidating its 1e material into the new core so I guess it can happen here well.</li> </ul>I also think we need to see the Arisen as compelling characters. Shuankhsen are cool and the Deceived upstaged the rest, I think, so some re-focus would be nice. Book of Going Westward would do well to explore the Judges and their relationship with their servants.<br /> <br /> And obligatory plea for a Night Horrors with ghostly horrors, strange mummy-like monsters created in mimicry of the Rite of Return, mortal sorcerers, cultists, Witnesses, and demons conjured out of Duat. This setting is up there with Mage and Werewolf for weird shit lurking around everywhere but I feel like that really wasn't explored as much as it could have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:01:34-07:00","id":1130667,"title":"","content":"Generally cleaner rules (please make Sybaris a chain of Conditions, I beg you), some supplemental stuff rolled into core, and a chapter about troupe play for the new core with a spicy Night Horrors book would be a dream come true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:30:53-07:00","id":1130680,"title":"","content":"I would like a considerably tighter ruleset, and drawing focus back enough allow people people to build meaningful mummy characters from broader archetypes (akin to most other supernaturals), while still supporting the Iremite paradigm as major force in mummy culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:41:07-07:00","id":1130683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130680#post1130680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like a considerably tighter ruleset, and drawing focus back enough allow people people to build meaningful mummy characters from broader archetypes (akin to most other supernaturals), while still supporting the Iremite paradigm as major force in mummy culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm the opposite there. Any kind of emphasis on player non-Iremite characters and I'm out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Unease Sybaris, specifically, was pretty hard to implement (it really should have been a single status effect akin to Terror Sybaris, not this scaling thing which was hard to keep track of), but what are the other issues with the rules that people took exception to? Mummy surpasses every other game in the Chronicles of Darkness set that I've played in terms of solid mechanics and balance, beating Demon and Promethean handily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:41:27-07:00","id":1130684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130680#post1130680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like a considerably tighter ruleset, and drawing focus back enough allow people people to build meaningful mummy characters from broader archetypes (akin to most other supernaturals), while still supporting the Iremite paradigm as major force in mummy culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would riot if this happened, as would most of the fanbase. Mummy is the story of Irem's heirs, and everyone should just accept that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:44:54-07:00","id":1130686,"title":"","content":"So absolutely zero possibility for some sort happy medium?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:49:20-07:00","id":1130688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130686#post1130686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So absolutely zero possibility for some sort happy medium?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more than happy for non-Iremite Mummies to have their own, separate game? Maybe as something like Revenants?<br /> <br /> But Mummy: The Curse isn't the place for them. The first edition provided two real easy ways to make non-Iremite Mummies, either as byproducts of the Blasphemous Depiction or as ghosts with the Revenant/Intruder Numen. That always felt like a good level for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T20:54:34-07:00","id":1130692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130686#post1130686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So absolutely zero possibility for some sort happy medium?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been years. Promethean is still a game about becoming a human, Demon is still a techgnostic game, and Mummy is still about Irem. There's plenty of room for non-Iremite undead elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:10:35-07:00","id":1130696,"title":"","content":"There are few reasons I'd rather modify Mummy (which is definitely going happen on some level, see every 2nd ed game thusfar), than create Lich: The Liching.<br /> <br /> 1. Its notable inconsistent with the approaches to most of the other gamelines. Mage has the pentacle front and center but its not about Atlantis and one can easily build a character without it. See also: covenants, courts, tribes. All of them have a particular culture that is dominant, but not all-consuming.<br /> <br /> 2. Allocation of resources: Anything that's effectively a spinoff is simply going to get less attention and end up a notably less cohesive and robust game. Even it gets to be a full gameline, it'd mean any Lich book is effort not going towards mummy and vice-versa.<br /> <br /> 3. Elegant Game Design: I think mummy has plenty of strong and meaningful themes and concepts that are perfectly capable of being evocative without having to rely on the Iremite Paradigm. However, having two separate &quot;Ancient Undead Sorcerer-Priest with Multi-Faceted Soul and a Connection to Judgemental Otherworldy Beings&quot; exist simultaneously is pretty ugly design. And since a lot of the Iremite Paradigm is based on IC beliefs and perceptions, its easier to slot it into a greater &quot;This is how Mummies Be&quot; than vice versa. (and even in 1st edition a lot of the &quot;True History&quot; of Irem is IC supposition that fails to take into account important things if you look at the Chronicles of Darkness as a whole. Possible mechanical discrepancies aside, expanding what means to be Mummy doesn't require changing the text of Dreams of Avarice in the slightest.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:23:03-07:00","id":1130699,"title":"","content":"Feel free to modify the game yourself. Just don't ask the text to understand the premise it has emphatically stated for years now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:27:18-07:00","id":1130700,"title":"","content":"I'd rather have an professionally written and designed game that let's me tell the stories I want to tell with it, that doesn't prevent you from telling the stories you want to tell with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:39:13-07:00","id":1130706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130700#post1130700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather have an professionally written and designed game that let's me tell the stories I want to tell with it, that doesn't prevent you from telling the stories you want to tell with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again; this game has set out to tell a specific story. It's not going to change that with a new edition, no more than any other game would, and both the writers and the bulk of the player base wouldn't want it to anyway. You can want what you want however much you like, but Mummy: the Curse is about the Nameless Empire, the servants of it, and just maybe their hope of escaping the cycle of servitude.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:42:59-07:00","id":1130707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130696#post1130696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are few reasons I'd rather modify Mummy (which is definitely going happen on some level, see every 2nd ed game thusfar), than create Lich: The Liching.<br /> <br /> 1. Its notable inconsistent with the approaches to most of the other gamelines. Mage has the pentacle front and center but its not about Atlantis and one can easily build a character without it. See also: covenants, courts, tribes. All of them have a particular culture that is dominant, but not all-consuming.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's not how the others do it&quot; isn't necessarily a bad thing. Mummy does a lot of things the other games don't, for that matter. They're all selling points.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130696#post1130696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Allocation of resources: Anything that's effectively a spinoff is simply going to get less attention and end up a notably less cohesive and robust game. Even it gets to be a full gameline, it'd mean any Lich book is effort not going towards mummy and vice-versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf is committed to bringing out new games on, what, a yearly basis now? Production schedules exist to allow resources to be shared. At some point in a book's development cycle, the writers aren't doing anything and can move to new projects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130696#post1130696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Elegant Game Design: I think mummy has plenty of strong and meaningful themes and concepts that are perfectly capable of being evocative without having to rely on the Iremite Paradigm. However, having two separate &quot;Ancient Undead Sorcerer-Priest with Multi-Faceted Soul and a Connection to Judgemental Otherworldy Beings&quot; exist simultaneously is pretty ugly design. And since a lot of the Iremite Paradigm is based on IC beliefs and perceptions, its easier to slot it into a greater &quot;This is how Mummies Be&quot; than vice versa. (and even in 1st edition a lot of the &quot;True History&quot; of Irem is IC supposition that fails to take into account important things if you look at the Chronicles of Darkness as a whole. Possible mechanical discrepancies aside, expanding what means to be Mummy doesn't require changing the text of Dreams of Avarice in the slightest.)</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't <i>have</i> to rely on the Iremite paradigm, in a strictly meta sense. But there's no reason that any other Mummy has use the same themes and concepts that Iremite mummies do. In fact, I would argue the opposite. Every culture that has made mummies in actual history has done so for different reasons and through different methods. Incan mummies, usually the most widely mentioned alternative when this topic comes up, were mummified through exposure to the elements rather than a ritual process and were the result of sacrifices, not burial traditions. The only reason we even use the word &quot;Mummy&quot; to refer to both these very different cultural artefacts is because, well, English can be lazy. They're only equivalent in the most vaguely superficial terms. So why would the supernatural equivalent be the same beyond the vaguely superficial? Why would non-Iremite mummies use the Egyptian conception of the multi-faced soul, or follow the idea of being servants of the Judges? <br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't think we'd even be having this discussion if English simply had different terms to reflect between the different variants of preserved body. Arguably, if you want to make all Mummies have the same base mechanics, it makes as much sense to extrapolate that out to <i>every</i> burial custom, but I don't see too many people arguing that cremated ashes should also use Mummy mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T21:52:28-07:00","id":1130708,"title":"","content":"The problem is that there <i>are</i> no &quot;broader mummy archetypes.&quot; While several cultures have traditions of preserving their dead, mummies <i>as a horror monster trope</i> are solely associated with Egypt. Vampires, mages, and Prometheans can draw from global culture in ways that mummies can't because they exist in other cultures the way that &quot;risen dead defending ancient tombs&quot; don't.<br /> <br /> For that matter, it's not as if Auspices or Tribes in Werewolf are lined up to cultural archetypes. It's not just Mummy. <br /> <br /> Including &quot;non-Iremite&quot; mummies (whatever the fuck that even means, admittedly) in a Night Horrors book is my way of suggesting a compromise, and expanding the setting.. I certainly don't want them as player options (nor would I like seeing Shuankhsen as player options).<br /> <br /> Promethean isn't about transhumanism and it's not about playing alchemists. Beast isn't about playing Heroes. Yeesh.<br /> <br /> I could sit in on Changeling threads all day about how I hate its themes of trauma and abuse, and how contrived I think it is that there are so many people kidnapped by Gentry that there's secret societies of escapees, but I instead I bite the bullet, accept Changeling the Dreaming as more in my taste, and let other games be what they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T22:20:06-07:00","id":1130718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130706#post1130706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again; this game has set out to tell a specific story. It's not going to change that with a new edition, no more than any other game would, and both the writers and the bulk of the player base wouldn't want it to anyway. You can want what you want however much you like, but Mummy: the Curse is about the Nameless Empire, the servants of it, and just maybe their hope of escaping the cycle of servitude.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If we operate on the assumption that &quot;Mummy has to be about a specific story&quot;, than I'd argue it should be changed on the grounds that Chronicles of Darkness gameline as a whole is intended to be a toolbox, which narrowing what stories can be told conflicts with. I don't actually want to ditch Mummy, but if we're arguing about the pieces of something not fitting the greater whole, Mummy already has a problem.<br /> <br /> Even in the examples you gave, there's some apples and oranges in regards to how they apply. &quot;Techgnosticism&quot; and &quot;Achieving Humanity&quot; are Themes. Irem is not a theme, its a plot element. Plot elements can and do get changed. (See: Covenants, Tribes, Courts, The Time Before.) Its especially weird to latch onto the &quot;History must be the History&quot; given that a major element of the game is the inability to retain information about one's past. A far more ambigious Irem arguably plays into the themes of the game better than &quot;The Heretic is Right About Everything.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130707#post1130707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's not how the others do it&quot; isn't necessarily a bad thing. Mummy does a lot of things the other games don't, for that matter. They're all selling points.</div> </div> </div> </div>The inverse isn't necessarily a good thing either. I certainly don't agree with all of Mummies differences being selling points. Even putting thematics aside, I think 1e Mummies are messy and confusing in unnecessary ways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130707#post1130707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf is committed to bringing out new games on, what, a yearly basis now? Production schedules exist to allow resources to be shared. At some point in a book's development cycle, the writers aren't doing anything and can move to new projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Changing Breeds book has issues and nothing else came of the War Against the Pure versions. Still waiting on quality approach to non-wolf changers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130708#post1130708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including &quot;non-Iremite&quot; mummies (whatever the fuck that even means, admittedly) in a Night Horrors book is my way of suggesting a compromise, and expanding the setting.. I certainly don't want them as player options (nor would I like seeing Shuankhsen as player options).</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal preference is essentially the reverse of this idea. The Iremite paradigm is the overwhelmingly largest piece of the still larger puzzle that is being a Mummy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130708#post1130708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> could sit in on Changeling threads all day about how I hate its themes of trauma and abuse, and how contrived I think it is that there are so many people kidnapped by Gentry that there's secret societies of escapees, but I instead I bite the bullet, accept Changeling the Dreaming as more in my taste, and let other games be what they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still want to play an &quot;Ancient Ancient Undead Sorcerer-Priest with Multi-Faceted Soul and a Connection to Judgemental Otherworldy Beings&quot; and I don't want the Iremite Paradigm thrown out. I don't want to change the Themes or the Moods of the game. (I do want to change the mechanics, but for purely logistical reasons.) All I'm looking for is more flexibility in who my character is when I design them, or at least enough empty spaces and unanswered questions to fake it. <br /> <br /> Ultimately I'm here because I like Mummy, and I want to like it more than already do. However, I'm getting a &quot;no true mummy fan&quot; vibe on an opinion that couldn't be about anything else.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T22:22:14-07:00","id":1130719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130708#post1130708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that there <i>are</i> no &quot;broader mummy archetypes.&quot; While several cultures have traditions of preserving their dead, mummies <i>as a horror monster trope</i> are solely associated with Egypt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well...there was that one time Hollywood did this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img.soundtrackcollector.com/movie/large/Mummy_tomb_emperor_(2008).jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ...which to be fair, looks like DE2 will be sort of covering this in their &quot;Rise of the Last Imperials&quot; Era. So eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T22:31:56-07:00","id":1130721,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"526\" data-vbnamecard=\"526\">schizoPOP</a> Point of order, the other shifters have shown up again; Dark Eras 1 had the bull shifters in The Sundered World, and the Beast Fiction Anthology has a Bastet in on of the stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T22:33:14-07:00","id":1130722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130719#post1130719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well...there was that one time Hollywood did this:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://img.soundtrackcollector.com/movie/large/Mummy_tomb_emperor_(2008).jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> ...which to be fair, looks like DE2 will be sort of covering this in their &amp;quot;Rise of the Last Imperials&amp;quot; Era. So eh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey now, I'm quite proud of my evil kung fu Deceived Cult!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T22:43:07-07:00","id":1130725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130718#post1130718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we operate on the assumption that &quot;Mummy has to be about a specific story&quot;, than I'd argue it should be changed on the grounds that Chronicles of Darkness gameline as a whole is intended to be a toolbox, which narrowing what stories can be told conflicts with. I don't actually want to ditch Mummy, but if we're arguing about the pieces of something not fitting the greater whole, Mummy already has a problem.<br /> <br /> Even in the examples you gave, there's some apples and oranges in regards to how they apply. &quot;Techgnosticism&quot; and &quot;Achieving Humanity&quot; are Themes. Irem is not a theme, its a plot element. Plot elements can and do get changed. (See: Covenants, Tribes, Courts, The Time Before.) Its especially weird to latch onto the &quot;History must be the History&quot; given that a major element of the game is the inability to retain information about one's past. A far more ambigious Irem arguably plays into the themes of the game better than &quot;The Heretic is Right About Everything.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I could happily argue the opposite. Memory as a mechanic only works if <i>there is something to remember</i>. The strive to find out what happened in ones' past works a hell of a lot less effectively if there is no past to remember. Ambiguity reinforces the unease and horror present at the game's start, but it actively obstructs the catharsis and promise necessary for a strong endgame.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130718#post1130718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inverse isn't necessarily a good thing either. I certainly don't agree with all of Mummies differences being selling points. Even putting thematics aside, I think 1e Mummies are messy and confusing in unnecessary ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, it's not necessarily a good thing, but in Mummy's case I've found most of them to be good. A strong, concrete backstory to give the characters something to remember is one of those elements that has benefited Mummy where it wouldn't, say, Vampire.<br /> <br /> Your mileage may vary but I don't think there's much more to be said beyond, &quot;You're wrong!&quot; &quot;No, you're wrong!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130718#post1130718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Changing Breeds book has issues and nothing else came of the War Against the Pure versions. Still waiting on quality approach to non-wolf changers.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have Geist, Promethean, Mummy, and Vampire, all dealing with variations on the theme of revenants, the dead, and/or eternity in different ways. They're all support. I'm sure a lich/revenant game could find its own niche easily. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130718#post1130718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ultimately I'm here because I like Mummy, and I want to like it more than already do. However, I'm getting a &quot;no true mummy fan&quot; vibe on an opinion that couldn't be about anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, less that mentality and more that it's an old, old argument that's been played out many times before. That's why it's drawing comparisons to the transhumanism/techgnosticism arguments of our subforums. It's not that &quot;no true Mummy fan&quot; wants non-Iremite Mummies, but that the consensus from the game's writers and a pretty big chunk of the fan base is that such creatures would be better off in a separate game line or blue book. They're not part of <i>Mummy: The Curse</i>, largely because of the aforementioned point about there being no reason for a substantive link between Iremite Mummies and non-Iremite Mummies beyond English linguistics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T00:41:38-07:00","id":1130738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130707#post1130707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;It's not how the others do it&amp;quot; isn't necessarily a bad thing. Mummy does a lot of things the other games don't, for that matter. They're all selling points.<br /> <br /> <br /> White Wolf is committed to bringing out new games on, what, a yearly basis now? Production schedules exist to allow resources to be shared. At some point in a book's development cycle, the writers aren't doing anything and can move to new projects.<br /> <br /> <br /> They don't <i>have</i> to rely on the Iremite paradigm, in a strictly meta sense. But there's no reason that any other Mummy has use the same themes and concepts that Iremite mummies do. In fact, I would argue the opposite. Every culture that has made mummies in actual history has done so for different reasons and through different methods. Incan mummies, usually the most widely mentioned alternative when this topic comes up, were mummified through exposure to the elements rather than a ritual process and were the result of sacrifices, not burial traditions. The only reason we even use the word &amp;quot;Mummy&amp;quot; to refer to both these very different cultural artefacts is because, well, English can be lazy. They're only equivalent in the most vaguely superficial terms. So why would the supernatural equivalent be the same beyond the vaguely superficial? Why would non-Iremite mummies use the Egyptian conception of the multi-faced soul, or follow the idea of being servants of the Judges? <br /> <br /> Frankly, I don't think we'd even be having this discussion if English simply had different terms to reflect between the different variants of preserved body. Arguably, if you want to make all Mummies have the same base mechanics, it makes as much sense to extrapolate that out to <i>every</i> burial custom, but I don't see too many people arguing that cremated ashes should also use Mummy mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who is this White Wolf you mention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T05:11:13-07:00","id":1130779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130718#post1130718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still want to play an &quot;Ancient Ancient Undead Sorcerer-Priest with Multi-Faceted Soul and a Connection to Judgemental Otherworldy Beings&quot; and I don't want the Iremite Paradigm thrown out. I don't want to change the Themes or the Moods of the game. (I do want to change the mechanics, but for purely logistical reasons.) All I'm looking for is more flexibility in who my character is when I design them, or at least enough empty spaces and unanswered questions to fake it.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I'm here because I like Mummy, and I want to like it more than already do. However, I'm getting a &quot;no true mummy fan&quot; vibe on an opinion that couldn't be about anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess the question is, &quot;What kind of character do you want to play that isn't supported in Mummy but still fits into that game?&quot;<br /> <br /> That question has been asked by many people to many people in many threads already, and I'd hate to see this thread about the long-awaited second edition announcement turn into something we're all exhausted debating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T07:16:17-07:00","id":1130809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130738#post1130738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who is this White Wolf you mention?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't they still your publishers or something? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But yeah, I did mean Onyx Path. I have a hard enough time not calling these games &quot;World of Darkness&quot; as it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T08:41:25-07:00","id":1130835,"title":"","content":"I'd figured this would be coming, but not quite so soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130659#post1130659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, to me it should be more like Promethean where it's essentially a systems update and not a setting overhaul like Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. The only substantive change I'd like to see in the setting is for a a more explicit distinction made between the levels the concept of Guild operates on: the ancient organisations that existed in Irem, the lingering philosophies among the Deathless informed by them (with the possibility that a given Deathless might have come to identify with the philosophy of a different Guild from which they were a member), and the modern organisations formed around those philosophies (which seem like they should come and go based on mummy populations, especially Sothic turns, and may bear little resemblance to their forebears).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A &quot;Storyteller's Wall&quot; was really unnecessary. For a section claiming to reveal all the secrets we still had to wait for, arguably, two or three future supplements to <i>actually</i> have those secrets revealed. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We all know Integrity replaced Morality, but I still like the idea of mummies have dual traits that play into each other. Pretty much every game has its spin on traits and I think this is fine for Mummy, too. </div> </div> </div>Memory and another Integritype you mean? What would you have in mind?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A lot of people want all the extra stuff from supplements in the core, but I think a lot of those rules are <i>extra</i> and don't need to be in the baseline core. However, Promethean did a good job of consolidating its 1e material into the new core so I guess it can happen here well. </div> </div> </div>The only supplemental thing that comes to mind that I'd love to see in the core are the seba. Not the Deceived (except inasmuch as the Deathless presume the seba are associated with them in much the same way as the five types of relic are associated with the Guilds). But the seba are a great concept, both for Mummy's cosmic air, and the sweep of history.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130708#post1130708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including &quot;non-Iremite&quot; mummies (whatever the fuck that even means, admittedly) in a Night Horrors book is my way of suggesting a compromise, and expanding the setting.. I certainly don't want them as player options (nor would I like seeing Shuankhsen as player options).</div> </div> </div> </div>While you're calling it a compromise, for my part, this is all I've ever wanted (except inasmuch as I'd offer enough to make them playable, much as Wicked Dead with its plethora of vampires). Mummy has three big areas for Night Horror: the darkness of history (mummies, people who have lived past their time, relics, Iremite ruins, Lifeless), the cosmos (Duat and other realms), and a world that will insist on doing things when the Deathless aren't around (which can include modern scholars and explorers - but also other peoples' interactions with Sekhem - including relics outside the five types, unusual forms of amkhata, non-Iremite ruins, and other attempts at creating Sekhem-infused beings, some of which use preserved bodies in which to root the magic, others not). My fantasy would be a book for all three: maybe Deathless Years, Black Stars, and I don't know what to call the other, maybe Forbidden Treasures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 08-18-2017, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T12:59:03-07:00","id":1130933,"title":"","content":"The first edition was basically a giant mess, which was tragic because it had such a strong concept and really powerful writing by a number of people. Unfortunately, there were also huge inconsistencies that the developer preferred to ignore than fix, particularly questions like &quot;how do mummies have an active, functional society when they're defined by being amnesiacs who are inanimate corpses most of the time&quot; or &quot;what do Guilds actually <i>do </i>given that none of them actually do the job that defines them any more?&quot; The divide between player knowledge and GM knowledge was pretty much never a positive addition, and the game eventually gave up on it anyway. Then there's stuff like the Deceived, who are identical to Arisen in every way except that basically everything about them has some small fiddly difference, just because. (Also their entire book was word salad.)<br /> <br /> That said, a second edition has a lot of promise! The concept of these ancient, powerful beings slowly awakening to the understanding that they're slaves and slave-takers, and the theme of there not being much difference between the ancient world and the modern one... it has <i>huge </i>amounts of promise. It just needs to be handled by someone who's prepared to reconcile all the aspects of the game into a more harmonious whole.<br /> <br /> (I honestly think they should shrink the game's scope a bit, to make it clear that it's really about the journey towards freedom and nothing else, like Promethean, because the bait-and-switch of the first edition caused a lot of its problems.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:53:10-07:00","id":1130960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130933#post1130933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first edition was basically a giant mess, which was tragic because it had such a strong concept and really powerful writing by a number of people. Unfortunately, there were also huge inconsistencies that the developer preferred to ignore than fix, particularly questions like &amp;quot;how do mummies have an active, functional society when they're defined by being amnesiacs who are inanimate corpses most of the time&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;what do Guilds actually <i>do </i>given that none of them actually do the job that defines them any more?&amp;quot; The divide between player knowledge and GM knowledge was pretty much never a positive addition, and the game eventually gave up on it anyway. Then there's stuff like the Deceived, who are identical to Arisen in every way except that basically everything about them has some small fiddly difference, just because. (Also their entire book was word salad.)<br /> <br /> That said, a second edition has a lot of promise! The concept of these ancient, powerful beings slowly awakening to the understanding that they're slaves and slave-takers, and the theme of there not being much difference between the ancient world and the modern one... it has <i>huge </i>amounts of promise. It just needs to be handled by someone who's prepared to reconcile all the aspects of the game into a more harmonious whole.<br /> <br /> (I honestly think they should shrink the game's scope a bit, to make it clear that it's really about the journey towards freedom and nothing else, like Promethean, because the bait-and-switch of the first edition caused a lot of its problems.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I take some offence at the idea that the Deceived were scarcely different from the Arisen, and their book is firmly my all-time favorite CofD supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:40:25-07:00","id":1131009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130835#post1130835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Memory and another Integritype you mean? What would you have in mind?<br /> ...<br /> While you're calling it a compromise, for my part, this is all I've ever wanted (except inasmuch as I'd offer enough to make them playable, much as Wicked Dead with its plethora of vampires). Mummy has three big areas for Night Horror: the darkness of history (mummies, people who have lived past their time, relics, Iremite ruins, Lifeless), the cosmos (Duat and other realms), and a world that will insist on doing things when the Deathless aren't around (which can include modern scholars and explorers - but also other peoples' interactions with Sekhem - including relics outside the five types, unusual forms of amkhata, non-Iremite ruins, and other attempts at creating Sekhem-infused beings, some of which use preserved bodies in which to root the magic, others not). My fantasy would be a book for all three: maybe Deathless Years, Black Stars, and I don't know what to call the other, maybe Forbidden Treasures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Couldn't we just use Integrity? You make up stuff that are your breaking points and then remember them as Memory increases.<br /> <br /> I agree with making non-Iremite mummies playable via sidebar Wicked Dead style; that's how I thought they would introduce Sekhem sorcerers, actually. That's a beautiful layout of the game, too; I always broke down my imaginary Night Horrors into three chapters of The Living, The Dead, and The Deathless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130933#post1130933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first edition was basically a giant mess, which was tragic because it had such a strong concept and really powerful writing by a number of people. Unfortunately, there were also huge inconsistencies that the developer preferred to ignore than fix, particularly questions like &quot;how do mummies have an active, functional society when they're defined by being amnesiacs who are inanimate corpses most of the time&quot; or &quot;what do Guilds actually <i>do </i>given that none of them actually do the job that defines them any more?&quot;<br /> ...<br /> (I honestly think they should shrink the game's scope a bit, to make it clear that it's really about the journey towards freedom and nothing else, like Promethean, because the bait-and-switch of the first edition caused a lot of its problems.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the core book states that you remember everything necessary about your Guild at Memory 2, which is lower than the default starting level of Arisen PCs. <i>Guildhalls of the Deathless</i> also introduced talismans which help with the issue as well. To say that there was <i>no </i>effort, or even poor effort, is kinda inaccurate. However, I remember the core claiming that, perhaps moreso than even vampires, the Deathless are the most 'political' splat with their Guilds and all, and <i>that</i> is an unnecessary and inaccurate claim; I hope second edition doesn't try to sell us so hard on MUMMIES BEING COOL XXHARDCOREXX WE RUN NIGHT CLUBS TOO IN OUR QUICKSTART PC BOOK.<br /> <br /> While it might be interesting to develop Mummy into just a game about Apotheosis I wouldn't want it defined by it. It gives Mummy one of its unique selling points anyway: in Vampire Golconda is a myth and in Promethean the New Dawn is standard experience, but Mummy is in between where Apotheosis is rare and unheard of but actually (secretly) possible. It's also a twist to say that striving towards Apotheosis makes you a rebel, rather than Promethean where quitting the Pilgrimage makes you a rebel. \u200bPromethean villains like the Centimanni are defined by choosing to <i>quit</i> the Pilgrimage; we don't need that for mummies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:09:55-07:00","id":1131018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130960#post1130960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I take some offence at the idea that the Deceived were scarcely different from the Arisen, and their book is firmly my all-time favorite CofD supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically they're different, but mechanically basically everybody about them is &quot;like the Arisen, but with one fiddly difference.&quot; It winds up with them having a <i>bunch</i> of fiddly little differences that wind up turning into this giant package without really adding anything to the experience.<br /> <br /> Then the stuff about them that's actually important, like having a temakh in your head all the time, is basically absent from the play experience. There's huge amounts of words spent on the guildmasters and their personalities and their wants, but <i>they can't talk.</i> There's no way for the player to even find out what they want unless the ST just, like, tells you or something. For something that's supposed to be their defining torment it's not a proper part of play at all, and the temakh descriptions are some of the most overwritten stuff White Wolf has ever done, which is honestly kind of an accomplishment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:21:45-07:00","id":1131024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131009#post1131009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't we just use Integrity? You make up stuff that are your breaking points and then remember them as Memory increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting... and... what if Integrity also comes with a mental analogue to Touchstones? Something that would a comfort or pleasure in Irem whose echoes can bring solace to the mummy now. And such a Touchstone can bolster the Deathless against Descent rolls for violating the Judge's will? Memory lets them recover their humanity/integrity, and if they can maintain their integrity, it allows them to claim back a little control over the currents of their Sekhem?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree with making non-Iremite mummies playable via sidebar Wicked Dead style; that's how I thought they would introduce Sekhem sorcerers, actually. </div> </div> </div>And that maintains Iremite and Shan'iatu primacy, which I agree is necessary. (Hey, have we finally made peace on this issue!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's a beautiful layout of the game, too; I always broke down my imaginary Night Horrors into three chapters of The Living, The Dead, and The Deathless. </div> </div> </div>Thankyou.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, I remember the core claiming that, perhaps moreso than even vampires, the Deathless are the most 'political' splat with their Guilds and all, and <i>that</i> is an unnecessary and inaccurate claim; I hope second edition doesn't try to sell us so hard on MUMMIES BEING COOL XXHARDCOREXX WE RUN NIGHT CLUBS TOO IN OUR QUICKSTART PC BOOK. </div> </div> </div>Also, politics runs pretty low on the list of things that interest me about the Mummy setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:42:49-07:00","id":1131034,"title":"","content":"God, those premade characters. Eugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:54:35-07:00","id":1131038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131024#post1131024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... and... what if Integrity also comes with a mental analogue to Touchstones? Something that would a comfort or pleasure in Irem whose echoes can bring solace to the mummy now. And such a Touchstone can bolster the Deathless against Descent rolls for violating the Judge's will? Memory lets them recover their humanity/integrity, and if they can maintain their integrity, it allows them to claim back a little control over the currents of their Sekhem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I'd like to see Memory expanded to cover a general sense of self and map some of the bouncing power level mechanics to that. Give the conflict between autonomy and the powerful forces that drive the mummy condition a more consistent and immediate relevancy to player activities.<br /> <br /> (Also creating more of a grey area between Guild Zealot and Heretic puts more space to put in thing that don't perfectly fit the Iremite Paradigm. Wee ulterior motives.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:24:29-07:00","id":1131048,"title":"","content":"I can agree with Deceived being a bit fidly-- Its hard to keep track of their true forms sometimes during intense game sessions when WP would be bleeding out like from a sieve, and their Utterances are really awesome but honestly hard to remember and keep track of (blessed of dead stars, btw, is impossible to convert to freeform diceless RP). The way I handled the Temakh is a bit more like Werewolf, or hopefully 2e Geist. I instructed my players to begin play as the Temakh, mentally speaking. Unlike Arisen, who are damn near blank slates when they wake up, I told the Deceived player to imagine themself AS the Musician, full of wrath and hubris and talking like he remembers the primordial nights and only has a passing grasp on actual human life. Then, like an arisen, as Memory increased, he started having flashbacks and memories of himself as a distinct person, and even began struggling so much against his Temakh that he is trying to ally with the Arisen and find the Dreams of Avarice. I do adore the Deceived, but it would be nice to see all mummies keep the Descent of Power and Ascent of memory, without having a billion variables and things to keep track of and (ironically) remember.<br /> <br /> It could be simple things, like a space on the character sheet for room to tell each Utterance's prerequisites so you can remember when they're inaccessible during descent, or if they have the Pillar requirements for the first and third tier but not the second, what specific pillar costs are involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 08-18-2017, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T19:55:48-07:00","id":1131091,"title":"","content":"In broad strokes...<br /> <br /> 1. While all of the books were well-done, I felt that a lot of effort went into Deceived that could have gone into exploring a lot of core story and mechanical elements of the Arisen. Cults deserve their own book, expanding not only on the mechanical elements, but the relationships between Arisen and their cults, and the role of the cults in a society where many of the Arisen in an area will slumber at any given time, and the utilization of grasp and reach. In some ways, the cultists of the Deceived have received more attention than those of the Arisen. There wasn't much development of the Shaunkhsen and human antagonists (though the latter is expanded in non-Mummy books). <br /> <br /> 2. Some of the mechanics seem to exist independent of one another (probably as a consequence of being introduced across multiple books). I think that the Arisen are balanced between two mechanics in tension with each other: Memory and Sekhem. That's a great idea and it works well in many regards, but I think there's a lot of opportunity to pull in the mechanics of relics, vessels, cults, and architecture to address the tension with some effort. The options currently available (affinities like entombed glory and utterance of the silenced vessel give some options to overcome dwindling Sekhem, while architecture can buttress memory or power) are there but feel more patched on than part of a coherent effort by an immortal seeking to grapple with the limitations of its condition (or embracing them to better serve its masters). I'd like to see something like the Vampire 2E linking of banes with Humanity, save in this case, it's a matter of mittigating (or amplifying) the tension between self and power. <br /> <br /> 3. More consistency in terms of the affinity and utterance mechanics. Interesting and evocative, the powers demand a fairly idiosyncratic understanding of how they work. I think some of the streamlining in terms of how they work in 2E would be advisable. The Mutapa chapter of the Dark Eras Companion offers some examples of how they think of this working in the Clash of Wills language, and I'd love to see it expanded. <br /> <br /> 4. Pillars feel a bit tacked on, and I'd like to see them linked directly to roleplaying decisions made by players in a way they currently aren't, perhaps in a way reflective of the updates to Werewolf renown. I love the idea of having two different power sources fueling the affinities and utterances. However, it feels a bit odd to rely solely on willpower to fuel affinities, while access to them rests with pillars. Am I the only one who thinks that? <br /> <br /> 5. I'd like to see some thought to apotheosis as an alternative play style. It radically shifts the play style and themes, but is itself inherently interesting. While the Heretic is presented as something of a White Knight fighting against the evil of the Judges, I think there's a lot of variety in stories about someone who has regained a sense of self at the cost of much of their power. The potential problem I see is in trying to distinguish it from the circumstances of a Demon who has rebelled against the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T20:08:35-07:00","id":1131098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131091#post1131091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The potential problem I see is in trying to distinguish it from the circumstances of a Demon who has rebelled against the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons only get more powerful the further they get in their rebellion, and if you're talking about their initial Fall that happens in the course of a moment. For one of the Arisen to choose the path of Apotheosis isn't to fall, it's to deliberately spend likely multiple Descents consciously working towards defying their godlike masters and choosing to lose their power.<br /> <br /> There's a lot of difference there, is what I'm trying to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T21:50:51-07:00","id":1131120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131091#post1131091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In broad strokes...<br /> <br /> 1. While all of the books were well-done, I felt that a lot of effort went into Deceived that could have gone into exploring a lot of core story and mechanical elements of the Arisen. Cults deserve their own book, expanding not only on the mechanical elements, but the relationships between Arisen and their cults, and the role of the cults in a society where many of the Arisen in an area will slumber at any given time, and the utilization of grasp and reach. In some ways, the cultists of the Deceived have received more attention than those of the Arisen. There wasn't much development of the Shaunkhsen and human antagonists (though the latter is expanded in non-Mummy books).<br /> <br /> 2. Some of the mechanics seem to exist independent of one another (probably as a consequence of being introduced across multiple books). I think that the Arisen are balanced between two mechanics in tension with each other: Memory and Sekhem. That's a great idea and it works well in many regards, but I think there's a lot of opportunity to pull in the mechanics of relics, vessels, cults, and architecture to address the tension with some effort. The options currently available (affinities like entombed glory and utterance of the silenced vessel give some options to overcome dwindling Sekhem, while architecture can buttress memory or power) are there but feel more patched on than part of a coherent effort by an immortal seeking to grapple with the limitations of its condition (or embracing them to better serve its masters). I'd like to see something like the Vampire 2E linking of banes with Humanity, save in this case, it's a matter of mittigating (or amplifying) the tension between self and power.<br /> <br /> 3. More consistency in terms of the affinity and utterance mechanics. Interesting and evocative, the powers demand a fairly idiosyncratic understanding of how they work. I think some of the streamlining in terms of how they work in 2E would be advisable. The Mutapa chapter of the Dark Eras Companion offers some examples of how they think of this working in the Clash of Wills language, and I'd love to see it expanded.<br /> <br /> 4. Pillars feel a bit tacked on, and I'd like to see them linked directly to roleplaying decisions made by players in a way they currently aren't, perhaps in a way reflective of the updates to Werewolf renown. I love the idea of having two different power sources fueling the affinities and utterances. However, it feels a bit odd to rely solely on willpower to fuel affinities, while access to them rests with pillars. Am I the only one who thinks that?<br /> <br /> 5. I'd like to see some thought to apotheosis as an alternative play style. It radically shifts the play style and themes, but is itself inherently interesting. While the Heretic is presented as something of a White Knight fighting against the evil of the Judges, I think there's a lot of variety in stories about someone who has regained a sense of self at the cost of much of their power. The potential problem I see is in trying to distinguish it from the circumstances of a Demon who has rebelled against the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, most of it. I don't know how many of you got to see CWoD's Mummy second edition, but... you chose the ''job'' you had in ancient Egypt, and each ''pillar'' was not only distinct in fluff but distinct in mechanics. Ba would literally affect how easily you could wander the Twilight and underworld, KA would literally help defend your corpse as it rested. The hardcover CWoD book that Mummies got was definitely not what I wanted but it expanded the ''pillars'' a lot. Honestly, I'd like to see a lot more of that. Make sure Ba powers feel like your soul has taken up mobility and wanders, make Ka feel like it is enhancing your body and tomb. Make sheut cast its shadow on you and what you so. Making each Pillar more flavorful and solid would help a LOT. It'd be easier to remember which powers go where from theme alone. Heck, even changing Utterance lists from alphabetical to Pillar based would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T03:45:28-07:00","id":1131175,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2096\" data-vbnamecard=\"2096\">willywonka</a> this, especially the cult and pillar stuff.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar935_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"935\" data-vbnamecard=\"935\">Cleverest of Things</a> That sounds kind of cool, actually. I'd like something similar in approach in this Mummy, too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:09:00-07:00","id":1131191,"title":"","content":"As a huge fan of 1st edition, I am glad 2nd ed is happening. Also hoping that 2nd edition does not diminish the material but rather serve as both an consolidation and update. Having the component systems interact from the start would be a huge boon and would allow for greater interactions between them.<br /> <br /> As far as the setting material goes, I would prefer the Judges, Anpu and Pillars get more of the spotlight but I don't want the Deceived and other elements reduced drastically. I am fine with them being pushed to a mostly storyteller section or the hypothetical &quot;Player's Guide&quot; or the &quot;Storytellers Guide&quot; but should be useable antagonists in the Core.<br /> <br /> Guidelines for STs to create Relics and Vessels (and the difference between the two) would be nice; Reliquary was a fantastic book but between the from the previous edition and it is not useful in determining a crucial detail about relics, the associated guild. Something akin to the Amkhat creation rules (minus construction requirements for relics at least).<br /> <br /> More details on how the social structures work would be nice: guilds, nomes, menats and cults should be something the characters (most of them anyway) should be used too and the interactions between them should be relatively frequent. Even when the Arisen is in Duat, the cult still functions, carrying on their duties, which can and should include monitoring cults of allies (menat), performing support functions for their 'god' (guild duties when at rest) and representing their master's interest in the local area (nome). And that is before personal agendas and beliefs are in the mix.<br /> <br /> I don't really want to lose anything, though some things may need to change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:14:12-07:00","id":1131193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131024#post1131024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting... and... what if Integrity also comes with a mental analogue to Touchstones? Something that would a comfort or pleasure in Irem whose echoes can bring solace to the mummy now. And such a Touchstone can bolster the Deathless against Descent rolls for violating the Judge's will? Memory lets them recover their humanity/integrity, and if they can maintain their integrity, it allows them to claim back a little control over the currents of their Sekhem?<br /> ...<br /> And that maintains Iremite and Shan'iatu primacy, which I agree is necessary. (Hey, have we finally made peace on this issue!? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see relics being some sort of Touchstone, or at least ones made into talismans. Maybe <i>that's</i> why they're so important to mummies.<br /> <br /> Well, I don't know if we made peace because I don't think I ever disagreed with you on the issue. I've been preaching my &quot;non-Iremite mummies in Night Horrors&quot; for (probably literally) years now. I never thought they should be playable by default, or even in a supplement unless it were done in a side-bar. I'm never sure what peoples' 'non-Egyptian' character concepts are when they're playing a game about Egyptian monsters and mythology <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>willywonka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131091#post1131091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. While all of the books were well-done, I felt that a lot of effort went into Deceived that could have gone into exploring a lot of core story and mechanical elements of the Arisen. Cults deserve their own book, expanding not only on the mechanical elements, but the relationships between Arisen and their cults, and the role of the cults in a society where many of the Arisen in an area will slumber at any given time, and the utilization of grasp and reach. In some ways, the cultists of the Deceived have received more attention than those of the Arisen. There wasn't much development of the Shaunkhsen and human antagonists (though the latter is expanded in non-Mummy books).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. I love the Deceived and am thankful for their lore, focus, and <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> and even the Cleopatra Dark Era for expanding the Iremite mythology first introduced in <i>Book of the Deceived</i>, but I'd definitely like to see the Arisen back in more of a spotlight (of course in the 2e core they would be regardless, I suppose). When I first read the core I was like, &quot;Oh, wow, cool, the Egyptian gods don't matter but these Judges do - interesting!&quot; Then we missed a stretch goal so we never saw them again (I think there was a cool poem in <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> about them, though).<br /> <br /> Frankly, the Arisen are a little boring when you compare them to Shuankhsen who have bane relics, command amkhata, and eat your face, and Deceived whose example relics includes <i>stardust</i>, are possessed by hauntingly vivid demon god-spirits, and are masters of true names. I know the Arisen are there as the baseline and cover the standard mummy expectations, but they just seem so less...cool? I'm not sure if I have a solution for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T05:26:02-07:00","id":1131203,"title":"","content":"What the heck are Bane Relics anyway? It was never explained (though based on their name, I am assuming they are relics in synch with the Devourer). It would be nice if they say so in the books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:26:16-07:00","id":1131230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1130721#post1130721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Point of order, the other shifters have shown up again; Dark Eras 1 had the bull shifters in The Sundered World, and the Beast Fiction Anthology has a Bastet in on of the stories.</div> </div> </div> </div> I found the Bastet tie to the Astral plane interesting in that story, makes them more different from Werewolves, harbringer of things to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T06:28:29-07:00","id":1131231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131193#post1131193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see relics being some sort of Touchstone, or at least ones made into talismans. Maybe <i>that's</i> why they're so important to mummies.<br /> <br /> Well, I don't know if we made peace because I don't think I ever disagreed with you on the issue. I've been preaching my &amp;quot;non-Iremite mummies in Night Horrors&amp;quot; for (probably literally) years now. I never thought they should be playable by default, or even in a supplement unless it were done in a side-bar. I'm never sure what peoples' 'non-Egyptian' character concepts are when they're playing a game about Egyptian monsters and mythology <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree with this. I love the Deceived and am thankful for their lore, focus, and <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> and even the Cleopatra Dark Era for expanding the Iremite mythology first introduced in <i>Book of the Deceived</i>, but I'd definitely like to see the Arisen back in more of a spotlight (of course in the 2e core they would be regardless, I suppose). When I first read the core I was like, &amp;quot;Oh, wow, cool, the Egyptian gods don't matter but these Judges do - interesting!&amp;quot; Then we missed a stretch goal so we never saw them again (I think there was a cool poem in <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> about them, though).<br /> <br /> Frankly, the Arisen are a little boring when you compare them to Shuankhsen who have bane relics, command amkhata, and eat your face, and Deceived whose example relics includes <i>stardust</i>, are possessed by hauntingly vivid demon god-spirits, and are masters of true names. I know the Arisen are there as the baseline and cover the standard mummy expectations, but they just seem so less...cool? I'm not sure if I have a solution for this.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree, both antagonist splats seem to outshine Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T12:58:46-07:00","id":1131395,"title":"","content":"I found out about Mummy after 2nd editions games had started coming out, so I'm delighted to hear this. The mechanics were always rooted in 1st edition stuff that didn't survive the transition, so I'm hoping for some streamlining there. I don't think the fluff needs much change, just a summarized and clearer presentation (and none of that Player/GM separation stuff, thank you)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T13:22:01-07:00","id":1131410,"title":"","content":"I forgot to add my bit about the dead. I think a decision needs to be made regarding the role of ghosts and revenants in Mummy. As presented, they can serve as retainers and minor antagonists in the vein seen in the rest of the ChroD. In that case, I think the mechanics from the core Chronicles book works fine. However, 1E also attempted to present them as player characters in a way other gamelines haven't necessarily done. If that's going to be retained in 2E (and I'd like it to be, since it makes for some decent leveling options in a number of Mummy chronicle structures in a world with few active Arisen), I think it needs to be expanded upon, perhaps in a way similar to what some of the sub-splats have seen in the other 2E revisions. I'm thinking here of the P:tC alchemists, M:tA sleepwalkers, and W:tF wolf-blooded. I wonder if you could write a cult book that also hit on supernatural sub-splats like ghosts, revenants, and Sadikh. Would you include the Fasad and Amkhata in such a book?<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, the pack generation material in Werewolf would be handy if adapted for populating a Cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T17:45:28-07:00","id":1131529,"title":"","content":"I'd love more material on ghosts, revenants, Sadikh and Fasad, Witnesses, and Sekhem sorcerers. Again I'm thinking of Night Horrors but exploring them as peripheral characters like Half-damned would be interesting, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T18:11:57-07:00","id":1131537,"title":"","content":"I think that a short, Heirs to Hell-style book on playing ghosts, Sadikh, Fasad, and Sekhem sorcerers would be perfect! And, I think playable ghosts are on the hit list for Geist 2e, so those rules should be usable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T21:10:09-07:00","id":1131600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1131537#post1131537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-ico