equivalent of those supporting roles are Sadikhs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Sleepwalker (and supporting Merits) would be a good equivalent, if not Wolf-blooded, for Witnesses.<br /> <br /> Give them a little edge and distinction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T05:22:54-07:00","id":1132973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1132961#post1132961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obsession with the Arisen is more of a hindrance though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you could look at it as a built-in potential motivator for plot hooks. Mages have a mechanical trait similar and it's literally called 'Obsession' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-23T07:13:35-07:00","id":1133006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1132961#post1132961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The obsession with the Arisen is more of a hindrance though.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a fight? Not as much as Sybaris, that's for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T09:22:23-07:00","id":1135177,"title":"","content":"This makes me happy, I wanted to play Mummy but I didn't want to play in 1st Ed rules anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T11:24:50-07:00","id":1139976,"title":"","content":"My personal hope is they drop the mechanics that alter the target number for the dice rolls. I always hated that in the original world of darkness. I wasn't pleased to see that make a return in 1ed Mummy, which is as far as I know the only Chronicles of Darkness game that used that mechanic. Hope they don't used it in 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5392-aikidragon","name":"Aikidragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T12:01:12-07:00","id":1139982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aikidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1139976#post1139976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal hope is they drop the mechanics that alter the target number for the dice rolls. I always hated that in the original world of darkness. I wasn't pleased to see that make a return in 1ed Mummy, which is as far as I know the only Chronicles of Darkness game that used that mechanic. Hope they don't used it in 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a hunch they won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T12:46:07-07:00","id":1139989,"title":"","content":"The term target numbers now refers to the number of successes needed to succeed at extended actions, and at least one dev has admitted that the rules for Mummy weren't that good. Unless you know something I don't I wouldn't count on shifting target numbers to remain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T13:57:07-07:00","id":1140004,"title":"","content":"It was a fine mechanic but there are likely better ways to depict fate jiggering mechanically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T14:56:37-07:00","id":1140014,"title":"","content":"I think even the team on Mummy had mixed feelings about it, but the author of it wanted to convey how mummies are so powerful and cosmic that they could, well, lower target numbers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T15:02:48-07:00","id":1140016,"title":"","content":"Shifting target numbers is the main reason my group never even tried to play Mummy so I'd be very happy if they get rid of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T16:08:15-07:00","id":1140031,"title":"","content":"It was more of an issue in WoD because WoD naturally had shifting target numbers as a base unlike Chronicles. My biggest issue with the mechanic is that it's incredibly boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T18:10:30-07:00","id":1140053,"title":"","content":"Huh. People had a problem with Target Numbers changing? That surprises me. It wasn't like World of Darkness, where it was a core part of the mechanics. It was an &quot;only if you had a magic ability&quot; sort of deal. The issue with the World of Darkness variant was that it meant there were two different metrics of task difficulty on basic rolls, which was redundant.<br /> <br /> And Tier 1 of Blessed is the God King was a favourite at my table. As a way of showing Fate in action, looking at a dice roll and being able to say, &quot;Well, no successes, but I trigger my ability to retroactively succeed on 6s and now I have four&quot; always <i>felt</i> fantastic to my players. Always accompanied by some narrative description of Fate swinging into action.<br /> <br /> But whatever. It's a mechanic. I always felt Mummy had the best mechanics of any Chronicles of Darkness game I ever played, better than the hot mess that was Demon and a lot less finicky than Changeling for example. I hope that it stays that way going into second edition. But this specific mechanic isn't a hill I'm going to die on. It always felt like it did its job of representing Fate well, but so long as they can find a new way of representing that I have no particular problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T13:38:11-07:00","id":1140299,"title":"","content":"I liked tge mechanic as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T07:23:31-07:00","id":1140510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1140053#post1140053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this specific mechanic isn't a hill I'm going to die on. It always felt like it did its job of representing Fate well, but so long as they can find a new way of representing that I have no particular problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I feel as well. Honestly, though, the CofD rules aren't some of my favorite game mechanics. I think the mechanics and powers are <i>just right</i> for the type of stories they tell, so that's good, but my own personal enjoyments exist at the ends of the spectrum: most games I run are lighter on the crunch, but then I like GURPS as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-27T19:24:59-07:00","id":1222567,"title":"","content":"Necro-ing this since it asked what I wished to see in the 2ed. Which is.<br /> <br /> 1. Refocus the guilds. It's not that I have a problem with them, just with how it is potrayed. In 1e it felt that the guilds(mostly Maa-kep especially in Guildhalls) were still a thing in modern day but that doesn't make sense given how mummies work. Like mummies having a status for the guild and that they could switch if they want. I don't know for splat that is so spread out and rare that's just feel like it's to much structure. I would like to see Guilds more as forgotten relics of an Arisen's past that he uses to interact and experience the world around them, which fits with mummies theme of reclaiming Memory and defining who you are from that. Originally Guilds would have been factions like Covenants and Orders during Irem, but now that the City of Pillars are gone they should be more like Agendas that is philosophies Arisen hold on to as a pillar of identity and support for those who fight to keep what memories they have. Whether it will be like that I don't know. We will have to see.<br /> <br /> 2. Really interested to see how Memory would work with Morality out of the picture. I'm really excited on that front.<br /> <br /> 3. I want to see the Restless Stars as a playable option like how Seers were in Mage, that be really fun. As much as I would love that I have to admit that it is unlikely given that for them to that they all so have to included the Temahk's also. So I wonder if that would be to complicated from the get go.<br /> <br /> 4. More focus on the Apotheosis. Also more variations on options. Because what the Apotheosis is you gaining memories, defining who you are and coming up with your own answer yeah? If so that means that not necessarily mean an Arisen would just choose to rebel against the Judges and Irem because of it, because those are important charastics for an Arisen and for one like the Maa-Kep whose whole point of existence is loyalty and reverence for the Judges, abandoning them is like saying everything he's ever done is meaningless. What I want Apotheosis to do is provide a choice, a choice in allowing the Arisen to do anything that he wishes to do, freedom but not freedom in going against Dust but freedom to decide what they want, no matter what it is. I just want them to focus on that part.<br /> <br /> 5. Also give more insight on Decrees. That be fun.<br /> <br /> Well those are my thoughts on it anyhow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T03:39:03-07:00","id":1222600,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd like to see the Guilds have structure, but have cultists form the lower rungs of that society with the Arisen serving as the leadership. No Mummy should have to bear the rank of 'Apprentice'.<br /> In fact, I'd like to see more light shined on cultists as a whole. I'd like to see them play a larger role in the 'Irem-in-Exile' that is Arisen culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T06:25:18-07:00","id":1222633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1222600#post1222600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd like to see the Guilds have structure, but have cultists form the lower rungs of that society with the Arisen serving as the leadership. No Mummy should have to bear the rank of 'Apprentice'.<br /> In fact, I'd like to see more light shined on cultists as a whole. I'd like to see them play a larger role in the 'Irem-in-Exile' that is Arisen culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's more preferable, especially since because they are mortal I honestly don't see why the Arisen don't teach them how to make relics or at least just the basics. That seems like a more reliable way to farm Sekhem plus also deepening the bonds between Cult and Arisen, with the Arisen taking a more master and teacher role, instead of just guardian when stuff gets bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-28T19:59:31-07:00","id":1222794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1222567#post1222567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necro-ing this since it asked what I wished to see in the 2ed. Which is.<br /> <br /> 1. Refocus the guilds. It's not that I have a problem with them, just with how it is potrayed. In 1e it felt that the guilds(mostly Maa-kep especially in Guildhalls) were still a thing in modern day but that doesn't make sense given how mummies work. Like mummies having a status for the guild and that they could switch if they want. I don't know for splat that is so spread out and rare that's just feel like it's to much structure. I would like to see Guilds more as forgotten relics of an Arisen's past that he uses to interact and experience the world around them, which fits with mummies theme of reclaiming Memory and defining who you are from that. Originally Guilds would have been factions like Covenants and Orders during Irem, but now that the City of Pillars are gone they should be more like Agendas that is philosophies Arisen hold on to as a pillar of identity and support for those who fight to keep what memories they have. Whether it will be like that I don't know. We will have to see.<br /> <br /> 2. Really interested to see how Memory would work with Morality out of the picture. I'm really excited on that front.<br /> <br /> 3. I want to see the Restless Stars as a playable option like how Seers were in Mage, that be really fun. As much as I would love that I have to admit that it is unlikely given that for them to that they all so have to included the Temahk's also. So I wonder if that would be to complicated from the get go.<br /> <br /> 4. More focus on the Apotheosis. Also more variations on options. Because what the Apotheosis is you gaining memories, defining who you are and coming up with your own answer yeah? If so that means that not necessarily mean an Arisen would just choose to rebel against the Judges and Irem because of it, because those are important charastics for an Arisen and for one like the Maa-Kep whose whole point of existence is loyalty and reverence for the Judges, abandoning them is like saying everything he's ever done is meaningless. What I want Apotheosis to do is provide a choice, a choice in allowing the Arisen to do anything that he wishes to do, freedom but not freedom in going against Dust but freedom to decide what they want, no matter what it is. I just want them to focus on that part.<br /> <br /> 5. Also give more insight on Decrees. That be fun.<br /> <br /> Well those are my thoughts on it anyhow.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean...Deceived ARE playable. But that, I definitely feel like Guilds need some res-structuring.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T03:12:39-07:00","id":1222854,"title":"","content":"I know that you can play as them, I just want that to be an option straight out in the 2e core","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T05:53:50-07:00","id":1222869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1222854#post1222854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that you can play as them, I just want that to be an option straight out in the 2e core</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be nice, but the mechanics may been to be simplified to make that work (for space reasons).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T06:19:01-07:00","id":1222879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1222869#post1222869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would be nice, but the mechanics may been to be simplified to make that work (for space reasons).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah that's my concern","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T07:19:44-07:00","id":1222889,"title":"","content":"Just like WtF 2e doesn't present the option to play Pure I'd guess that MtC won't have the option to play the Deceived in the core. It's better to do a proper text in another book than having to simplify it to fit in the core if it's not actually part of the core experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T12:14:52-07:00","id":1222963,"title":"","content":"I would like to see something similar to what was done in Vampire and Werewolf. In both was brought a little-worked enemy in supplements as something important the configuration that return to the world, in the case of Mummies, could be a rebirth of the inhuman races before civilization , beings who represent the enemies of the judges of any mummy.<br /> <br /> That would even bring all sorts of mummies to the basic book, since they though they continued to hate each other, would have a common enemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T15:24:49-07:00","id":1223035,"title":"","content":"Mummy has a lot of events shaking its world already.<br /> <br /> Firstly, mummies themselves are constantly the creatures returning to the world, which ties into the second point of how we're in the midst of a Sothic Turn right now. An event like that not only awakens the Deceived and Shuankhsen, but also perhaps new villains: demons who are cursed to slumber except for during a Turn. Finally, the spreading sermons of the Heretic and Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-29T16:02:18-07:00","id":1223051,"title":"","content":"But it would give a new flavor to the second edition. And it is something that exists in your configuration, just does not have due prominence. That would make this moment something unique, that the mummies are not used to, is something that takes forward the already initiated chronicles of the players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T03:01:50-07:00","id":1223144,"title":"","content":"It's what many other 2e core books has done. Does anyone know if MtC 2e will have a Chronicle title associated with it? In the cases of Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling and Hunter the Chronicle title has revealed which antagonist will have extra focus in the core instead of being relegated to other source books like the Night Horrors series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T03:23:35-07:00","id":1223147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1223144#post1223144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's what many other 2e core books has done. Does anyone know if MtC 2e will have a Chronicle title associated with it? In the cases of Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling and Hunter the Chronicle title has revealed which antagonist will have extra focus in the core instead of being relegated to other source books like the Night Horrors series.</div> </div> </div> </div>The adventures that came with the books were called &quot;the Avarice Chronicles&quot; after the Dreams of Avarice. We could end up with something like that. Or akin to Mage and it's 'subtitle' (the Fallen World), it could be tied to the constant ongoing effect that afflicts these immortal beings. The Descent may be taken, but notion certainly carries weight here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T05:40:22-07:00","id":1223178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1222963#post1222963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see something similar to what was done in Vampire and Werewolf. In both was brought a little-worked enemy in supplements as something important the configuration that return to the world, in the case of Mummies, could be a rebirth of the inhuman races before civilization , beings who represent the enemies of the judges of any mummy.<br /> <br /> That would even bring all sorts of mummies to the basic book, since they though they continued to hate each other, would have a common enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The rebirth of the pre-human species feels like it's really just retreading much the same space as the Idigam Chronicles. Alien beings from prehistory with a Lovecraftian bent suddenly return to the world after a long absence?<br /> <br /> Also not sure why it would necessarily unify all the different strands of Mummies? The Deceived have a Movement founded on prehuman influences and accursed mutations in the Rotting Temple, and I don't see Shuankhsen being phased by the manifestation of earlier horrors in the slightest.<br /> <br /> For the Arisen, I think the obvious shake-up would be to simply update the setting. The original Mummy was &quot;set&quot; in 2012, the first Sothic Turn after the Heretic had achieved Apotheosis. Fast forward even a handful of years and it's clear that a pretty seismic shift is happening in Arisen society. Rio touched on this change, with one of the Arisen in the city being a hidden Mummy who had successfully achieved her Apotheosis. The entire point of the Sothic Turn was to spread Dreams of Avarice in a situation where Arisen had the time and inclination to pursue alternatives to their current state of existence. We're in a situation where most Arisen who have woken for the Sothic Turn will still be awake barring unfortunate happenstance, but at the low ebb of their power. The Guilds need to react to the enormous shock of Apotheosis going from rumour to reality, and some Arisen may be so bold that they pursue it without secrecy. The invisible, undetectable presence of those Arisen who have achieved Apotheosis will be felt in places as they influence comrades who no longer remember their old existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-30T08:01:02-07:00","id":1223252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1222889#post1222889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's better to do a proper text in another book than having to simplify it to fit in the core if it's not actually part of the core experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Though I wouldn't mind seba in the core book - and a Seba Chronicle, with the Sothic Turn provoking a spike in their number - falling into both mummy and human hands, spreading both new concepts and memories of Irem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-01T03:28:21-07:00","id":1223868,"title":"","content":"I hope the 2nd eition will be a more cooperative game. Right now I feel it's really hard for a group of mummies to find a reason to work as together unless they share the same cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-07T06:06:20-07:00","id":1225555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1223868#post1223868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope the 2nd eition will be a more cooperative game. Right now I feel it's really hard for a group of mummies to find a reason to work as together unless they share the same cult.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another reason for including a chapter/supplement for cultists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T00:52:00-07:00","id":1226390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1225555#post1225555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's another reason for including a chapter/supplement for cultists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cultists with guns, relics, and briefcases full of cash, Witnesses with more of their abilities explored, Sekhem sorcerers... Mummy has a thriving non-Arisen ecosystem of player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T01:06:02-07:00","id":1226392,"title":"","content":"Atamajakki has a good point about the number of player options that are theoretically possible in Mummy without even including the Arisen.<br /> <br /> As a wild idea Mummy 2E might want to adopt the Tier's of play system Hunters used for a while now. <br /> <br /> Tier 1:<br /> Cultists (Basically normal Blue Book humans with access to some unique resources) <br /> Witnesses (Since I don't see them getting that much more powerful in 2E just more fleshed out)<br /> <br /> Tier 2:<br /> Sadikh (These guys, for me are the obvious mini-splat akin to Ghouls, they just need a bit of reworking) <br /> Ghost Cultists (One again, basically made with Blue Book rules but with some unique merits or numina)<br /> <br /> Tier 3:<br /> Arisen <br /> Deceived <br /> <br /> I'm dicey about including Sekhem Sorcerers as a player option. Mainly because most of the 1E fluff about them was focused on them being considered upstart pretenders to the Shan'Iatu's power who kinda mangled Sekhem everytime they managed to pull off any magic. I think they might be better off in an antagonist role aking to Alchemists in Promethean 2E. <br /> <br /> Of course, while this approach would put renewed focus on Cults, who we pretty much all agree need a lot more love in the new addition, it still does not exactly solve the problem of getting a group of Arisen to work togeather aside from Guild affiliations or sharing a Cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-11T05:21:18-07:00","id":1226433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1226392#post1226392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tier 1:<br /> Cultists (Basically normal Blue Book humans with access to some unique resources) <br /> Witnesses (Since I don't see them getting that much more powerful in 2E just more fleshed out)</div> </div> </div> </div>For Witnesses, I could see them being enhanced like Stigmatics (bonus Supernatural merit), Wolf-Blooded (Curse with a linked Boon), or Sleepwalkers (Witness being a Gateway merit/state for other Merits).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T08:52:21-07:00","id":1227446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1226392#post1226392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a wild idea Mummy 2E might want to adopt the Tier's of play system Hunters used for a while now.<br /> <br /> Tier 1:<br /> Cultists (Basically normal Blue Book humans with access to some unique resources)<br /> Witnesses (Since I don't see them getting that much more powerful in 2E just more fleshed out)<br /> <br /> Tier 2:<br /> Sadikh (These guys, for me are the obvious mini-splat akin to Ghouls, they just need a bit of reworking)<br /> Ghost Cultists (One again, basically made with Blue Book rules but with some unique merits or numina)<br /> <br /> Tier 3:<br /> Arisen<br /> Deceived<br /> <br /> I'm dicey about including Sekhem Sorcerers as a player option. Mainly because most of the 1E fluff about them was focused on them being considered upstart pretenders to the Shan'Iatu's power who kinda mangled Sekhem everytime they managed to pull off any magic. I think they might be better off in an antagonist role aking to Alchemists in Promethean 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I'm in agreement with those who think the Deceived would be better off in a supplement where they can get maximum room. But you could quite easily fill all three tiers with groups who would antagonists to the Arisen, but viable player characters.<br /> <br /> For example, in the core book, you could have:<br /> <br /> Tier 1: Cultists, Witnesses<br /> <br /> Tier 2: Sadikh, Ghost Cultists (or Revenant Cultists)<br /> <br /> Tier 3: Arisen<br /> <br /> <br /> And in supplements, you could have:<br /> <br /> Tier 1: Tomb Raiders (in this context, I mean humans with interest in and talents regarding relics)<br /> <br /> Tier 2: Sekhem-users (sorcerers, the scientists alluded to in the core book, mystics who enhance or enlighten themselves via their pillars)<br /> <br /> Tier 3: Deceived<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-14T10:32:05-07:00","id":1227466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1227446#post1227446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue