ath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:23:58-07:00","id":1241338,"title":"","content":"For easy access:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mummy the Curse Second Edition, Onyx Path Publishing Brorchure</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mummy: The Curse 2nd Edition</b> expands the popular concepts of tragic Memory, devastating Utterances, pernicious cults, and fractured guilds. It introduces new aspects to the game, including horrifying rituals, expanding your troupe play to include sorcerers and non-Arisen immortals and finally allowing players to experience and interact with the nightmarish journey through Duat. This edition extends <b>Mummy</b>\u2019s reach around the globe, providing justification and story hooks for starting your chronicles as far from the Nameless Empire as a meret of mummies could wish to go. <b>Mummy</b> tightens its grasp on godlike terror, as the presence of the deific Judges becomes more pervasive and insidious than before. This new chronicle of immortals not only begs the question, \u201cWhat does it mean to be Deathless?\u201d but also \u201cWhat does it mean to be Timeless?\u201d <b>Coming Soon!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:36:32-07:00","id":1241344,"title":"","content":"All super hype, the expansion on the meret is a pretty good thing all things considering, it feels wierd that all mummies would organize as such given how active they are. Very curious on none Arisen Immortals, will this be a chance to talk about mummies from other cultures? Will this go into depth on vampire/mummy interaction? Will this update the Immortals book to 2e? Can\u2019t wait to see.<br /> <br /> Also journeys into duat, that be fun. I\u2019m curious tho how this will relate to Memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:42:37-07:00","id":1241347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241338#post1241338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For easy access:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'm on my iPad, so I couldn't copy it directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:44:12-07:00","id":1241348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241344#post1241344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All super hype, the expansion on the meret is a pretty good thing all things considering, it feels wierd that all mummies would organize as such given how active they are. Very curious on none Arisen Immortals, will this be a chance to talk about mummies from other cultures? Will this go into depth on vampire/mummy interaction? Will this update the Immortals book to 2e? Can\u2019t wait to see.<br /> <br /> Also journeys into duat, that be fun. I\u2019m curious tho how this will relate to Memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re non Arisen immortals. Definitely guessing it's an expansion of inclusion of bluebook style immortals. Getting Sekhem sorcery style stuff in the corebook is going to be gooooooooooooood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:44:35-07:00","id":1241349,"title":"","content":"As always, I am not only skeptical but actively repulsed by the idea of non-Nameless Empire mummies-but if the idea is to basically expand the breadth of the Empire to allow for the Arisen/Decieved/Shuankhsen to have a wider starting range, I could get behind it.<br /> <br /> Clarity: Other kinds of immortals, on the other hand, are open game, and I look forward to expanding the roster of immortal bastards in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:53:21-07:00","id":1241352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241349#post1241349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As always, I am not only skeptical but actively repulsed by the idea of non-Nameless Empire mummies-but if the idea is to basically expand the breadth of the Empire to allow for the Arisen/Decieved/Shuankhsen to have a wider starting range, I could get behind it.<br /> <br /> Clarity: Other kinds of immortals, on the other hand, are open game, and I look forward to expanding the roster of immortal bastards in general.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I my feelings are pretty much the opposite. I am very much a card-carrying member of the &quot;Mummy should be about more than Irem&quot; club, but I do think Mummy should still be fundamentally about Mummies. If it turns what we get is a &quot;this how to apply the Mummy Framework to things besides proto-egyptians&quot; that'll satisfy my desires in practice, if not in spirit. On the other hand, I don't think a character with a handful of longevity themed supernatural merits will be nearly as compelling an experience around Ancient God-Monsters as it might sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T09:56:06-07:00","id":1241354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241352#post1241352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I my feelings are pretty much the opposite. I am very much a card-carrying member of the &quot;Mummy should be about more than Irem&quot; club, but I do think Mummy should still be fundamentally about Mummies. If it turns what we get is a &quot;this how to apply the Mummy Framework to things besides proto-egyptians&quot; that'll satisfy my desires in practice, if not in spirit. On the other hand, I don't think a character with a handful of longevity themed supernatural merits will be nearly as compelling an experience around Ancient God-Monsters as it might sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do you, but blegh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:13:52-07:00","id":1241395,"title":"","content":"The blurb for 2e has me all sorts of hyped. I\u2019m really looking forward to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:15:35-07:00","id":1241396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241349#post1241349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As always, I am not only skeptical but actively repulsed by the idea of non-Nameless Empire mummies</div> </div> </div> </div>? Why's that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:19:28-07:00","id":1241397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241396#post1241396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ? Why's that?</div> </div> </div> </div>To borrow from Malcolm to express the root of my problem:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/32279-how-to-get-around-the-racial-restrictions?p=39949#post39949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Mummy&quot; is not a generic archetypal monster even if the same term is used in English for a variety of preserved bodies. Having Incan mummies is a thematically incoherent addition to the game for the sake of a linguistic quirk. Mummy: The Curse is not about how it's weird that English uses a word derived from a slang term for Egyptian preserved corpses for all preserved corpses.</div> </div> </div> </div>EDIT: Expanding a bit in my prep time:<br /> <br /> 1) Mummies as a pop-cultural monster icon do not stem from us having the same reaction to preserved bodies from all over the world, it emerged from the specific Egyptomania of the late 1800s and early 1900s, and it is that specific expression that has power and meaning as a result. THe other are just...well, preserved bodies. THis is not so much a reason as it is stage setting for some of the later points, namely:<br /> <br /> 2) I am not interested in a concept of preserved bodies being immortal people of vast magical power from around the world- hell I'm not interested in direct Egyptian concepts of that concept-but I am invested in the mythos of Nameless Empire and the cosmology of Curse, with an irrepeatable capstone in the form of the Rite of Return and playing out the relics of all of that searching for a place outside of it. To have equivalents outside of that concept cheapens and weakens it for me, and I don't care for that.<br /> <br /> 3) Also, while not always prevalent in the complaint, there's been a lot of subtle racism against the idea of having to play someone of African origin that seems to come in with a lot of the complainers of this point and I am all for flipping the bird to that.<br /> <br /> 4) And finally, too much fan insistence on anything usually does a good job of killing something for me. It happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-01-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:22:49-07:00","id":1241400,"title":"","content":"Well, they did said &quot;non Arisen immortals&quot;, not &quot;non Iremite mummies&quot;. By the former definition, the Deceived, Shuankhsen, Sadikh, Fascad, Eternal, Reborn, Visitors, Blood Bathers, Body Thieves, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> But at anyway, I'll have no problem with non iremeite sekhem based immortal life forms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:24:18-07:00","id":1241401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241338#post1241338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For easy access:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm, cool. The lack of a Mummy 2nd Edition is something I feel more heavily than that of other games for several reasons and I do crave for it quite badly. This blurb also hints at changes I'll probably appreciate, especially as someone that also prefers Arisen to be a Nameless Empire exclusive (while other kind immortals are fair game) and wants to see more of Duat, the Judges and the other divine beings of the gameline.<br /> <br /> Also, I wonder where those oblique Lovecraftian references will stand in 2nd Edition, if they remain at all. They were interesting and I would lie if I said they did not make me giggle, but Duat knows if I'm aware, as a fan of those, of how quickly they can turn wrong and ruin something fresh if abused. Not sure what I want to happen with those. Might be worth discussing it as a community, just for the sake of having a dialogue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-01-2018, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T11:40:34-07:00","id":1241411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241352#post1241352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, I my feelings are pretty much the opposite. I am very much a card-carrying member of the &quot;Mummy should be about more than Irem&quot; club, but I do think Mummy should still be fundamentally about Mummies. If it turns what we get is a &quot;this how to apply the Mummy Framework to things besides proto-egyptians&quot; that'll satisfy my desires in practice, if not in spirit. On the other hand, I don't think a character with a handful of longevity themed supernatural merits will be nearly as compelling an experience around Ancient God-Monsters as it might sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I think it would undermine the themes I enjoy about Mummy to expand beyond it's proverbial borders. That said, things like attempts to recreate the Rite and the results of those,etc would be neat to see in a supplement. Expanding the cults and having the core book go into details on things like blood bathers,etc being part of the supernatural atmosphere around the Deathless is a good touch though I think. It worked well in the Dark Eras materials so anything that expands that is a plus in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-01T15:03:26-07:00","id":1241508,"title":"","content":"Would be interesting if they include the purified in this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T00:54:04-07:00","id":1241724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241397#post1241397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3) Also, while not always prevalent in the complaint, there's been a lot of subtle racism against the idea of having to play someone of African origin that seems to come in with a lot of the complainers of this point and I am all for flipping the bird to that.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and this is your one point that makes me head-tilt.<br /> <br /> In a vacuum this point would have some merit...and yet in wider context, not really. The other cultures that other people have been asking to be integrated into Mummy are not exactly white cultures. South American and Chinese culture (which if memory serves are the two regions that people want non-proto-Egyptian Mummies out of) is about as far from typical white culture you can get.<br /> <br /> And, if I'd be a bit flippant, seems odd to declare racism if they want to spotlight a different brown-skinned people...from the usual brown skinned peoples.<br /> <br /> It'd be one thing if there were alternative white-Western cultures with extensive history of having their own mummies that were widely known...yet there isn't. And it's not what people are insisting get added into the game.<br /> <br /> (but oh boy have mummies in pop fiction in general dealt with the issue of exoticism to the umpth degrees...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 08-02-2018, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T02:22:22-07:00","id":1241733,"title":"","content":"My own attitude towards non-Iremite Mummies is basically aligned with ArcaneArts on this one. It's always struck me as just a tad... aesthetically shallow, I guess. That quote from Malcolm largely hits it on the head. There is no thematic link between an Incan Mummy and an Egyptian Mummy beyond them both being preserved bodies. They were different people from different social strata preserved for different reasons in different methods. Asking for the former to appear in a game about the latter makes as much sense as also requesting a cloud of sentient ash be part of the same gameline because cremations are part of some cultures' mortuary traditions. Hell, the cloud of ash probably has the stronger claim to kinship with an Egyptian Mummy than the Incan Mummy, since at least cremations and Egyptian mummification are intentional means of dealing with the bodies of the dead instead of what you get when you leave a sacrifice behind on a mountaintop. Where exactly is the connection, beyond the word, that would lead people to expect that the existence of one Immortal undead creature from one tradition would have any bearing on the existence of another from a different culture?<br /> <br /> And at the same time, I always felt that Mummy: The Curse <i>already offered</i> mechanics for Arisen-like but not-Arisen forms of revenant, if all you really want is differently flavoured walking corpses. The expanded Ghost mechanics allowed you to have lucid, fully realised ghosts animating their own bodies and fuelled with powers like regeneration and even Pillars. If you want an Incan Mummy, there you have it. The announcement that they'll be having different kinds of Immortals floating around in second edition is something I'm more than happy with, since they do feel like natural foils for the Arisen through descent after descent.<br /> <br /> Fingers super crossed on the new edition though. The first edition is still my favourite game but I'm trying other lines out until it releases and I can run another Mummy campaign. If it proves disappointing it will be genuinely crushing. I haven't been this nervous about a game in a long time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T03:33:27-07:00","id":1241743,"title":"","content":"The origin of Arisen will still remain Irem in second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T05:49:24-07:00","id":1241779,"title":"","content":"Does development start this year yet? =O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:13:24-07:00","id":1241865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241724#post1241724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and this is your one point that makes me head-tilt.<br /> <br /> In a vacuum this point would have some merit...and yet in wider context, not really. The other cultures that other people have been asking to be integrated into Mummy are not exactly white cultures. South American and Chinese culture (which if memory serves are the two regions that people want non-proto-Egyptian Mummies out of) is about as far from typical white culture you can get.<br /> <br /> And, if I'd be a bit flippant, seems odd to declare racism if they want to spotlight a different brown-skinned people...from the usual brown skinned peoples.<br /> <br /> It'd be one thing if there were alternative white-Western cultures with extensive history of having their own mummies that were widely known...yet there isn't. And it's not what people are insisting get added into the game.<br /> <br /> (but oh boy have mummies in pop fiction in general dealt with the issue of exoticism to the umpth degrees...)</div> </div> </div> </div>THere's a reason why I put an emphasis on African, because it's not just a racial component.(Price of explaining things in less then ten minutes while also setting up work tools.)<br /> <br /> And mind you, a lot of people who make the complaint don't have that problem, either racially or regionally-but there's been enough of them that I will gladly still flip them the bird on the subject.<br /> <br /> Anyways, we should try and reverse the derail(my bad folks) and focus on cool stuff like OH MY GOD, WE CAN ACTUALLY PLAY AROUND IN DUAT, WHAT TERRIBLE THINGS WILL THAT RESULT IN.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:26:37-07:00","id":1241876,"title":"","content":"I for one, want to see what a more prevalent Judge presence looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:29:49-07:00","id":1241877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241876#post1241876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one, want to see what a more prevalent Judge presence looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm hoping that this means when Mummy 2e gets kickstartered, the Book of Going Westward will return as a stretch goal. <br /> <br /> Also, full colour images of all the Judges would be rad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:36:35-07:00","id":1241881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241877#post1241877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, full colour images of all the Judges would be rad.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are 42 of them, so that seems pretty resource intensive. I just think they're kind of weirdly ignorable in 1st ed considering they're your X-axis and a defining part of one's personal Rite of Return experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:42:56-07:00","id":1241887,"title":"","content":"Think it will follow 1e\u2019s declining power over time. Or will mummy\u2019s increase in stength over the course of play like the other splats regularly do? I\u2019m referring to their power stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:54:51-07:00","id":1241889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241887#post1241887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think it will follow 1e\u2019s declining power over time. Or will mummy\u2019s increase in stength over the course of play like the other splats regularly do? I\u2019m referring to their power stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without a doubt, the former.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T09:59:01-07:00","id":1241890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrOwl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241887#post1241887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think it will follow 1e\u2019s declining power over time. Or will mummy\u2019s increase in stength over the course of play like the other splats regularly do? I\u2019m referring to their power stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no doubt that they\u2019ll still decline. The Descent is such a huge part of Mummy that getting rid of it would be like having a whole new game rather than a new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T10:22:31-07:00","id":1241903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241890#post1241890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no doubt that they\u2019ll still decline. The Descent is such a huge part of Mummy that getting rid of it would be like having a whole new game rather than a new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that so? Hmm okay. I only ever read the core and that was back when it first came out. So my knowledge on the mummy subject is super scarce.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24316-mrowl","name":"MrOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T16:17:24-07:00","id":1242119,"title":"","content":"I just hope they don't break the parts of the game and setting that aren't broken. We still need the Descent, starting at low Memory, mummies being from Irem (gasp!), and cults. Everything they're adding sounds really great, though, but there's one part I don't like. I think Duat should remain off-limits, but to be fair at Memory 10 you are supposed to be able to remember it (or is it upon Apotheosis? still.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T16:53:54-07:00","id":1242129,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it'll be interesting to see if they preserve the great wall between GM and player content. They could certainly move some things around at the very least (I never quite understood why Relics, potentially starting equipment, were gated off beyond the Pale Brood's misleadingly spoilery description text).<br /> <br /> The core's biggest flaw to me was always the lack of end game content. I.e. unclear Apotheosis mechanics, little to no information on what remembering Duat might mean, etc. You can make that stuff up, sure, but I could never really think of an interesting &quot;grand truth&quot; to reveal if my campaigns ever got to that point. Part of that is me. I struggle to find the grand, cosmology-level lore to be terribly interesting. And I understand the intrinsic irony in both expressing that disinterest while calling its absence the game's &quot;biggest flaw&quot;. For me, revelations about who the characters have been and details about their past lives are more human and a thousand times more interesting than The True Identity Of The Judges or anything like that, but I'm not so dismissive as to assume that a revelation on that level would have no impact or be inherently boring in any way. I just don't think I'm the person to try and write something like that.<br /> <br /> The easiest thing to do, from my perspective, would be to ditch the wall and have all the information about the game's setting be up front to the characters. Memory just becomes something entirely personal. But if they were to keep the wall then it would need a marked improvement over the first edition. It felt genuinely frustrating as a GM to get no clear answers from the game billing itself as the only Chronicles game to have a clear Truth. The core book in particular was somewhat notorious for keeping things ambiguous and with little more than clever innuendo and hints even in the &quot;behind the wall&quot; section. Never really bothered me, I wasn't inclined to be running chronicles delving into that stuff in the first place, but the discrepancy between what the book seemed to sell itself as and what was actually there stood out even to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T16:55:19-07:00","id":1242131,"title":"","content":"I'm glad to hear that the Judges are becoming more important; they always did fascinate me. And Duat? I'm overjoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:07:19-07:00","id":1242167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242119#post1242119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just hope they don't break the parts of the game and setting that aren't broken. We still need the Descent, starting at low Memory, mummies being from Irem (gasp!), and cults. Everything they're adding sounds really great, though, but there's one part I don't like. I think Duat should remain off-limits, but to be fair at Memory 10 you are supposed to be able to remember it (or is it upon Apotheosis? still.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to debate what constitutes as &quot;not broken.&quot; I do think that the bouncing power level is integral part of the mummy experience, but the actual Descent rules in 1st ed are pretty wonky. The starting a low memory thing is also kind of weird and arbitrary since there's no particular in-character reason that all mummies have to have uniformly low starting memory unless you're still in the scene where they're all waking up. In addition, the starting value is far less meaningful in of itself now that morality traits are now longer uniform. (Prometheans start at 1, Changeling is a derived trait, Beast starting value varies, Werewolves want to be at five.)<br /> <br /> Morality traits have been pretty significantly reimagined in every 2nd ed thusfar. Beyond the broad strokes concept 2e memory shouldn't be beholden to anything from 1e memory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242129#post1242129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it'll be interesting to see if they preserve the great wall between GM and player content. They could certainly move some things around at the very least (I never quite understood why Relics, potentially starting equipment, were gated off beyond the Pale Brood's misleadingly spoilery description text).<br /> <br /> The core's biggest flaw to me was always the lack of end game content. .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the perceived need for &quot;End-game content&quot; is a problem in of itself. Concepts like Galconda and Ascension do provide possible endgame plot devices, but Vampire and Mage certainly aren't written with the assumption that they should be the conclusion of every campaign. Mummies need to be able to have meaningful character arcs without template-transforming plot devices or the ST breaking out Dreams of Avarice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:24:11-07:00","id":1242172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242167#post1242167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the perceived need for &quot;End-game content&quot; is a problem in of itself. Concepts like Galconda and Ascension do provide possible endgame plot devices, but Vampire and Mage certainly aren't written with the assumption that they should be the conclusion of every campaign. Mummies need to be able to have meaningful character arcs without template-transforming plot devices or the ST breaking out Dreams of Avarice.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I have run multiple Mummy campaigns, including one pretty lengthy one, without ever touching Apotheosis. Only one player out of the seven or eight I had across those games even ever expressed an interest in Apotheosis, and they never came close to achieving it. As I said in my original post, that's the part of the game I found the least interesting and basically left untouched. I don't think anything you've said is wrong. I also believe Mummy is already that game.<br /> <br /> 2) Unlike Galconda, Apotheosis is written in a way that suggests it is a concrete and very much integral part of modern descents. Later supplements show it becoming more and more widespread as the years march on, with the Heretic no longer the only canonical Arisen to achieve it. It's presented in a pretty similar manner to the New Dawn, except with a cultural aversion to it instead of an inbuilt need to achieve it. It's just that the book gives you no real ideas on what to tell a player who achieves it (in terms of what they now remember about Duat), and no concrete mechanics for their most important new power (relic creation). Like the New Dawn, you by no means need to have it occur in any Chronicle. Like the New Dawn, there's the definite suggestion though that a not-insignificant number of Chronicles <i>might</i> end in it, or at least have it as their driving force.<br /> <br /> This gap, to me, represented what felt like the first edition's biggest flaw. It isn't, however, a big flaw. This is my favourite game, I have to work hard to find things I dislike...<br /> <br /> Edit: Just to clarify a little further, Mummy is the <i>only</i> Chronicles game to build itself around a player-GM divide. It calls this out itself in the core. It makes a really freaking big deal about it. But... there's practically nothing behind the core's GM &quot;wall&quot; that feels worth the fuss. Not every game needs something massive for the end game but Mummy very explicitly sold itself as having something. And I don't think it pulled it off well. That's why my original post was speculating on whether they'd toss out that particular concept, or redo it with a little more oomph.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 08-02-2018, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:37:32-07:00","id":1242181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241876#post1241876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one, want to see what a more prevalent Judge presence looks like.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was probably my favourite part of the teaser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:39:52-07:00","id":1242185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242172#post1242172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) I have run multiple Mummy campaigns, including one pretty lengthy one, without ever touching Apotheosis. Only one player out of the seven or eight I had across those games even ever expressed an interest in Apotheosis, and they never came close to achieving it. As I said in my original post, that's the part of the game I found the least interesting and basically left untouched. I don't think anything you've said is wrong. I also believe Mummy is already that game.<br /> <br /> 2) Unlike Galconda, Apotheosis is written in a way that suggests it is a concrete and very much integral part of modern descents. Later supplements show it becoming more and more widespread as the years march on, with the Heretic no longer the only canonical Arisen to achieve it. It's presented in a pretty similar manner to the New Dawn, except with a cultural aversion to it instead of an inbuilt need to achieve it. It's just that the book gives you no real ideas on what to tell a player who achieves it (in terms of what they now remember about Duat), and no concrete mechanics for their most important new power (relic creation). Like the New Dawn, you by no means need to have it occur in any Chronicle. Like the New Dawn, there's the definite suggestion though that a not-insignificant number of Chronicles <i>might</i> end in it, or at least have it as their driving force.<br /> <br /> This gap, to me, represented what felt like the first edition's biggest flaw. It isn't, however, a big flaw. This is my favourite game, I have to work hard to find things I dislike...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm going to hard disagree on point #2, at least in terms of the game in its current state. Especially since you can't define a game's status quo by what happens in later supplements. Now if 2e wants to lean hard on &quot;Mummy is about the Journey to Apotheosis&quot;, that's a valid, if not necessarily preferable, approach. But at that point a lot more of the game's systems need to be purposed towards facilitating the journey. Promethean has pages and pages outlining the process the new Dawn and how it applies to each character. Mummy has about three page that directly discuss Apotheosis tucked away in the ST section.<br /> <br /> Its less an issue of &quot;Can I run the game this way&quot; and more &quot;Where is the game's focus.&quot; (Which is essentially where my issue with Nameless Empire stuff comes from.) The most important thing should be what the player's are doing &quot;now&quot; (whenever now is), and that's where the world-building should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:53:21-07:00","id":1242196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242185#post1242185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to hard disagree on point #2, at least in terms of the game in its current state. Especially since you can't define a game's status quo by what happens in later supplements. Now if 2e wants to lean hard on &quot;Mummy is about the Journey to Apotheosis&quot;, that's a valid, if not necessarily preferable, approach. But at that point a lot more of the game's systems need to be purposed towards facilitating the journey. Promethean has pages and pages outlining the process the new Dawn and how it applies to each character. Mummy has about three page that directly discuss Apotheosis tucked away in the ST section.<br /> <br /> Its less an issue of &quot;Can I run the game this way&quot; and more &quot;Where is the game's focus.&quot; (Which is essentially where my issue with Nameless Empire stuff comes from.) The most important thing should be what the player's are doing &quot;now&quot; (whenever now is), and that's where the world-building should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I probably shouldn't have tucked this away in an edit to the previous post, since you were clearly replying when I did so, but when I said &quot;end game content&quot; I wasn't just talking about Apotheosis. I was talking about every single thing behind the GM wall. Indeed, the very <i>concept</i> of the GM wall. This is the only game in the entire line to go with that sort of concept, it made it a fundamental point of its entire structure. Mummy has secrets and when you play it you, the player, should find them out. But Book of the Deceived (an entirely GM book) was the only supplement to actually give concrete information for the players to discover.<br /> <br /> And as you say, we shouldn't define the status quo by later supplements, which makes it worse that the GM content in the core is barely more detailed than the player content. We get some vague allusions to who the Shan'iatu were and what they were trying to do, but were told by the developers that the obvious conclusions (that the Shan'iatu became the Judges) were wrong and didn't have much more to go on for a very long time. This ties into Apotheosis because one thing you're meant to discover as part of that journey is the true story of Duat, but the books hold nary a tidbit to give a GM an idea of where to start for that.<br /> <br /> I happily ran a weekly game for eighteen months without any of the above posing a problem, which is why half of my original post was talking about how I think they might as well just ditch the concept. But if they are going to persist with the divide, I think they really need to knuckle down and give solid mechanics and ideas for Apotheosis and something tangible you can give to players when they achieve it in terms of what they now remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T18:59:47-07:00","id":1242201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242196#post1242196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I happily ran a weekly game for eighteen months without any of the above posing a problem, which is why half of my original post was talking about how I think they might as well just ditch the concept. But if they are going to persist with the divide, I think they really need to knuckle down and give solid mechanics and ideas for Apotheosis and something tangible you can give to players when they achieve it in terms of what they now remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I think we're basically on the same page about the problem. Just different ideas about dealing with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T19:02:51-07:00","id":1242202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242185#post1242185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy has about three page that directly discuss Apotheosis tucked away in the ST section.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, just to detail where I'm coming from a little bit more precisely, I see the entire GM section as being about Apotheosis to some extent. It might not deal with the process or the mechanics of having achieved it directly, but Apotheosis is why Mummy is divided and the GM section is built to support it. You start off with little memory and gradually rebuild it over the course of a campaign. Apotheosis represents the end goal. Regardless of whether or not it is achieved, the entirety of the GM section is written to provide information you can drip feed players on the course of their progression towards it. Whether or not the players are actively trying to reach Apotheosis, they almost always have some desire to increase their Memory and discover who they have been. Mummy's divide makes the setting itself a secret, but if they aren't going to do something a bit more dramatic with that secret then I don't really feel the need for the fuss in the second edition.<br /> <br /> My players got all their kicks from flashback scenes and the like in personal discoveries, finding out who they had been. That's enough for my group. If Mummy really thinks it needs a wall in the second edition then I just feel they should put something worthwhile behind it, because if not then those personal flashbacks will comfortably pick up the slack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T19:07:34-07:00","id":1242205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242202#post1242202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players got all their kicks from flashback scenes and the like in personal discoveries, finding out who they had been. That's enough for my group. If Mummy really thinks it needs a wall in the second edition then I just feel they should put something worthwhile behind it, because if not then those personal flashbacks will comfortably pick up the slack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could port over Thousand Years of Night's flashback system. Maybe give it some more mechanical teeth, since &quot;Wait a minute, I have three dots in brawl&quot; makes more sense if you are literally reclaiming a memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T19:16:24-07:00","id":1242211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242201#post1242201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I think we're basically on the same page about the problem. Just different ideas about dealing with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does indeed sound like we have very similar philosophies on actually running/playing this game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242205#post1242205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could port over Thousand Years of Night's flashback system. Maybe give it some more mechanical teeth, since &quot;Wait a minute, I have three dots in brawl&quot; makes more sense if you are literally reclaiming a memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I did flashbacks in all sorts of different ways over the course of my games. Mixing it up from time to time was fun. The reason I mention the wall is because the first edition felt the need to make the setting of Mummy a secret that would be revealed in play, but neglected to really have any secrets significant enough to feel worth revealing (at least until the expansions). That's the part I think they need to work on, along with tidying up Apotheosis, if they want to keep the wall. Otherwise I'm happy for them to ditch the GM-player divide entirely, if doing so is too much bother. It probably won't actually change how I run my games either way...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T00:40:29-07:00","id":1242261,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to measure the advantages of Mummy presenting an objective account of events, against presenting readers with historical revisionism and unreliable narrators. The former approach gives the player-base a common ground for discussion and makes in easier to invest into presented concepts. The latter approach enables GMs to choose between alternate truths, which they can tailor for their campaign and use them to actually surprise players, which synergises well with the concept of reclaiming Memory. I wonder what balance will the game go for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T05:53:21-07:00","id":1242318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242167#post1242167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to debate what constitutes as &quot;not broken.&quot; I do think that the bouncing power level is integral part of the mummy experience, but the actual Descent rules in 1st ed are pretty wonky. The starting a low memory thing is also kind of weird and arbitrary since there's no particular in-character reason that all mummies have to have uniformly low starting memory unless you're still in the scene where they're all waking up. In addition, the starting value is far less meaningful in of itself now that morality traits are now longer uniform. (Prometheans start at 1, Changeling is a derived trait, Beast starting value varies, Werewolves want to be at five.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I understand what you're saying, but consider what a higher starting value would mean: your mummy remembers a lot more, or nearly everything? Where's the story in that? Where's the built-in mechanic for character arc and development if you start right out the gate knowing it all?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242181#post1242181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that was probably my favourite part of the teaser.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually one I'm cautious about. I liked that the Judges were distant masters, almost uninterested in the affairs of their servants. There's games out there about Gentry and huntsmen, ghostly reapers, God-machine angels, and I'd even say Deviant conspiracies. Let Mummy portray its niche where the Judges' influence is largely unseen.<br /> <br /> With that said I wouldn't mind knowing more about them. I think what's so engaging about the Deceived is the detail gone into about the temakhs, and I think the Arisen experience would be stronger if we knew more about the Judges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T12:29:02-07:00","id":1242453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241411#post1241411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, things like attempts to recreate the Rite and the results of those,etc would be neat to see in a supplement. Expanding the cults and having the core book go into details on things like blood bathers,etc being part of the supernatural atmosphere around the Deathless is a good touch though I think. It worked well in the Dark Eras materials so anything that expands that is a plus in my book.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I don't think anything non-Iremite should be in the core book. But I would be interested in a &quot;global supplement&quot; because Sekhem is a universal force, not created or exclusive to Irem, humans can use it, and one theme of the game is the world will insist on continuing on and doing things when the Arisen aren't looking. But that could include other types of relic than the familiar five, amkhata and similar beings of unknown types, and different kinds of Sekhem-powered immortals (some of which would be mummified as part of becoming what they are) (also regular mummies would probably make pretty good uter).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1241865#post1241865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, we should try and reverse the derail(my bad folks) and focus on cool stuff like OH MY GOD, WE CAN ACTUALLY PLAY AROUND IN DUAT, WHAT TERRIBLE THINGS WILL THAT RESULT IN.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm with you there. Does this mean mummies can go there during their Descents, or will we see what happens to them in henet?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242172#post1242172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify a little further, Mummy is the <i>only</i> Chronicles game to build itself around a player-GM divide. It calls this out itself in the core. It makes a really freaking big deal about it. But... there's practically nothing behind the core's GM &quot;wall&quot; that feels worth the fuss. Not every game needs something massive for the end game but Mummy very explicitly sold itself as having something. And I don't think it pulled it off well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's worth trying to carry it over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242318#post1242318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually one I'm cautious about. I liked that the Judges were distant masters, almost uninterested in the affairs of their servants. There's games out there about Gentry and huntsmen, ghostly reapers, God-machine angels, and I'd even say Deviant conspiracies. Let Mummy portray its niche where the Judges' influence is largely unseen.<br /> <br /> With that said I wouldn't mind knowing more about them. I think what's so engaging about the Deceived is the detail gone into about the temakhs, and I think the Arisen experience would be stronger if we knew more about the Judges.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question is how overt their influence is? Several fan-hacks have suggested that a nearby crime within your Judge's purview could be an additional reason for waking up - which implies the Judges taking a more active hand in Deathless lives, and also that they can see the world even when their servants are not present - if something like that was incorporated, their presence would be more keenly felt, even if they're never directly encountered. Or else, if the Guilds are &quot;fractured&quot; - whatever that means - perhaps they no longer serve as unifying factions for many Arisen, and the allegiance to your Judge replaces it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T14:07:16-07:00","id":1242485,"title":"","content":"At the risk of overanalysis, the teaser describes the Judge's has having &quot;Presence&quot; that is more &quot;Pervasive&quot; and &quot;Insidious.&quot; (at least that seems like deliberate word choice on the part of the author.) That to me suggests the Judges influence will be reoccurring (Pervasive), but subtle (Presence, Insidious). <br /> <br /> (There's also some ambiguity in the wording as to whether not the change is due to the edition update, or if this is something happening In-Universe. &quot;Featuring the Judge Chronicle&quot; or something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T05:59:55-07:00","id":1242694,"title":"","content":"I do like the fact the the Judges were distant forces...but to the Arisen, they are their Masters and I thought they should have a greater impact on the individuals bound to tuem.<br /> <br /> So the &quot;Pervasive&quot; and &quot;Insidious&quot; presence alluded to in the teaser is very interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T09:16:11-07:00","id":1242737,"title":"","content":"At this point I am not going to speculate or trepidate over what it could possibly mean about the Judges. Especially given the penchant of some to devolve to harassing levels of anger over even the most minor of speculations and just let the info come out when it comes out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T19:22:59-07:00","id":1242842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242737#post1242737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At this point I am not going to speculate or trepidate over what it could possibly mean about the Judges. Especially given the penchant of some to devolve to harassing levels of anger over even the most minor of speculations and just let the info come out when it comes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>But our hate makes us powerful.<br /> <br /> (At least, that's what it says on the pamphlet I got with this cookie...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T17:43:58-07:00","id":1243341,"title":"","content":"I've already settled for the Andean and Chinese Mummies and I think we'll see them in other games. The Andes in Promethean and the Chinese in Desviants.<br /> <br /> But the ideas that the Andean Mummies are formed by nature after a sacrificial ritual similar to that of the Meso-American is historically wrong. Mummification was more like the Egyptian (and it was intentional and post-mortem) than the Sacrifice that was not related to the Mesoamerican sacrifices and seemed like the rare sacrifices in the Fertile Crescent.<br /> <br /> I really hope that Mummy expands to something more Lovecraftian and we have the prehistoric inhuman creatures at least in the Night Horrors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T18:13:19-07:00","id":1243350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1243341#post1243341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the ideas that the Andean Mummies are formed by nature after a sacrificial ritual similar to that of the Meso-American is historically wrong. Mummification was more like the Egyptian (and it was intentional and post-mortem) than the Sacrifice that was not related to the Mesoamerican sacrifices and seemed like the rare sacrifices in the Fertile Crescent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm genuinely curious as to what your sources are for that. The last time I was in Peru I actually got the chance to visit Juanita, for example, and everything there told me she'd been preserved by the ice rather than subjected to a post-mortem mummification ritual. The exhibit could always have been wrong or corrected in the couple of years since but I've never actually heard that argument before and I'd be interested to read up on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T13:37:35-07:00","id":1244259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242694#post1242694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the fact the the Judges were distant forces...but to the Arisen, they are their Masters and I thought they should have a greater impact on the individuals bound to tuem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If nothing else, a little more emphasis on the crimes the Judges preside over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T20:59:51-07:00","id":1244365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1242694#post1242694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the fact the the Judges were distant forces...but to the Arisen, they are their Masters and I thought they should have a greater impact on the individuals bound to tuem.<br /> <br /> So the &quot;Pervasive&quot; and &quot;Insidious&quot; presence alluded to in the teaser is very interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Methinks they'll be more like the temakh are to the Deceived. They're very present, if aloof, forces in your mind that try to contact and order you around regularly, offering carrots and sticks as appropriate. Probably more distant the the temakh by nature, because they aren't possessing their servants, but they know when you're planning to chase Apotheosis, and they don't like it one bit. Also they probably possess you at Memory 0, because being a thug doesn't sound as terrifying as a Memory 0 mummy should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T08:05:43-07:00","id":1244494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1244365#post1244365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Methinks they'll be more like the temakh are to the Deceived. They're very present, if aloof, forces in your mind that try to contact and order you around regularly, offering carrots and sticks as appropriate. Probably more distant the the temakh by nature, because they aren't possessing their servants, but they know when you're planning to chase Apotheosis, and they don't like it one bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps it's more ambiguous. You <i>know</i> when your actions are right and wrong in their eyes, and you <i>know</i> they're watching - but is this knowledge communicated by them, or part of your nature - where's the line between their presence and your sense of duty?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T09:45:25-07:00","id":1244528,"title":"","content":"The latest Pathcast has a short section on 2E: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/special-episode-two-whats-up-with-onyx-path-gen-con-2018/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/special-episo...-gen-con-2018/</a><br /> <br /> Cults can be tiered, we're getting Immortals brought back in the book, and the subtitle will be &quot;The Timeless Chronicle&quot;, so this all sounds suitably <i>amazing</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T10:55:20-07:00","id":1244563,"title":"","content":"I must say that I do like the &quot;timeless&quot; nature of mummies- the fact that you exist in all times and all incarnations sounds really cool, and it actually has some physical sense (I'm a scientist, I love physical sense), and your ability to &quot;remember&quot; the future does sounds really interesting. Also- Immortals getting updated and unified as a part of Mummy's setting. I wonder if the Purified would also be included (Blood Bathers, Eternals and Visitors were mentioned, and Dark Eras has mentioned the Reborn and Body Thieves, but the rest- Purified, Wardens, Patchwork people and Harvester- are an open game)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T11:30:06-07:00","id":1244579,"title":"","content":"I like how the new direction sounds (make the game more Toolbox-y), and the &quot;Timeless&quot; chronicle certainly adds some interesting wrinkles. (starts with Godlike power, ends with Godlike knowledge.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T21:37:28-07:00","id":1244716,"title":"","content":"Anyone who listened to the Podcast could comment on what was spoiled by the developers?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-13T09:01:04-07:00","id":1245509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1244716#post1244716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone who listened to the Podcast could comment on what was spoiled by the developers?</div> </div> </div> </div>You may not experience time as a straight line. More like you're dipping in and out of a river of time.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, you probably were sacrificed along with the rest of the group. So you have an in-setting reason to be grouping up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8719,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","user":"Florin","date":".  I finished listening to the podcast. 08-13-2018, 02:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:24:27-07:00","id":1245854,"title":"","content":"You can invest your Pillars in your cultists. Doing so allows a cultist to access some of a mummy\u2019s related powers, limited by the cultist\u2019s tier. The tiers are:<br /> 1. Ordinary mortals <br /> 2. Sorcerers<br /> 3. Immortals<br /> 4. Sadikh<br /> You can also use Pillars invested in your cultists to resurrect yourself if your body is utterly destroyed, taking their body as your new one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","user":"White Oak Dragon","date":". 08-14-2018, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T06:55:13-07:00","id":1245861,"title":"","content":"I wonder if there would. Be Tibetan and Inca mummies everyone seems to by clamoring for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 08-14-2018, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:13:39-07:00","id":1245872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245861#post1245861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there would. Be Tibetan and Inca mummies everyone seems to by clamoring for them</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies from Irem showing up in Tibet and the Andes? Probable. Mummies-just-like-the-Aisen from there? Unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:41:16-07:00","id":1245875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1244563#post1244563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I must say that I do like the &quot;timeless&quot; nature of mummies- the fact that you exist in all times and all incarnations sounds really cool, and it actually has some physical sense (I'm a scientist, I love physical sense), and your ability to &quot;remember&quot; the future does sounds really interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>All</i> incarnations? Does that mean all instances of awakening as a mummy, or does it include your mortal life too? Still, it ties in with the idea that the Rite broke time in some fashion. But the question that jumps out at me most was whether this was an intended effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also- Immortals getting updated and unified as a part of Mummy's setting. I wonder if the Purified would also be included (Blood Bathers, Eternals and Visitors were mentioned, and Dark Eras has mentioned the Reborn and Body Thieves, but the rest- Purified, Wardens, Patchwork people and Harvester- are an open game) </div> </div> </div>Unified... does that mean they're being incorporated into Mummy's mythos, as beings of Sekhem? Most of them seem like they could fit in reasonably well (Patchworks I'd rather see plugged into Promethean). Reliquary is something I wouldn't mind seeing unified with Mummy as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245509#post1245509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You may not experience time as a straight line. More like you're dipping in and out of a river of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>How prominent a part did that sound like it was playing?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245854#post1245854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can invest your Pillars in your cultists. Doing so allows a cultist to access some of a mummy\u2019s related powers, limited by the cultist\u2019s tier. The tiers are:<br /> 1. Ordinary mortals<br /> 2. Sorcerers<br /> 3. Immortals<br /> 4. Sadikh</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh. Implying that sorcery will be in the core too. Are &quot;Sorcerer&quot; and &quot;Immortal&quot; things that the mummy can grant (implying that mummies can be sorcerers too), or does the mortal have to come by them another way?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245861#post1245861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if there would. Be Tibetan and Inca mummies everyone seems to by clamoring for them</div> </div> </div> </div>If immortals are getting included in the core, then they might be a subset of those. Otherwise, I'd be <i>really</i> surprised. (The best place for them IMO would be a supplement on non-Iremite expressions of Sekhem - covering relics from crafts other than the &quot;big five,&quot; amkhata formed from foreign animals, and different forms of sekhem-infused people and animals, some of which could be mummified as part of the process).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T07:47:09-07:00","id":1245877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245875#post1245875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>All</i> <br /> How prominent a part did that sound like it was playing?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounded like it was mostly an explanation to justify some of the wonky things about being a mummy involving memory, skills, etc. However, it could hold greater prominence than I interpreted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:05:18-07:00","id":1245880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245877#post1245877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounded like it was mostly an explanation to justify some of the wonky things about being a mummy involving memory, skills, etc. However, it could hold greater prominence than I interpreted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the way they pick up languages quickly?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T08:35:05-07:00","id":1245892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245880#post1245880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the way they pick up languages quickly?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, that kind of thing. Matthew mentioned a couple of things, but I don't remember them off the top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-14T11:08:05-07:00","id":1245972,"title":"","content":"With it being called the Timeless Chronicle, I\u2019m sure it will be very prominent, or at least have easy options to make it so.","signa