 Chile.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) This is already how it goes.<br /> 2) This is already how it goes.<br /> 2) Still impossible based on the rest of what is said. We have a time frame for when the Nameless Empire happened, we even know when you became Arisen, you're still an Iremite, and 7000 BCE is right out.<br /> <br /> Nothing has changed here. Maybe it's clarified, but nothing has changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-18-2018, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:11:11-07:00","id":1247551,"title":"","content":"Well...depending how badly the Rite of Return broke time, it might be doable, but that is not among the information we have on 2e.<br /> <br /> I would not hold my breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:17:40-07:00","id":1247554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247472#post1247472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's entirely possible to make a character who has a Chinchorro body, speaks their tongue, and remembers what it was like to live in 7000 BCE in what is now northern Chile.</div> </div> </div> </div>As pointed out, this is unlikely, though mostly due to the last one.<br /> <br /> An Arisen could have a Chinchorro body by either their Sahu subtly reshaping until it matched, or more directly by returning in a Chinchorro cultist who was holding one of their Pillars. Speaking the language - well, they just have to learn it. But memories from that far back? Not gonna happen, if they think they are actually Chilean. I'm iffy on the exact timeline, but they would have to have first lived in Irem, undergone the Rite of Return, arose during the first Sothic Turn, then migrated to the region, and formed a cult/assimilated. <i>Then</i> their Memory would have to decay so that they think their recent memories are of their origin. I don't think that would have all happened 9K years ago...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:35:47-07:00","id":1247561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247472#post1247472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's entirely possible to make a character who has a Chinchorro body, speaks their tongue, and remembers what it was like to live in 7000 BCE in what is now northern Chile.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the others have pointed out, the time frame is right out... but there's never been anything preventing you from playing a character who was deluded <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can do all of this with a current Mummy character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T19:03:02-07:00","id":1247583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247472#post1247472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's entirely possible to make a character who has a Chinchorro body, speaks their tongue, and remembers what it was like to live in 7000 BCE in what is now northern Chile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, since this tangent is not going away soon, let's examine it.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...depending how badly the Rite of Return broke time, it might be doable, but that is not among the information we have on 2e.<br /> <br /> I would not hold my breath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following up with that, the earlist point observed in the Chronicles so far is the Sundered World (Dark Eras, 5500-5000 BCE) which states that the Shan'iatu are yet to create Irem.<br /> <br /> This means that A) previous cultures lacked the information on Sekhem to attempt the Rite; B) had to deal with Pangeans and the Border Marches in addition to everything else.<br /> <br /> Now, nothing is stopping you from playing it your way at your table. Trying to make it canonical has issues that can mostly be dealt with via the Rite of Return breaking reality or your character being mistaken about their memories.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Chinchorro could not puzzle out the world's greatest act of sorcery, but did manage to create a potential recepticle/vessel. Maybe the broken soul that returned from Duat and came to inhabit this vessel did not remember the mortal life they had before this Descent. But there are a lot of assumptions and handwaves there. We can't really say that is an option, nor do I personally feel we have enough information about the culture this example is meant to emulate to do so in a non-offensive manner.<br /> At my table I would request not only the player do research, but share that research with the ST.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the timeframe makes me more inclinde to look at other immortals, such as Purified or Blood Bather; neither of which works as a 'mummy'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T01:28:19-07:00","id":1247641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247583#post1247583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, since this tangent is not going away soon, let's examine it.<br /> <br /> Following up with that, the earlist point observed in the Chronicles so far is the Sundered World (Dark Eras, 5500-5000 BCE) which states that the Shan'iatu are yet to create Irem.<br /> <br /> This means that A) previous cultures lacked the information on Sekhem to attempt the Rite; B) had to deal with Pangeans and the Border Marches in addition to everything else.<br /> <br /> Now, nothing is stopping you from playing it your way at your table. Trying to make it canonical has issues that can mostly be dealt with via the Rite of Return breaking reality or your character being mistaken about their memories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building a little on the chronology, for the thread's sake:<br /> <br /> As mentioned, the earliest covered point in Chronicles history is the Dark Era The Sundered World, taking place from 5500 to 5000 BCE. In this time, Azar will eventually be killed and shipped off to Duat via Iset Ghost leading the creation of the star Sodpet because!<br /> <br /> In both the Book of the Deceived and Dreams of Avarice, it is firmly stated that with the death of Azar and the shipment of his body by means of the corpse/ghost of Iset comes the birth of the star Sodpet, the star by which the Sothic Cycle is determined and hinged on. Now putting aside real world actual evidence, we know when <i>this</i> happened because one Sothic Cycle later, the Rite of Return was performed, taking advantage of the changing Cycle, and the Nameless Empire was sacrificed off the map, and we know when <i>that</i> happened, because<br /> <br /> a) Sothis Ascends literally tells us that around 3832, the Rite of Return was performed and Irem disappeared, and it would be one Sothic Cycle later when Mummies entered the scene again the event of the Cannibal Hymn,<br /> b) backtracking a Sothic Cycle gives us a time frame of 5293 BCE, and<br /> c) also we know that the Empire started somewhere between those two points because the Book of the Decieved makes it clear that most of the events, including the creation of the Empire, fall between these two Sothic Cycles.<br /> <br /> TL;DR, It is literally the time frame killing the argument.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;but what if I want to play a mummy who believes themselves to be an ancient Chinchorro within the time frame?&quot;, well, yeah, that was always doable. Upon awakening, all you remember is your name, your Judge, your Guild, and a <i>little bit</i> about Irem, with some details about the previous Descent in rough detail. That automatically gives the recent history more precedent over the culture of Irem outside of the essentials of your job. As they rise in Memory by one, they remember a little more about Irem, yes, but they also still remember more about their previous Descent, making the last culture you were in as much a major influence as the Nameless Empire. From there, it takes <i>Memory 8</i> to really fully remember their mortal life in Irem, by which time their current experience is already colored by the many lives they've had and the current incarnation of the Guilds they operate in and around, many of which are heavily influenced by the cultures they are entrenched in.<br /> <br /> Mix in a decent reason for them to be Twice-Arisen, and you basically have your ancient Chinchorro.<br /> <br /> Again, nothing is new on this note of news. It might clarify this point more, but it was always there.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the more intriguing point of it all is how it reinforces this sense of Mummy's Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T09:28:36-07:00","id":1247737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247641#post1247641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mix in a decent reason for them to be Twice-Arisen, and you basically have your ancient Chinchorro.</div> </div> </div> </div>That argument sounds convincing to someone with no interest in playing an Andean (or otherwise non-Iremite) mummy, but is basically the same argument as those who said there was no need for a Mummy game at all because you could just play an Osirian or Mekhet, or no need for a Demon game because you could play a vampire, or no need for playable ghosts because you could play a Sineater (none of those are hypothetical - they're all arguments I've actually heard first hand). But since I don't want anything non-Iremite in the core either, I'll leave it there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T09:31:30-07:00","id":1247738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247737#post1247737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That argument sounds convincing to someone with no interest in playing an Andean (or otherwise non-Iremite) mummy, but is basically the same argument as those who said there was no need for a Mummy game at all because you could just play an Osirian or Mekhet, or no need for a Demon game because you could play a vampire, or no need for playable ghosts because you could play a Sineater (none of those are hypothetical - they're all arguments I've actually heard first hand). But since I don't want anything non-Iremite in the core either, I'll leave it there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think my stance as someone firmly interested in the Nameless Empire's immortal monsters is pretty well known.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T10:28:14-07:00","id":1247752,"title":"","content":"*Scrubbed*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 08-19-2018, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T03:39:14-07:00","id":1247968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247737#post1247737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That argument sounds convincing to someone with no interest in playing an Andean (or otherwise non-Iremite) mummy, but is basically the same argument as those who said there was no need for a Mummy game at all because you could just play an Osirian or Mekhet, or no need for a Demon game because you could play a vampire, or no need for playable ghosts because you could play a Sineater (none of those are hypothetical - they're all arguments I've actually heard first hand). But since I don't want anything non-Iremite in the core either, I'll leave it there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a particularly good argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC, but then it really wasn't an argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC anyway. Just ArcaneArts pointing out that the recent podcast didn't add anything for that prospect that wasn't already present in 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T08:22:15-07:00","id":1248062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247551#post1247551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well...depending how badly the Rite of Return broke time, it might be doable, but that is not among the information we have on 2e.<br /> <br /> I would not hold my breath.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, Matthew made it sound like Mummies experience time non-linearly. So, it's possible but not probable they could experience time before they existed. However, I never read past the corebook in Mummy. So, Irem has always existed in some nebulous time for me without any actual year attached to it. And in that case, it works just fine if you put Irem early enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T08:37:33-07:00","id":1248070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247968#post1247968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't a particularly good argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC, but then it really wasn't an argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC anyway. Just ArcaneArts pointing out that the recent podcast didn't add anything for that prospect that wasn't already present in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the original developer has gone on about the sort of realities of the cultures a mummy could have adopted along their incredibly long existences since at least the preview time period including the Con audio before Mummy was out so I don't know why people keep acting surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T09:14:02-07:00","id":1248090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248062#post1248062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah, Matthew made it sound like Mummies experience time non-linearly. So, it's possible but not probable they could experience time before they existed. However, I never read past the corebook in Mummy. So, Irem has always existed in some nebulous time for me without any actual year attached to it. And in that case, it works just fine if you put Irem early enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the &quot;non-Linear Time&quot; bit may be restricted to their Descents - so if you have a Flashback, you can just treat your character then as a continuation of your character &quot;now&quot;, instead of having to figure out what your character would have been like (built) in that time period. And why all of that went away when you woke up &quot;now&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T09:29:57-07:00","id":1248100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247968#post1247968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't a particularly good argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC, but then it really wasn't an argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I meant was that &quot;Playing a deluded and amnesic Iremite mummy is basically the same as playing a Chinchorro one&quot; is only ever going to sound convincing to those with no interest in playing a Chinchorro one. But anyway, the Chinchorro practice of mummification is too early to derive from Irem.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to the Iremites.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1246335#post1246335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see that Irem practice of forcing slaves to dig for gold<br /> <br /> And big companies forcing indigenous people to dig up cobalt Inst reallly different</div> </div> </div> </div>The parallels between Irem and now are one of my favourite things. Not just seeing echoes of the master/slave and exploitation dynamics, but Irem was a time of rapid technological growth, a revolution in communications, and a milieu were concepts were in common currency that hadn't existed a mere century before. It's a fascinating contrast to the future shock that most stories of immortals rely on, particularly those with punctuated lives like the Arisen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248090#post1248090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the &quot;non-Linear Time&quot; bit may be restricted to their Descents - so if you have a Flashback, you can just treat your character then as a continuation of your character &quot;now&quot;, instead of having to figure out what your character would have been like (built) in that time period. And why all of that went away when you woke up &quot;now&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think someone described it earlier as you kind of existing in all your Descents &quot;at once,&quot; so you could pick up things from your future lives as well as your past ones. That doesn't sound like you'd be existing at any other time - but the question of whether it applies to an Arisen's mortal life is interesting - it makes sense that it wouldn't, though.<br /> <br /> There was something I'd wondered about earlier, but it fell by the wayside. To those who have listened to the podcast, particularly this bit:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1245854#post1245854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can invest your Pillars in your cultists. Doing so allows a cultist to access some of a mummy\u2019s related powers, limited by the cultist\u2019s tier. The tiers are:<br /> 1. Ordinary mortals<br /> 2. Sorcerers<br /> 3. Immortals<br /> 4. Sadikh</div> </div> </div> </div>... did it sound like the &quot;sorcerer&quot; and &quot;immortal&quot; parts were things mummies could make someone into, the way they can a sadikh? Or would the cultist have to come by those conditions another way?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:00:40-07:00","id":1248116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1247968#post1247968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It wasn't a particularly good argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC, but then it really wasn't an argument for playing a Chinchorro mummy in MTC anyway. Just ArcaneArts pointing out that the recent podcast didn't add anything for that prospect that wasn't already present in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Again, my positions are made pretty clear.<br /> <br /> Now I will point out that the specific post that warranted the response did not specifically call out being natively Chinchorro beyond possibly it's time frame, and some of the following conversation was basically more about valuing a different culture over Irem's, which is kind of already a big deal for Mummy-the world you live in as the Arisen is one with the benefit of hindsight, and a big part of how the game works is looking back at what you remember of the Nameless Empire through the critical lens of the societies and cultures they've taken part in and deciding whether things were better or right or true or &quot;just the way things are&quot; then or if it's a thing to escape from.<br /> <br /> In that vein of the last point, a mummy being(as in choosing to be) Chinchorro over being an Iremite is hella important, and with it understanding that you not only can but do have a period of your Descent where you don't <i>inherently</i> know that you're an Iremite, or what life in the Nameless Empire is like, and will thus more strongly associate with the cultures of your Descents is likewise important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T20:41:34-07:00","id":1248292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248116#post1248116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">understanding that you not only can but do have a period of your Descent where you don't <i>inherently</i> know that you're an Iremite, or what life in the Nameless Empire is like, and will thus more strongly associate with the cultures of your Descents is likewise important.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still a fancy way of saying &quot;Your character can always just be amnesiac and deluded.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here's a question: if the Judge's are going to have a greater presence, if an insidious one, what does that mean for the Shan'iatu? Going by the Book of the Deceived, the intended to supplant the Judges, but either failed or are still in the middle of their attempt. But the Deathless are also their creations, so the Deathless serving the Judges is a little at odds with that - that was true in the first edition too, but if the Judges are playing a greater role, that's brought further to the foreground.<br /> So what do people think? Do the Shan'iatu still mean to replace the Judges, with the Deathless will ending up serving them instead - or did the make the attempt and it's definitively failed, so their intended servants now serve their intended victims - or will they have succeeded this time around - or do they have another plan? (One of my theories had always been that it was &quot;Here, have these as your servants instead of us &quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T20:55:47-07:00","id":1248295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248292#post1248292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here's a question: if the Judge's are going to have a greater presence, if an insidious one, what does that mean for the Shan'iatu? Going by the Book of the Deceived, the intended to supplant the Judges, but either failed or are still in the middle of their attempt. But the Deathless are also their creations, so the Deathless serving the Judges is a little at odds with that - that was true in the first edition too, but if the Judges are playing a greater role, that's brought further to the foreground.<br /> So what do people think? Do the Shan'iatu still mean to replace the Judges, with the Deathless will ending up serving them instead - or did the make the attempt and it's definitively failed, so their intended servants now serve their intended victims - or will they have succeeded this time around - or do they have another plan? (One of my theories had always been that it was &quot;Here, have these as your servants instead of us &quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the best approach, at least for a corebook, is to leave the answer to this conundrum ambigious. (Though possibly put the question front and center rather than drawing it out.) The Answer probably won't have immediate consequences for your everyday descent, and there's a multitude of possible directions for &quot;what's the deal with the Judges&quot; to take. The whole Timeless quality adds another wrinkle. (If the Shan'iatu are going to have have usurped the Judges, would the Arisen have been always serving their will even when the original Judges were chronologically speaking, in charge.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T21:01:02-07:00","id":1248299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248292#post1248292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a fancy way of saying &quot;Your character can always just be amnesiac and deluded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the original post by Florin, yes, that's exactly what we think he was advocating.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248292#post1248292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a question: if the Judge's are going to have a greater presence, if an insidious one, what does that mean for the Shan'iatu? Going by the Book of the Deceived, the intended to supplant the Judges, but either failed or are still in the middle of their attempt. But the Deathless are also their creations, so the Deathless serving the Judges is a little at odds with that - that was true in the first edition too, but if the Judges are playing a greater role, that's brought further to the foreground.<br /> So what do people think? Do the Shan'iatu still mean to replace the Judges, with the Deathless will ending up serving them instead - or did the make the attempt and it's definitively failed, so their intended servants now serve their intended victims - or will they have succeeded this time around - or do they have another plan? (One of my theories had always been that it was &quot;Here, have these as your servants instead of us &quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>It was never entirely clear whether the original Judges of Life were the same as the Judges in the core book, or whether the latter were created as part of some cosmic exchange/perversion of the natural order by the Shan'iatu, or if the Shan'iatu became the Judges in the corebook (and whether those are the same as the Judges of Life), or whether the ritual failed entirely and the Arisen are bound to the original Judges as a form of permanent penance for enabling the Shan'iatu to even attempt such blasphemy, or... you get the idea. It's a very fuzzy grey area. We might get some clearer answers in second edition.<br /> <br /> I always assumed the Judges of Life and the core book Judges were the same, which is where that slight dissonance creeps in, so it'll be interesting to see how second edition answers it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T21:09:17-07:00","id":1248303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248292#post1248292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's still a fancy way of saying &quot;Your character can always just be amnesiac and deluded.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if you really want to toss everything I said out the window and replace it with something stupidly reductive.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, there's a case for that, but the people who might find that attractive for avoiding the Nameless Empire and the rest of that bag are also not going to be satisfied by that response, so it's very definitely not my point.<br /> <br /> My <i>point</i> is that a big part of the game is making the decision, as an Arisen, about whether or not the way the Nameless Empire was is truly the way of things and that adhering to it's central position of the nature of existence is the best course of action OR that the societies that have emerged since then have revealed fuller truths that are more harmonious with the nature of things and rebelling against the old judgments against flawed humanity, AND that the ability to be a full participant in those societies for a time is important for establishing the contrast of those choices, thereby rendering desires to be [X] mummies more meaningful then simply changing out the Nameless Empire with [X].<br /> <br /> Also, Curse is not a game about how it's odd that we've started applying a slang term for Egyptian corpses to every preserved body. See &quot;my positions are well known.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T22:02:57-07:00","id":1248318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248303#post1248303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Curse is not a game about how it's odd that we've started applying a slang term for Egyptian corpses to every preserved body.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>not</i> odd that we used a term referring to preserved corpses to refer to other preserved corpses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See &quot;my positions are well known.&quot; </div> </div> </div>And yet out of the two of us, I'm the one who keeps trying to turn the conversation back to Irem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248295#post1248295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Answer probably won't have immediate consequences for your everyday descent, and there's a multitude of possible directions for &quot;what's the deal with the Judges&quot; to take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The whole Timeless quality adds another wrinkle. (If the Shan'iatu are going to have have usurped the Judges, would the Arisen have been always serving their will even when the original Judges were chronologically speaking, in charge.) </div> </div> </div>It also opens the way for the Shan'iatu to be the Judges, even when their &quot;lifespans&quot; overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248299#post1248299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always assumed the Judges of Life and the core book Judges were the same, which is where that slight dissonance creeps in, so it'll be interesting to see how second edition answers it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too - also, one of the developers said that the Shan'iatu and the Judges weren't the same, and both numbering 42 was a red herring - less of one when the Deceived book came out, though. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It will be interesting to see whether the second edition holds to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 08-21-2018, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T13:34:55-07:00","id":1248497,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"321\" data-vbnamecard=\"321\">SunlessNick</a> I think you should read Dreams of Avarice. It has some of the answers you seem to seek (like, who are the Judges, their connection to the Shan'itau and the finale fate of those who devised the Rite of Return)<br /> <br /> EDIT- unless you read it, of course. I don't know, after reading DoA, it was very clear to me who the Judges are, and how fucked up are, well, <i>everyone</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 08-21-2018, 04:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T22:40:09-07:00","id":1248629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248497#post1248497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT- unless you read it, of course. I don't know, after reading DoA, it was very clear to me who the Judges are, and