n-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T08:16:07-07:00","id":1251072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1251056#post1251056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Please</i>, I can handle that just fine. By the way, does any of you know a sculptor who's good at making big self-aggrandizing statues? Either marble or gold is fine. Asking for a friend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, you need a blend to really bring out a person's features.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T10:47:29-07:00","id":1251103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1251072#post1251072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, you need a blend to really bring out a person's features.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it probably also needs some onyx or obsidian as well.<br /> <br /> And what are you doing if you don't have some lapis lazuli or precious gemstone mixed in.<br /> <br /> And really, it also needs, like, saint's bones on the inside so that it can capture the purity of the character it presents.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust some thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T11:35:52-07:00","id":1251126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1251103#post1251103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, it probably also needs some onyx or obsidian as well.<br /> <br /> And what are you doing if you don't have some lapis lazuli or precious gemstone mixed in.<br /> <br /> And really, it also needs, like, saint's bones on the inside so that it can capture the purity of the character it presents.<br /> <br /> \u200bJust some thoughts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dammit, even if I think I can steal a sain'ts bone easily around here, that still raises the costs way beyond my budget. Ehm, my friend's budget, I mean.<br /> <br /> Also, since I don't want to derail the thread too much, these are also <b>#cultproblems</b>. And after this silly joke, I'll go back to the actual Mummy books <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T12:00:03-07:00","id":1251131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1251126#post1251126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit, even if I think I can steal a sain'ts bone easily around here, that still raises the costs way beyond my budget. Ehm, my friend's budget, I mean.<br /> <br /> Also, since I don't want to derail the thread too much, these are also <b>#cultproblems</b>. And after this silly joke, I'll go back to the actual Mummy books <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's almost like the people you rely on to handle the regular affairs of your portion of an endless empire have power over you as regards all of that and also have their own personalities and agendas.<br /> <br /> I'm not as cult crazy as everyone else, but that is neat to hear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T12:02:01-07:00","id":1251132,"title":"","content":"So, question: Are Witnesses being altered beyond &quot;these people are immune to Sybaris&quot;? I don't need to know what the changes are (because that probably isn't even finalized), but knowing if they are getting looked at and redone (or not) would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T14:34:22-07:00","id":1251187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1250842#post1250842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not going to say much but hell, I need to learn to celebrate the good things: I'm also part of the Mummy writing team. For a first freelancing job, I could not have asked for more. I hope this will be the first of many Onyx Path books I'll work on, but this is already a honor.<br /> <br /> As part of the Iremite pact I had to make I can't let out any details, but trust me when I say that 2nd Edition will be awesome. The whole team is filled with talented and passionate people and it's quite surreal for me to actually be a part of that.<br /> <br /> If a Peter Cushing expy makes it into the final book, blame me.<br /> <br /> Also, because I need to try it once: so far, my favorite thing about the 2nd Edition is [REDACTED]</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations, Cinder. We\u2019re happy to have you on the team. And I agree, [REDACTED] is awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T17:09:02-07:00","id":1251234,"title":"","content":"Can't believe I didn't think of it earlier but one thing I hope gets updated, improved, touched on more,etc is death curses. They felt a little up and down and wonky in 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T07:57:30-07:00","id":1252506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1248303#post1248303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, if you really want to toss everything I said out the window and replace it with something stupidly reductive.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeah, there's a case for that, but the people who might find that attractive for avoiding the Nameless Empire and the rest of that bag are also not going to be satisfied by that response, so it's very definitely not my point.<br /> <br /> My <i>point</i> is that a big part of the game is making the decision, as an Arisen, about whether or not the way the Nameless Empire was is truly the way of things and that adhering to it's central position of the nature of existence is the best course of action OR that the societies that have emerged since then have revealed fuller truths that are more harmonious with the nature of things and rebelling against the old judgments against flawed humanity, AND that the ability to be a full participant in those societies for a time is important for establishing the contrast of those choices, thereby rendering desires to be [X] mummies more meaningful then simply changing out the Nameless Empire with [X].<br /> <br /> Also, Curse is not a game about how it's odd that we've started applying a slang term for Egyptian corpses to every preserved body. See \u201cmy positions are well known.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I've recently mentioned it elsewhere, but I figured I'd mention it in the Mummy forum as well: I wouldn't object to mummy-like immortals derived from other cultures being introduced into <b>Mummy 2e</b> \u2014 though I'd probably leave toward doing so in a <b>Night Horrors</b> supplement rather than, say, the core book or the Player's Guide, just to highlight that they're not <i>really</i> intended to be player characters (though, like some of the other kinds of vampires found in <b>Wicked Dead</b>, there might be enough to allow them to be played if someone wants to) but rather as antagonists such as rivals. The Purified, for instance, could be reintroduced into Chronicles of Darkness in this way, possibly revealing that as the Iremite immortals started their Diaspora from Egypt, they encountered the Purified in the Far East, implying that the first Purified were Asian mummies. Likewise, Iremites who migrated to South America might have encountered a different kind of immortal deriving from various local cultures' views on life after death \u2014 though, like the Purified, I'd want to emphasize the differences between them and the Arisen; make them their own thing that doesn't tread on the central role that Iremites have in the game. <br /> <br /> Part of it is that as old as the Nameless Empire is, it's not the oldest civilization ever; and challenges to whether the Iremite way is the best way don't have to come just from younger cultures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-08T18:05:14-07:00","id":1252634,"title":"","content":"Meow. Maybe they\u2019ll do something with witnesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T15:58:40-07:00","id":1253153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1252506#post1252506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently mentioned it elsewhere, but I figured I'd mention it in the Mummy forum as well: I wouldn't object to mummy-like immortals derived from other cultures being introduced into <b>Mummy 2e</b> \u2014 though I'd probably leave toward doing so in a <b>Night Horrors</b> supplement rather than, say, the core book or the Player's Guide, just to highlight that they're not <i>really</i> intended to be player characters (though, like some of the other kinds of vampires found in <b>Wicked Dead</b>...</div> </div> </div> </div>This is essentially how I've seen it since the game was released. I don't know why it's so important to folks to have non-Iremite mummies, or what it adds to the game, but I'm totally on board with putting them in as antagonists in a Night Horrors book. It's reasonable that other cultures have mystical rituals involving the sanctity of their dead, and even that some cultures attempted to copy and re-create the Rite of Return after encountering the Deathless, but mummies <i>as a horror trope</i> belong to Egypt and that needs to be the game's foundation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:14:25-07:00","id":1253167,"title":"","content":"Well, the other thing that <b>Mummy</b> is big on is stories that span history. That's easier to do when you can have recurring characters that span history, too \u2014 which is the other use that non-Iremite immortals serve. And I mean that in the broadest sense, including the likes of vampires as well as Blood Bathers, Body Thieves, Purified, and others. And not <i>just</i> as foils, but also as allies. <br /> <br /> One thing that I remember the original writer of Mummy saying once was that he wanted the game to be about more than just the Arisen. That's what the chronicle Frameworks were supposed to be about<b></b>: encouraging playstyles that feature a mixture of character types, not just the one \u2014 although, the game being <b>Mummy</b>, that one should always have a presence in the story. I'm hoping that 2e gets back to that idea, with more emphasis on others who have become involved in Item's legacy. And that can include Chinese and Andean mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:32:05-07:00","id":1253173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1250842#post1250842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not going to say much but hell, I need to learn to celebrate the good things: I'm also part of the Mummy writing team. For a first freelancing job, I could not have asked for more. I hope this will be the first of many Onyx Path books I'll work on, but this is already a honor.<br /> <br /> As part of the Iremite pact I had to make I can't let out any details, but trust me when I say that 2nd Edition will be awesome. The whole team is filled with talented and passionate people and it's quite surreal for me to actually be a part of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay! Looking forward to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-10T17:35:36-07:00","id":1253174,"title":"","content":"I think the point of contention/contrast for some people is that having other sorts of attempts at the Rite of Return,etc makes sense as material for the game line. But there is a contingent of people that seem to push that inclusion in the direction of harming some of the core themes of Mummy with how they want to include non Iremite style mummies. It's a small difference, but an important one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T14:24:46-07:00","id":1253381,"title":"","content":"Inclusion for the sake of inclusion is bad. Now if it adds to the story, that's good<br /> <br /> For example, the aquaman movie is making to where aquaman is related to Polynesian mythology, and that is actually cool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T14:57:45-07:00","id":1253385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1253381#post1253381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inclusion for the sake of inclusion is bad. Now if it adds to the story, that's good<br /> <br /> For example, the aquaman movie is making to where aquaman is related to Polynesian mythology, and that is actually cool</div> </div> </div> </div>1) casting Jason Momoa justifies itself because he\u2019s awesome and thus is not \u201cjust for inclusion\u201d. It can be \u201cjust for Jason Momoa\u201d and be a good enough reason.<br /> <br /> 2) The Aquaman canon they\u2019re drawing on is as much an interracial narrative as Superman\u2019s is an immigrant narrative. Casting an interracial actor to play that role is already justified by that reality without other changes being necessary.<br /> <br /> 3) The reason the core Justice Leaguers are as white as they are is because of publishing norms in the 40s-60s. New media updating their origins to be contemporary, instead reflecting current social norms around race as diversity (just as the all-white except the one green guy League reflected social norms) is justified without needing the above two points.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is a sore spot for me, because of being asked to justify LGBT characters\u2019 identity as plot relevant in my own original work, but NEVER being asked to justify a characters\u2019 hetersexuality or cis-status. \u201cIt needs to be plot relevant or its pandering\u201d is a standard that is only ever applied to minority representation, but never majority representation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T15:51:51-07:00","id":1253399,"title":"","content":"Did you think I was criticising it? I actually meant they made the character aquaman cool again and made a backstory involving the actors culture. I think they did a good job","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T15:55:15-07:00","id":1253400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1253399#post1253399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you think I was criticising it? I actually meant they made the character aquaman cool again and made a backstory involving the actors culture. I think they did a good job</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sorry, knee jerk response from putting up with a lot of bullshit. I thought you were saying it WOULD be ok IF they sufficiently do (x) in his solo movie, but it needs to reach that standard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T15:58:12-07:00","id":1253403,"title":"","content":"Oh I understand. As a conservative, the only thing that actually annoys me is the &quot;shipping&quot; of every couple of characters who are great friends and such. It's like friendship automatically means romantic relationship","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T16:21:51-07:00","id":1253408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1253403#post1253403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I understand. As a conservative, the only thing that actually annoys me is the &quot;shipping&quot; of every couple of characters who are great friends and such. It's like friendship automatically means romantic relationship</div> </div> </div> </div>It pisses me off when actual writers clearly feel that way about male/female friendships (I will never forgive Warehouse 13!)<br /> <br /> No comment on straight shippers with fetishes, but for the actual LGBT audience, queering texts for our own enjoyment is a response to so rarely getting actual media that reflects us and our relationships. You\u2019ll theoretically one day see way less shipping from us of characters extradiagetically intended to be straight platonic friends when we actually also get the stories we want in our mass market superhero/fantasy/scifi/etc/etc genre fiction so we don\u2019t have to create it out of what\u2019s there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T16:49:12-07:00","id":1253414,"title":"","content":"Understandable, but to be honest, i just meant in general. And when I think of forced romantic straight relationships, i think Batman and Wonder Woman","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-12T09:05:08-07:00","id":1253607,"title":"","content":"Wow! Man, I seriously always love it when I see people I enjoyed forum exchanges in the first months of a 1e game line to end up a freelancer in 2e, or even if i had just been a general fan of their forum posts. I am once again glad to congratulate the new iremite crew, I've been a big fan of a few of you that I didn't realize are working on 2e! That pleases me so much, and makes me quite confident that this game will deliver!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T13:07:28-07:00","id":1257250,"title":"","content":"I really hope there\u2019s a reference to Sybaris being channeled by a CHILDS CARD GAME","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T15:40:53-07:00","id":1257850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1257250#post1257250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope there\u2019s a reference to Sybaris being channeled by a CHILDS CARD GAME</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Now, after 5000 years of waiting, I'm going to challenge you to a children's card game! And then I'll destroy the world!&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;</b>Why would you want to do that?&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;</b>What?&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;</b>What's the point in destroying the world? What do you gain from it?&quot;<br /> &quot;...I don't understand the question.&quot;<br /> &quot;Look, you must have some reason for wanting to destroy the world. Otherwise, this whole movie was just pointless bickering!&quot;<br /> &quot;Of course I have a reason!&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, goodie! Do you feel like sharing it with the class?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, it's a secret.&quot;<br /> <br /> TL;DR:<i> Mummy: The Curse the Abridged Series</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-28T15:49:18-07:00","id":1257851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1257250#post1257250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope there\u2019s a reference to Sybaris being channeled by a CHILDS CARD GAME</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1257850#post1257850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Now, after 5000 years of waiting, I'm going to challenge you to a children's card game! And then I'll destroy the world!&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;</b>Why would you want to do that?&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;</b>What?&quot;<br /> <b>&quot;</b>What's the point in destroying the world? What do you gain from it?&quot;<br /> &quot;...I don't understand the question.&quot;<br /> &quot;Look, you must have some reason for wanting to destroy the world. Otherwise, this whole movie was just pointless bickering!&quot;<br /> &quot;Of course I have a reason!&quot;<br /> &quot;Oh, goodie! Do you feel like sharing it with the class?&quot;<br /> &quot;No, it's a secret.&quot;<br /> <br /> TL;DR:<i> Mummy: The Curse the Abridged Series</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Obligatory mention:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Oh1nqnZAKxw\" data-code=\"Oh1nqnZAKxw\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/Oh1nqnZAKxw/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-29T04:44:49-07:00","id":1257946,"title":"","content":"ANCIENT EGYPTATIN LASER BEAMS!!<br /> <br /> PS I can also imagine Thief King Bakura as a Shuankhsen","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 09-29-2018, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T10:31:33-08:00","id":1271490,"title":"","content":"With <b>They Came From Beneath The Sea!</b> as the next kickstarter, it looks like Mummy will be in 2019?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12820-mythicjustice","name":"MythicJustice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T12:12:48-08:00","id":1271530,"title":"","content":"One of the absences I feel most strongly with Mummy is that it's the only splat which doesn't really &quot;blend&quot; with the regular world and which doesn't really have a persistent community its members belong to. I hope that becomes more of a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> I also very much want more reasons for actual Arisen working together to be the default mode of play rather than indicative of some rare and unusual situation. Nobody wants to feel like they're just the sidekick. And the game is Mummy, so let's play Mummies - if I wanted to play mortals in an occult world I'd just play the blue book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-28T13:35:45-08:00","id":1271556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cielle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1271530#post1271530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the absences I feel most strongly with Mummy is that it's the only splat which doesn't really &quot;blend&quot; with the regular world and which doesn't really have a persistent community its members belong to. I hope that becomes more of a thing in 2e.<br /> <br /> I also very much want more reasons for actual Arisen working together to be the default mode of play rather than indicative of some rare and unusual situation. Nobody wants to feel like they're just the sidekick. And the game is Mummy, so let's play Mummies - if I wanted to play mortals in an occult world I'd just play the blue book.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the former, their seperation from the mortal world was part of the point of their imposed isolation, though Cults remained an important means for them to interact with humanity, and ideally characters will gain Touchstones as they decrease in Sekhem/rise in Memory. As for mummy society, the later books do a good job of establishing a more persistent and richly involved community, and the Second Edition core needs to bring more of that to the front.<br /> <br /> As for the latter, to be fair, the mixed gameplay argument makes sense given how top-loaded a mummy is. If anything, it keeps the storyteller from being swamped by the grand power two or three Mummies bring to the fore. It also helps the humanity arguement.<br /> <br /> The tools were there for an entirely Mummy driven game, but there needed to be more storyteller support and advice on what to do with that much power-in-varieties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T06:57:59-08:00","id":1272168,"title":"","content":"I never truly found even the later books to convincingly argue about why certain mummies were somehow stronger than others, or how they would maintain an organizational structure across such long periods of time with frequent absences, or how their cults could play a role in filling those gaps. I loved all the details given in Guildhalls, don't get me wrong, but in the end the game felt more about solitary monsters and their cults than anything else.<br /> <br /> I ended up houseruling a lot of things like making Memory always reset to 3 or lower at the beginning of every Descent, stats resetting to a fixed Character Creation point (while raising the starting XP amounts), and really just using mummies as NPC centerpieces for games non-mummy PCs to do their thing around or with. It worked out fairly well for my group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T07:34:57-08:00","id":1272176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1272168#post1272168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never truly found even the later books to convincingly argue about why certain mummies were somehow stronger than others, or how they would maintain an organizational structure across such long periods of time with frequent absences, or how their cults could play a role in filling those gaps. I loved all the details given in Guildhalls, don't get me wrong, but in the end the game felt more about solitary monsters and their cults than anything else.<br /> <br /> I ended up houseruling a lot of things like making Memory always reset to 3 or lower at the beginning of every Descent, stats resetting to a fixed Character Creation point (while raising the starting XP amounts), and really just using mummies as NPC centerpieces for games non-mummy PCs to do their thing around or with. It worked out fairly well for my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel like it was heavily implied that stats didn't reset between Descents for player characters, or that Memory shouldn't <i>just</i> drop back to 3 and require you to start over again once you got over the post-summoning Memory slump, but again, that's stuff could have been better clarified.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T08:04:15-08:00","id":1272180,"title":"","content":"The impression I get is that &quot;every Descent is a clean reset&quot; is deliberate change that they're implementing to deal with some logistical oddities of the mummy condition. That said, I think for that to work would also require a far more deliberately paced structure for the Descent, since one's chronicle still may have other immortals to account for, and backtracking xp mid-chronicle is unwieldy at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T08:20:16-08:00","id":1272183,"title":"","content":"If the Mummy is reset every Descent, but there are ways to &quot;store&quot; it for later retrieval, that seems to give both the &quot;fresh&quot; feeling of each Descent and still allow for power accumulation.<br /> <br /> Mummy weak this Descent? They just haven't found all their power stockpiles (whatever form they take). Want to play stronger? They find their secreted mojo more quickly this Descent. I think one of the 2E conversions even used something similar with &quot;Monuments&quot; (or whatever they were called).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 12-01-2018, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T09:18:42-08:00","id":1272189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1272176#post1272176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel like it was heavily implied that stats didn't reset between Descents for player characters, or that Memory shouldn't <i>just</i> drop back to 3 and require you to start over again once you got over the post-summoning Memory slump, but again, that's stuff could have been better clarified.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, it was not compulsory to start with Memory 3, since you could spend XP to start the game with more than that. As far as I know you lose 1 of Memory to each Descent. Even because in the first Descent all Mummy had Memory 1, it would not make sense for them to be trapped in 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15464-raphatheascended","name":"RaphaTheAscended","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T14:21:10-08:00","id":1272239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1272189#post1272189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, it was not compulsory to start with Memory 3, since you could spend XP to start the game with more than that. As far as I know you lose 1 of Memory to each Descent. Even because in the first Descent all Mummy had Memory 1, it would not make sense for them to be trapped in 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was the case, but at hte time of writing I didn't know for sure and just wanted to commit to the barge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T14:47:50-08:00","id":1272242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RaphaTheAscended</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1272189#post1272189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I know, it was not compulsory to start with Memory 3, since you could spend XP to start the game with more than that. As far as I know you lose 1 of Memory to each Descent. Even because in the first Descent all Mummy had Memory 1, it would not make sense for them to be trapped in 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition, the reason an Arisen typically started at Memory 3 was because that was the minimum you could drop to just from starting new Descents. To go lower you had to commit sins and generally prove yourself a devoted slave to your Judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-01T19:34:04-08:00","id":1272288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1272176#post1272176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I kind of feel like it was heavily implied that stats didn't reset between Descents for player characters, or that Memory shouldn't <i>just</i> drop back to 3 and require you to start over again once you got over the post-summoning Memory slump, but again, that's stuff could have been better clarified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I made that a house rule because it fit the narrative better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-02T16:25:52-08:00","id":1272480,"title":"","content":"In my own games I often played with flashback scenes by giving Skills and Merits (and Affinities and Utterances) to player characters that they had clearly forgotten in the intervening centuries, though Attributes remained somewhat constant. Mind you, these were usually short diversions from the main story, rather than playing a true multi-descent chronicle. I mean, every player character bar one (really) had multiple descents over the course of those campaigns, but they were usually being woken relatively shortly after their current descent ceased so that they could continue the campaign, with their Memories universally high enough to recall the immediately preceding events and thus their experience progression over that time.<br /> <br /> I didn't touch Pillars though. Pillars were low in past lives and grew until they hit the starting level for the campaign to begin. Because, barring Shuankhsen, I don't think &quot;forgetting&quot; fragments of your soul is terribly empowering as a concept.<br /> <br /> The little we know about Mummy 2E is that Arisen don't necessarily experience a linear progression of time, right? Assuming I'm not misremembering, that's an easy solution to the problem, such as it is. Your character's accumulation of experience can easily apply retrospectively to past descents because that's exactly how a consciousness skipping back and forth through history would work. Pretty elegant solution to that incongruity I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T13:52:17-08:00","id":1281365,"title":"","content":"Hey weirdos, the Style Guide for Chronicles stuff in the Storyteller's Vault talks about Mummy Second Edition.<br /> <br /> Links incoming, thoughts later coming.(Links like <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product_info.php?products_id=258968\" target=\"_blank\">this thing here.</a>)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-17-2019, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T14:02:12-08:00","id":1281367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1281365#post1281365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey weirdos, the Style Guide for Chronicles stuff in the Storyteller's Vault talks about Mummy Second Edition.<br /> <br /> Links incoming, thoughts later coming.(Links like <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product_info.php?products_id=258968\" target=\"_blank\">this thing here.</a>)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T14:02:53-08:00","id":1281368,"title":"","content":"Holy shit this is some creative refocusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T14:48:49-08:00","id":1281380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1281368#post1281368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit this is some creative refocusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! I look forward to seeing how this develops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T16:18:58-08:00","id":1281390,"title":"","content":"So the big changes are the Arisen's experience of non-linear time (already mentioned), the more explicit agenda of Arisen in reshaping mortal societies (I always felt that molding the mortals around them in their own image was a given for most Arisen, since you can raise the odds of having a mortal within your influence make a relic once every other century), and making it more of an open information game where player characters are able to know more or less the facts of Irem at the start? Oh, and changing Guilds from a social splat to more something internal. Cool, subtle changes that I like the sound of so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T19:03:35-08:00","id":1281424,"title":"","content":"I find the refocus on guilds to be interesting considering 1st edition where they were whole organizations (along with the fact that means, obviously, a lesser to no longer social splat)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T04:29:01-08:00","id":1281484,"title":"","content":"Between this, the upcoming Contagion Chronicles,etc I'm glad to see them sprinkling in ways to get us excited for the changes coming with Mummy 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T06:15:05-08:00","id":1281498,"title":"","content":"There's a bit more info about Mummy 2e in the interview DaveB and I did with Darker Days Radio at Dragonmeet, which has just been released:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://d2bwo9zemjwxh5.cloudfront.net/image-logo/286887/darkerdays_sq_1200x628.jpg?s=ef9d996b77a32657cc00ba35c6884454&amp;e=jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\"> #97: The Annual Dragonmeet Coffee Bar Special | Darker Days Radio </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://podcast.darker-days.org/e/96-the-annual-dragonmeet-coffee-bar-special/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chris was at Dragonmeet 2018, in London last December, a day after getting back from Boston, and he sat down with&nbsp;Onyx Path Publishing&nbsp;freelancers and developers&nbsp;David Brookshaw&nbsp;and&nbsp;Christopher Allen. They chat all about the releases coming up, plus some more exclusive information for&nbsp;Mummy: the Curse 2nd Edition&nbsp;and&nbsp;Deviant: the Renegades. &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Be sure to check us out on&nbsp;Facebook&nbsp;or through our Google Plus Community. To stay up to date,&nbsp;subscribe through iTunes!&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Links For This Episode:&nbsp;&nbsp; White Wolf Entertainment: http://www.white-wolf.com/ Occam's Laser Music: https://occamslaser.bandcamp.com/ Midnight Express Podcast: https://midnightexpress.podbean.com/ Mike's History Podcast on the Satanic Panic: http://historylessons.libsyn.com/161-the-satanic-panic Full Metal RPG Podcast: http://fullmetalrpg.com/ &nbsp; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","user":"Acrozatarim","date":".  Updating the link 01-18-2019, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T07:18:41-08:00","id":1281503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1281368#post1281368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Holy shit this is some creative refocusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy's 2nd Edition is, in general, so creatively focused it can cut through diamonds.<br /> <br /> I will not say more because Dixie and Matthew would send NDA ninja squads after me if I did, and I don't think I can defeat those. But seriously, there's lots to look forward in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 01-18-2019, 10:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T09:35:16-08:00","id":1281520,"title":"","content":"Something that occured to me as I listened to the interview: Mummies experiencing time non-linearly means there could be Arisen running about with experiences of future millenia, maybe reaching into billions of years. They could have witnessed space colonies or a dead post-apocalyptic world. On the other hand, if no such Mummies exist that fact alone is notable to Arisen Mystics. I wonder if the Corebook addresses that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T09:39:07-08:00","id":1281522,"title":"","content":"will it still just be focused on mummies being only grouped up with his cultists and no other mummies? just wondering","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T13:30:39-08:00","id":1281557,"title":"","content":"Question for the Devs:<br /> <br /> Given how nonlinear awakening events can be, would this be because that Arisen suffer from the problem that time in Duat flows not in a line, but a Jeremy Bearimy?<br /> <br /> (Take your bets: will the next post be a WTF or &quot;I understood that reference!&quot;?)<br /> <br /> More seriously, I get the sense that cults pretty much are mummy society here, which is...way better. I had actually always played the Guilds as being more populated by cultists than Arisen, and it was they who kept the tradition alive. Here, the Guilds are pretty much just organizing principles of cults, which makes a lot more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T17:53:13-08:00","id":1281594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1281557#post1281557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question for the Devs:<br /> <br /> Given how nonlinear awakening events can be, would this be because that Arisen suffer from the problem that time in Duat flows not in a line, but a Jeremy Bearimy?<br /> <br /> (Take your bets: will the next post be a WTF or &quot;I understood that reference!&quot;?)<br /> <br /> More seriously, I get the sense that cults pretty much are mummy society here, which is...way better. I had actually always played the Guilds as being more populated by cultists than Arisen, and it was they who kept the tradition alive. Here, the Guilds are pretty much just organizing principles of cults, which makes a lot more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, The Good Place puts up clips all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T10:03:28-08:00","id":1281655,"title":"","content":"The Guilds being a lot more internal to Mummies is good: they strained to make sense as <i>somehow</i> being dynamic, living mummy society. Ohhh, all the timey-wobbly stuff though... their body only going one way but their mind when they awaken passing through whatever points back and forth in the river of time? Remembering things that from their perspective haven't happened yet? Their memory is going to be even more shot. Exciting to theorize on the possibilities. It certainly reinforces the notion of the Rite of Return <i>breaking time</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T12:09:33-08:00","id":1281669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1281655#post1281655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guilds being a lot more internal to Mummies is good: they strained to make sense as <i>somehow</i> being dynamic, living mummy society. Ohhh, all the timey-wobbly stuff though... their body only going one way but their mind when they awaken passing through whatever points back and forth in the river of time? Remembering things that from their perspective haven't happened yet? Their memory is going to be even more shot. Exciting to theorize on the possibilities. It certainly reinforces the notion of the Rite of Return <i>breaking time</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually enjoyed the inevitable structure it developed, but this is definitely easier for people to handle it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T03:37:34-07:00","id":1300790,"title":"","content":"I could be wrong (I likely am) but since the first Contagion Chronicle preview involves Mummy's it might have given a hint towards some more details from 2E.<br /> <br /> For example it mentions that shortly after a Mummy awoke the majority of people in the immediate area were &quot;subdued in a feast of mortal memory&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that this is new take on Sybaris type effects that accompany an Arisen waking up. Alternatively, maybe Mummy's can &quot;eat&quot; mortal memory to &quot;reinforce&quot; their own, though I imagine this plays hell with their sense of identity. <br /> <br /> The preview also mentions the Mummy being summoned from his &quot;Ashen Kingdom beyond Twilight&quot; making me wonder if Mummy's in henet are each in their own &quot;version&quot; of Duat. Basically following the idea that while Duat is its own realm, the Rite of Return sectioned of thin slices of it to be &quot;containers&quot; for each Arisen. Meaning that every Mummy's Duat is different and tailored to them. Meaning that they might have a really good (God in Dreams) or really bad (personal hell) sorta time while there. <br /> <br /> Once again, this is all speculation, but its some hints (maybe) of what we might see in 2E Mummy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T07:02:05-07:00","id":1300826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1300790#post1300790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could be wrong (I likely am) but since the first Contagion Chronicle preview involves Mummy's it might have given a hint towards some more details from 2E.<br /> <br /> For example it mentions that shortly after a Mummy awoke the majority of people in the immediate area were &amp;quot;subdued in a feast of mortal memory&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that this is new take on Sybaris type effects that accompany an Arisen waking up. Alternatively, maybe Mummy's can &amp;quot;eat&amp;quot; mortal memory to &amp;quot;reinforce&amp;quot; their own, though I imagine this plays hell with their sense of identity. <br /> <br /> The preview also mentions the Mummy being summoned from his &amp;quot;Ashen Kingdom beyond Twilight&amp;quot; making me wonder if Mummy's in henet are each in their own &amp;quot;version&amp;quot; of Duat. Basically following the idea that while Duat is its own realm, the Rite of Return sectioned of thin slices of it to be &amp;quot;containers&amp;quot; for each Arisen. Meaning that every Mummy's Duat is different and tailored to them. Meaning that they might have a really good (God in Dreams) or really bad (personal hell) sorta time while there. <br /> <br /> Once again, this is all speculation, but its some hints (maybe) of what we might see in 2E Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the preview I think that the memory eating is probably a unique trait of that mummy as I feel gaining a memory every round would be pretty overpowered in the hands of a PC. <br /> <br /> On the other hand the way the &quot;Ashen Kingdom&quot; is talked about seems to suggest is something more common for Mummy's to be able to do which is certainly an interesting development, it's worth pointing though the 3 other Mummy's mentioned sounds a lot more in line with current 1e Mummy's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:06:47-07:00","id":1300844,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind this mummy is not from our reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:40:17-07:00","id":1300851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1300844#post1300844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Bear in mind this mummy is not from our reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh awesome, I was literally hoping I could ask you this question since I read the preview <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I think I got a bit confused because I thought the &quot;other dimension&quot; was referring to Duat or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T08:52:27-07:00","id":1300854,"title":"","content":"No no, Contagion has worn a fissure between our world and another one. This mummy stepped through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T10:31:19-07:00","id":1300877,"title":"","content":"oh shit. I thought this Contagion just infected the reality, not break it and allow others in.<br /> <br /> also, so mummies (I mean players) can choose a judge for them to represent, interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"ht