Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T18:44:34-07:00","id":1302410,"title":"","content":"Do we know enough for there to be any differences? The 'changes' I've heard of so far are more akin to clarifications unless I am forgetting something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T10:46:46-07:00","id":1305763,"title":"","content":"Preview vid from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=X9lbz4TWY9s\" data-code=\"X9lbz4TWY9s\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/X9lbz4TWY9s/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T13:41:44-07:00","id":1305801,"title":"","content":"Alright, so, here we go with a bit of a summary of the video regarding all the juicy bits.<ul><li>For accessibility of character concepts, the <b>Guilds</b> are going to have nicknames that immediately gives an idea of what they're about. Examples given include &quot;Spies, Secret Police&quot; for the Maa-Kep and &quot;New Pharaohs&quot; for Tef-Aabhi in addition to the standard nickname of &quot;Masons&quot;.</li> <li>While in <b>henet</b>, the Arisen wander the <b>Duat</b>, facing all kinds of torment, only to be judged by their Judge, and if the Judge finds them wanting, they are sent back to their khat/sahu (their physical body) at an &quot;appropriate time&quot;. Appropriate times include, but are not limited to, Sothic Turns, being summoned by your cult, and &quot;great acts of necromancy, even if there is no necromancer or sorcerer behind them&quot;. The Reign of Terror Dark Era is called out as an example.<ul><li>I will note that this gives them interesting overlap with the Bound (IE. Sin-Eaters), who experience population spikes in tumultuous times where there's a lot of death, and often a lot of diverse deaths.</li> </ul></li> <li>Your character has starting levels of experience. This makes little sense if you're an (admittedly forgetful) immortal who first awoke in Egypt's Third Dynasty during the reign of Unas and have experienced a couple years of activity (more or less) on or off at regular or irregular intervals for the next several thousand years. Instead, accept this premise. <b>That your first in-play Descent is your <i>very first </i>Descent. Ever.</b> Since the Judges are godlike cosmic beings and Duat doesn't really experience linear time, your next Descent could be, well, anywhere and any<i>when </i>as well. If Memory still retains suggested recollections like &quot;your last Descent&quot; and such, your &quot;last Descent&quot; could be in the distant past, the future, at any point in time really. The Arisen could be recollecting future events if they wake in what is (to us) the past.<ul><li>This also makes raising Memory very peculiar and allows some &quot;permissiveness for metaknowledge&quot;. An example given is your Mummy raiding with a group of Vikings and, all of a sudden, remembering how to drive a car. Or use a computer. Or speak a language that might not exist yet.</li> </ul></li> <li>Antagonists are great. <b>Tiered Cultists</b> are kind of, sort of, explained. You can build up your <b>Pillars</b> and invest them in your Cultists, and it sounds like they're referring to the dot rating. It's described as being &quot;like a lich's phylactery&quot;. If it is referring to dot rating, it would explain why the Tiers only go up to 4. At the highest levels, you can keep a dot for yourself, and still invest in a Sadikh. Also, <b>potentially all the Immortals from World of Darkness: Immortals will make it into this book</b>. <b>Blood Bathers and Eternals are specifically called out. </b>Can be playable Cultists, or NPC antagonists that build up their own cults.</li> <li><b>Judges </b>are NPC Antagonists you can encounter in play. Inspirations for the Judges-as-manifested-characters include D&amp;D, Planescape: The Torment, Lovecraft, and the idigam of Werewolf: The Forsaken. Apparently... there is some kind of <b>connection between the Judges and the Idigam</b>.</li> </ul>So some of this was already known. Some of the things we already know are given a little extra detail. In particular... anyone want to join in me in kind-of-sort-of freaking out about the second half of the last point?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 04-18-2019, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:02:43-07:00","id":1305821,"title":"","content":"Do you know what's really interesting? When you watch a video about a game you are writing for and it gets you super pumped up. Very, very cool feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T15:28:03-07:00","id":1305829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305821#post1305821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know what's really interesting? When you watch a video about a game you are writing for and it gets you super pumped up. Very, very cool feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Despite knowing the information already, it was still just as exciting listening to this preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-18T17:02:32-07:00","id":1305851,"title":"","content":"idigram and judges huh? I'll admit I did not see that coming. in hindsight, judges are actually nameless just as the idigram are conceptless. perhaps judges are a sort of complete idigram (obviously an extreme bare bones theory)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T03:11:16-07:00","id":1305947,"title":"","content":"Can someone give me the boilerplate on the Idigam in Second Edition Foresaken?<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with the take on them in 1E WtF as these kinda quasi-spirits without anything to actually be the spirit of. Breaking the usual animistic nature of spirits. If I remember correctly they were sealed on the Moon by Luna because in a defined world like our own they would cause chaos. Also it was implied they were her &quot;first children&quot; before she hooked up with Father Wolf right?<br /> <br /> I'm curious how they got altered in 2E WtF, since the 1E editions I'm kinda-sorta familiar with seem like a hard thing to link back to the Judges without jumping some major mental hoops. The only thing that I can see they have in common is being ancient and alien (but mostly understandable in intention). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T05:52:25-07:00","id":1305975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305947#post1305947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone give me the boilerplate on the Idigam in Second Edition Foresaken?<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with the take on them in 1E WtF as these kinda quasi-spirits without anything to actually be the spirit of. Breaking the usual animistic nature of spirits. If I remember correctly they were sealed on the Moon by Luna because in a defined world like our own they would cause chaos. Also it was implied they were her &quot;first children&quot; before she hooked up with Father Wolf right?<br /> <br /> I'm curious how they got altered in 2E WtF, since the 1E editions I'm kinda-sorta familiar with seem like a hard thing to link back to the Judges without jumping some major mental hoops. The only thing that I can see they have in common is being ancient and alien (but mostly understandable in intention).</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the change they made was to make the idigam's origins ambiguous; there are a number of theories about what they are, but none with strong evidence.<br /> <br /> Also, not all of the idigam were imprisoned on the moon; some remained on Earth, eventually sinking into slumber. They run by the same rules as their Moon-Banished kin..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T06:45:15-07:00","id":1305983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305975#post1305975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, not all of the idigam were imprisoned on the moon; some remained on Earth, eventually sinking into slumber. They run by the same rules as their Moon-Banished kin..</div> </div> </div> </div>A notable exception: The bans and banes of every Earthbound idigam \u2014 even the ones who haven't Coalesced and therefore have a different ban and bane every scene \u2014 always have something to do with humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T06:53:52-07:00","id":1305985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305801#post1305801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST][*]Your character has starting levels of experience. This makes little sense if you're an (admittedly forgetful) immortal who first awoke in Egypt's Third Dynasty during the reign of Unas and have experienced a couple years of activity (more or less) on or off at regular or irregular intervals for the next several thousand years. Instead, accept this premise. <b>That your first in-play Descent is your <i>very first </i>Descent. Ever.</b> Since the Judges are godlike cosmic beings and Duat doesn't really experience linear time, your next Descent could be, well, anywhere and any<i>when </i>as well. If Memory still retains suggested recollections like &amp;quot;your last Descent&amp;quot; and such, your &amp;quot;last Descent&amp;quot; could be in the distant past, the future, at any point in time really. The Arisen could be recollecting future events if they wake in what is (to us) the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ultimate prophecy power. Saying things that things will be like this because I have seen it took a note of being literal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T07:13:42-07:00","id":1305987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305821#post1305821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know what's really interesting? When you watch a video about a game you are writing for and it gets you super pumped up. Very, very cool feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was weird but I felt exactly the same. It's a mixture of excitement, pride and eager anticipation. Looking forward the day people get to see what we're working on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T07:30:31-07:00","id":1305993,"title":"","content":"Open question to the Mummy the Curse 2e team: If it does not break Non-disclosure agreements, would you be able to tell us fans what the Anchors for Mummy 2e will be called? Will Mummies have Virtues and Vices like mortals, hunters, mages and demons (which admittedly would make an intriguing parallel of power with the least powerful - mortals and hunters - sharing anchors with arguably the most powerful - mummies) or will there be a new set of anchors for the Arisen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T10:03:31-07:00","id":1306031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305993#post1305993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open question to the Mummy the Curse 2e team: If it does not break Non-disclosure agreements, would you be able to tell us fans what the Anchors for Mummy 2e will be called? Will Mummies have Virtues and Vices like mortals, hunters, mages and demons (which admittedly would make an intriguing parallel of power with the least powerful - mortals and hunters - sharing anchors with arguably the most powerful - mummies) or will there be a new set of anchors for the Arisen?</div> </div> </div> </div>As of first drafts, the Anchors are [REDACTED]. Nope, the NDA ninjas are still on guard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T11:26:34-07:00","id":1306052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1305993#post1305993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Open question to the Mummy the Curse 2e team: If it does not break Non-disclosure agreements, would you be able to tell us fans what the Anchors for Mummy 2e will be called? Will Mummies have Virtues and Vices like mortals, hunters, mages and demons (which admittedly would make an intriguing parallel of power with the least powerful - mortals and hunters - sharing anchors with arguably the most powerful - mummies) or will there be a new set of anchors for the Arisen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, FWIW, the Mummy antagonist used in the KS draft for Contagion Chronicle does list Virtue/Vice...but it also has a big disclaimer at the top claiming that the stat arrangement might change as Mummy 2e gets closer to final drafts. So take care.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T11:29:43-07:00","id":1306053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's too derivative.</div> </div> </div> </div>dude, I literally stated it was a bare bones theory. it's not even one I would ever truly consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T12:56:05-07:00","id":1306071,"title":"","content":"As someone who backed the first ed kickstarter but was heavily dissapointed in the result this all spunds very interesting. I like the non linear time from a world perspective and yet growth from a characters personal perspective. The fact that the first return cpyld be 2000 AD, the second 34 AD, the third 10,213 AD is brilliant! <br /> <br /> So does this mean the power stat goes 1 to 10, like tradition, rather then 10 to 1, if so that's awesome. <br /> <br /> I also like memory being a bit more useful, especially in how modern knowledge could be used in the ancient past or future knowledge in the present. <br /> <br /> I hope thereis little limitation in working with others as groups sound cool. <br /> <br /> But yeah this sounds fun, and a nice change to certain elements of 1e that were less than spectacular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T13:01:04-07:00","id":1306073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306071#post1306071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does this mean the power stat goes 1 to 10, like tradition, rather then 10 to 1, if so that's awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They already confirmed that Sekhem will still decrease over time, and going as far as saying that that's part of what makes Mummy unique among the other CofD gamelines. Therefore, no reason to change it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T13:03:26-07:00","id":1306074,"title":"","content":"You really could not have Mummy without the Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T13:03:36-07:00","id":1306075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306073#post1306073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. They already confirmed that Sekhem will still decrease over time, and going as far as saying that that's part of what makes Mummy unique among the other CofD gamelines. Therefore, no reason to change it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's sad and unfortunate. That said thanks for the heads up before I got to excited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306074#post1306074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really could not have Mummy without the Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I obviously super heavily disagree. Mummy is about immortality and tge weight of ages. It doesnt have to be about starting a life super powered then fading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 04-19-2019, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T13:13:38-07:00","id":1306077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306075#post1306075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I obviously super heavily disagree. Mummy is about immortality and tge weight of ages. It doesnt have to be about starting a life super powered then fading.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time keeps on slipping, slipping, slipping- into the future.<br /> <br /> But no, Seriously, the Descent is a drastically different play mechanic from pretty much anything else out there on the market and sets the tension, tone and play style of Mummy perfectly. It's a thrilling mechanic that works perfectly with the themes and mood of the game, and taking it out of Curse would be like trying to gut the Pilgramage from Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T15:09:26-07:00","id":1306092,"title":"","content":"Personally I kinda dislike the idea of non-linear time. <br /> <br /> Has there been any revelation about Memory itself? Is it still tied to morality? That last part was my only dissappointment in 1st edition. And morality as power stat was aggravating in Mummy the Resurrection aswell.<br /> <br /> So if Memory is untangled from morality I\u2019m more than happy. Non-linear time I can House-rule if I wish or I might like it after reading the 2nd edition, who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T15:17:29-07:00","id":1306093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't call it too derivative because it was bare boned.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok, whatever dude. not getting into this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T19:59:45-07:00","id":1306150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306031#post1306031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As of first drafts, the Anchors are [REDACTED]. Nope, the NDA ninjas are still on guard.</div> </div> </div> </div>lol that's what I thought would be the case, but I figured I'd give it a go and ask just in case. Power to you folks on the Mummy the Curse 2nd edition team!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T20:11:39-07:00","id":1306154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306092#post1306092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I kinda dislike the idea of non-linear time.<br /> <br /> Has there been any revelation about Memory itself? Is it still tied to morality? That last part was my only dissappointment in 1st edition. And morality as power stat was aggravating in Mummy the Resurrection aswell.<br /> <br /> So if Memory is untangled from morality I\u2019m more than happy. Non-linear time I can House-rule if I wish or I might like it after reading the 2nd edition, who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, the other 2e Integrity stats don't often resemble Morality anyway. It is a lot more fluid that way. I expect 'sins' against memory would more closely resemble Clarity (changeling triggers) or Loyalty (from Deviant) to the Judge. The later would likely go hand in hand with a Descent reset. If that is still thematically appropriate.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T21:58:01-07:00","id":1306171,"title":"","content":"To be fair, once we CAN talk about Mummy, I'm pretty sure it will be impossible to shut us up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:27:18-07:00","id":1306176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306171#post1306171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, once we CAN talk about Mummy, I'm pretty sure it will be impossible to shut us up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that will be like the moment Pandora opened her box, I feel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T22:43:35-07:00","id":1306180,"title":"","content":"We know from the Style Guide that Mummy 2E focuses more on the Arisen as artists and craftspeople; my guess is that cults are as much about leaving legacies before you go through the Jeremy Bearimy of Duat again, and Memory often involves discovering what you have made with your own hands - or making it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-19T23:33:14-07:00","id":1306187,"title":"","content":"I do hope Apotheosis will still be an option for players that wish to do so At the same time I am excited to see how non-linear time will play out in game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Also - lesser immortals in Mummy cults!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-20T14:31:41-07:00","id":1306338,"title":"","content":"To me the Descent is a clear attempt to tie the game into the notion made popular in Mummy horror that the corpse is tied to its tomb and the need to rest and can only be active in the world so long before returning to a dead slumber. <br /> <br /> As for Memory, I kind of liked it being tied to Morality. Its like- the more you remember about what it was like to be alive the more you remember what you considered to be right and wrong as a mortal and what will betray those ancient sensibilities. In contrast, acting immorally or like an unfeeling monster puts you out of touch with who you used to be and places your further away from the familiar that helps drawn out those ancient memories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-21T03:33:09-07:00","id":1306494,"title":"","content":"But the problem with tying memory to morality is that not all people, immortal or mortal, are necessarily that moral and why should such immoral people have worse memories or be less in touch to their memories due to their own nature. <br /> <br /> It is just plain wrong that bad people have weaker memories. Memory and morality are not one and the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T01:55:34-07:00","id":1306782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306494#post1306494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the problem with tying memory to morality is that not all people, immortal or mortal, are necessarily that moral and why should such immoral people have worse memories or be less in touch to their memories due to their own nature.<br /> <br /> It is just plain wrong that bad people have weaker memories. Memory and morality are not one and the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> That is not how the Memory stay is intended to be interpreted.<br /> <br /> It is not that bad people have weak memories. It is the Judge's Will that overwrites the consciousness of the Arisen. Memory is the assertion of Self and ones values over the Curse.<br /> It is not that weak memories are a sign of moral failing. It is just you can't be a good magic robot/slave if you have memories.<br /> Low Memory is not a sign that you are a bad person; it is a sign that you are apathetic to things not related to your mission.<br /> <br /> Bad people don't have weak memories; it is that you can't be good without them.<br /> You must know of consequences, know what can, has and will be done.<br /> Otherwise it is not a choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T03:10:21-07:00","id":1306788,"title":"","content":"@FallenEco<br /> <br /> I know that is not the intention but it is what it effectively becomes if Memory and Morality traits are tied together as they were in 1st edition. If you act immorally, even if that were true to your nature and would be an assertion of self over the judges will and mission, you will loose, or just not gain, any memory. Ergo it becomes that bad people have harder time to remember because acting true to themselves actually weakens memory stat as that is tied to morality instead of strenghthening it.<br /> <br /> Remember that in 1st edition there were specific sins against Memory (MtC p.77) but in that table it is said that those are in addition to the 1st edition WoD\u2019s sins against morality (1st ed WoD p.91).<br /> <br /> To remind you those sins are as follows:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>World of Darkness 1st edition page 91</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morality Sin<br /> 10 Selfish thoughts. (Roll five dice.) 9 Minor selfish act (withholding<br /> charity). (Roll five dice.)<br /> 8 Injury to another (accidental or otherwise). (Roll four dice.) <br /> 7. Petty theft (shoplifting). (Roll four dice.)<br /> 6. Grand theft (burglary). (Roll three dice.)<br /> 5 Intentional, mass property damage (arson). (Roll three dice.)<br /> 4 Impassioned crime (manslaughter). (Roll three dice.)<br /> 3 Planned crime (murder). (Roll two dice.)<br /> 2 Casual/callous crime (serial murder). (Roll two dice.)<br /> 1 Utter perversion, heinous act (mass murder). (Roll two dice.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So as you can see thievery and for example injury to another, even accidentally, weakens your Memory in 1st edition. And at highest levels of Memory even an selfish thought may take a piece of your Memory away. So a bad or selfish person cannot have a good memory score and I would love for that connection to be removed in 2nd edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T03:39:34-07:00","id":1306790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306782#post1306782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No.<br /> That is not how the Memory stay is intended to be interpreted.<br /> <br /> It is not that bad people have weak memories. It is the Judge's Will that overwrites the consciousness of the Arisen. Memory is the assertion of Self and ones values over the Curse.<br /> It is not that weak memories are a sign of moral failing. It is just you can't be a good magic robot/slave if you have memories.<br /> Low Memory is not a sign that you are a bad person; it is a sign that you are apathetic to things not related to your mission.<br /> <br /> Bad people don't have weak memories; it is that you can't be good without them.<br /> You must know of consequences, know what can, has and will be done.<br /> Otherwise it is not a choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah the good old Memory vs Morality and how they should be integrated debate. <br /> <br /> Personally, I hope Memory gets an overhaul on at least the same level that Humanity and Clarity got in the 2E of thier respective games. Really, at this point in 2E lifespan I think there is an expectation by the fanbase that the &quot;ethics stat&quot; of each splat gets a massive revision as of 2E. I'd honestly be disappointed if they kept more then the smallest fraction of an old 1E Morality style system in place for it. <br /> <br /> Mind you, that's just my viewpoint, and it should be taken with a hefty dose of salt. I am the guy that back when Mummy 1E had just came out had arguments with at least one Mummy writer about the fact that Morality and Memory really should not be linked.<br /> <br /> It's one of those memories (ha!) that kinda make me wary of Mummy 2E. Memory is also one of the three (Utterances and the Deceived being the others) things that if I don't like the look of during the previews I won't be touching 2E Mummy at all. I'll give it all the benefit of the doubt until the inevitable manuscript reveal during the likely Kickstarter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T03:45:17-07:00","id":1306791,"title":"","content":"We. Don't. Have. Morality. In. Second. Edition.<br /> We have Integrity, which is a lot more flexible AND lacks a hierarchy of sins.<br /> <br /> It is not the same issue to say that Memory is like Integrity, as it is to compare it to first edition's Morality trait. Integrity more closely resembles the Code from HtV. I don't think Memory is going to go backwards rather tailor itself to the game.<br /> <br /> I'm trying not to dismiss your concerns. It is valid. I just think Chronicles already addressed it and see no reason why they would undo that change. It is not like Vampire, Humanity as a trait has to be very rigid. Memory, like Clarity and Wisdom is much less so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 04-23-2019, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T10:07:07-07:00","id":1306884,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting at this point that we have....Humanity, Harmony, Wisdom, Pilgramage, Clarity, Synergy, The Code, Cover, Satiety, and a little bit of Stability? All as 2E Integrity Slots? As well as Integrity Itself? And they are all radically different from each other, with most being pretty different from Integrity, all to end aim of better supporting the themes and struggles of the games they're in? And none of them really look like Morality?<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, it's starting to sound like someone either hasn't read 2E materials or hasn't developed (or isn't willing to employ) an ability to read trends and project forward with them.<br /> <br /> Cause yeah, this problem isn't one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:23:38-07:00","id":1306958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306884#post1306884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just saying, it's starting to sound like someone either hasn't read 2E materials or hasn't developed (or isn't willing to employ) an ability to read trends and project forward with them.<br /> <br /> Cause yeah, this problem isn't one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I am much more familiar with 2nd edition systems/material than 1st edition which I didn\u2019t particularly care for, except CtL and MtC both of which I used in OWoD instead of in nWoD. I much prefer Chronicles of Darkness, that is 2nd edition, material which I actually like quite a bit.<br /> <br /> The thing with Mummy and Memory/Morality is that if my memory serves me correctly it\u2019s original developer did defend the connection between Memory and Morality in the discussions about it on these forums, hence my worry. Of course I have no idea how much or little he has a hand in 2nd edition or how much will the team of 2nd edition hang on to his vision.<br /> <br /> Yes the trend of 2nd editions in general is promising, I love that each supernatural has it\u2019s own trait for this in their own flavour, but there is always an exception to every rule and I hope Mummy will not be that exception.<br /> <br /> Especially since Resurrection went towards this morality thing even though none of the earlier editions of Mummy were not about such themes and then Curse followed suite eventhough it was a completely different game even if of a similar subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:27:12-07:00","id":1306959,"title":"","content":"the original dev is not on the team, that I think is pretty sure anyway","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:39:47-07:00","id":1306965,"title":"","content":"Yeah, CAS isn't involved with 2E at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T13:46:42-07:00","id":1306968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306958#post1306958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing with Mummy and Memory/Morality is that if my memory serves me correctly</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> it\u2019s original developer did defend the connection between Memory and Morality in the discussions about it on these forums </div> </div> </div>One of the writers responded to the question of why Memory couldn't work more like Integrity with the fact that the way Memory worked in general made &quot;answer these questions about your character's background as it informs their personal stress-fractures&quot; an incoherent baseline to build from, and another one of the writers pointed out that Memory is antithetical to what the Judges made the Arisen for and is directly imperiled by a lot of the stuff they expect of them. The gameline itself made something of a point out of the fact that retaining stolen Sekhem and actively caring for other people are at odds with each other.<br /> <br /> That doesn't really paint a strong picture of Mummy 2e being fodder for the old ridiculous arguments about whether regular grand larceny should imply a lower rating than aggravated assault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:20:02-07:00","id":1306978,"title":"","content":"It wasn\u2019t CAS. It was Malcolm, who wrote on almost every book for 1e Mummy. Or at least I\u2019ve heard him opine that Memory is about reclaiming your lost identity, and human morality is indivisible from that.<br /> <br /> Mal is also not writing on 2e, FWIW. IIRC no one who wrote the 1e core is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-22T14:30:13-07:00","id":1306981,"title":"","content":"Does he still do writing for OP in general? I've always liked his ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T08:20:17-07:00","id":1307223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1306978#post1306978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn\u2019t CAS. It was Malcolm, who wrote on almost every book for 1e Mummy. Or at least I\u2019ve heard him opine that Memory is about reclaiming your lost identity, and human morality is indivisible from that.<br /> <br /> Mal is also not writing on 2e, FWIW. IIRC no one who wrote the 1e core is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's honestly pretty worrying. Malcolm's mythcrafting in Mummy 1e - especially Dreams of Avarice - was amazing.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:20:23-07:00","id":1307356,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mummy 1E is still my favourite Chronicles game (heck, my favourite RPG period) by a solid leap and a bound, so I can't say that the second edition involving an entirely new cast of writers is terribly inspiring. Chronicles writers are generally on the ball, and all the tidbits about the new edition range from fine to genuinely cool, but they're still not the original creators of my favourite game.<br /> <br /> It's a reasonably small thing though. Artists muck up sequels to their crowning achievements all the time. Others take on the work of their predecessors and redefine it in ways that make it even better than it was before. The second edition team literally has the first edition as their launch pad. There's every expectation that they'll turn out something pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Now back to tempering my expectations so I don't end up <i>too</i> badly disappointed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:23:54-07:00","id":1307358,"title":"","content":"I learned to stop expecting things a long time ago!<br /> <br /> And Kingdom Hearts 3 still hurt me!<br /> <br /> (But jokes asides, working to set aside pre-conceptions is a good way to avoid unnecessary disappointments.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-23T18:58:37-07:00","id":1307371,"title":"","content":"The Wachowskis are a gift for learning to temper expectations. I'm pretty sure their creative process is bound into some kind of perverse good-bad cycle. It's like every time they knock one out of the park they need to follow it up with something terrible.<br /> <br /> Edit: Come to think of it, Cloud Atlas is one heck of an example of non-linear storytelling, and may be responsible in part for why I find the idea of Mummies experiencing time in a non-linear fashion so interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T06:19:25-07:00","id":1307449,"title":"","content":"Have any of the 2e books been developed by the same person who developed the first edition? I can't think of any off the top of my head, but I believe pretty much all of the 2e books are considered better than their first incarnations. I have every hope the same will happen with Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T07:48:40-07:00","id":1307473,"title":"","content":"While I do love the idea of mummies unstuck in linear time (I used that concept even before the sothic turn book made it explicitly possible), I have misgivings about the &quot;starter level experience&quot; thing. I know the Descent isn't gone, but part of mummy's draw was starting off overpowered like endgame. Granted, mummy had very clear character progression (pillars, new utterances, new affinities, talismans, merits) so is this really that different? Is our first Descent going to be as &quot;weak as a starting vampire? Is Sekhem being redesigned so that it still makes a freshly arisen mummy insanely overpowered, but gives more satisfactory character progression while preserving the &quot;you're growing old, fading, losing the power you once had&quot; aspect of Mummy. I've played very heavily into the whole angle for all of 1e. <br /> <br /> Also, does that suggest we play out non linear time in order, like our memory grows and gameplay progresses OOC linearly even if it isn't IC? That could be cool but may muck with some things in my game group because mummy cults are a big part while mummies are just a minority of actual characters, and I don't want to rely on the Contagion to explain while the mummy characters don't line up with the rest of the gaming group. Would I just have to hardware exactly how powerful a mummy is at any given moment because they had a flashback? <br /> <br /> I still trust the writers, though. As I said before, having spiralled and theorized with many of them during the first kickstarter and the forums, I bet it will end up great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T07:56:12-07:00","id":1307475,"title":"","content":"Nope, At the start of Decent your still as OP as hell, you just have less of a EX investment. I bet you will still get Utterances at the start, even if its the first time you woke up.<br /> <br /> an idea just popped up though, being unbound by time gives some interesting implications, like the Heretic being aware of the Dreams before he wrote it, or unless him writing the Dreams was a big event that stretched throughout time or something","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T08:51:09-07:00","id":1307490,"title":"","content":"yup, nothing was said against the starting power level. this aspect is stated to be staying in 2nd edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T09:39:51-07:00","id":1307503,"title":"","content":"I'm firmly of the opinion that we went for the best team for Mummy. Everyone on the book is a fan of the game, importantly they've read the books from first edition, they've contributed some amazingly creative ideas, and not one person was late turning in their work.<br /> <br /> I'm confident you'll enjoy second edition even more than first edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-24T10:18:46-07:00","id":1307517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1307503#post1307503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm firmly of the opinion that we went for the best team for Mummy. Everyone on the book is a fan of the game, importantly they've read the books from first edition, they've contributed some amazingly creative ideas, and not one person was late turning in their work.<br /> <br /> I'm confident you'll enjoy second edition even more than first edition <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, Matthew. I am proud to be a member of this team, and to hear it called the best for the project makes my day. I eagerly await the day this book makes it into everyone\u2019s hands, so they may see what we\u2019ve done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T09:27:09-07:00","id":1307776,"title":"","content":"I am really looking forward to this, even if I have to fiddle with things to get it to work with a crossover group. I remember the amazing discussions we had in open development of 1e, and I know that the writers and I and other fans had discussions that didn't make it into 1e but could in 2e.<br /> <br /> Also, ironically, in 1e in the beginning, my only mummy related pc wad a sekhem sorcerer. We played him as the normal reincarnation of the first sorcerer that my npc mummy had as high priest. Then, guildhalls said at least the Scribes ban and kill arkham sorcerers, so I had to retcon a lot and the player had a hard time adapting. I am REALLY glad that Cult tiers have let me undo this retcon and go back to my original story.<br /> <br /> Do the tiers build on each other? Like.. one day you are a sorcerer, then with time a full blown immortal? Probably not something you guys can answer, but I hope it's part of it. <br /> <br /> As long as potential crossover is addressed in the material (or at least Contagion Chronicle) I'll be happy. The rest I can tinker with. <br /> <br /> Regardless, imma back it if I'm not broke at the time. So far, not a single 2e has disappointed, and my two favorite CofD games were changeling and Mummy. And old forum pals and fellow speculators are writing for both (oh Sean, please go back to writing changeling material, pretty please, you are my favorite). <br /> <br /> One thing I love though, it sounds like the difference between Arisen and Deceived experiences during a death cycle is blurred a bit. While deceived may still be running from a temakh and arisen running towards their Judge, I like that both experience this, just with differences of opinion. <br /> <br /> If a mummy is still a theoretically designed OP monster from the start and slowly loses power, even if there is clear pc progression and memory complications, I'm still down for it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm hoping that the non linear playstyle implies memory is counterbalanced by prophecy, that almost every mummy you meet may know of the future. That would really hit home their connection to fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-25T15:32:18-07:00","id":1307864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1307449#post1307449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have any of the 2e books been developed by the same person who developed the first edition? I can't think of any off the top of my head, but I believe pretty much all of the 2e books are considered better than their first incarnations. I have every hope the same will happen with Mummy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, not! Last time I spoke to Malcolm (who is now very busy at Green Ronin: they just announced the setting for the gameline he's Developer of) he was of the same opinion as me; Mummy was something we greatly enjoyed working on, and have no desire to work on again. It'd be <i>weird</i>.<br /> <br /> Personally, the changes Matthew and his team have teased to the gameline sound brilliant, and I hope the game becomes as popular as it deserves to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T05:09:14-07:00","id":1308281,"title":"","content":"While I like the idea of Mummies being unstuck in time, the idea of the current Descent being the player's first Descent is immensely disappointing to me. I loved the idea of Mummies being these ancient beings with huge, sprawling, half-remembered histories that shaped them into who they are, I thought that was a fantastic niche that nothing else really filled, and I loved coming up with and playing a character like that. The first Descent being the 'now' Descent takes away from that, making it seem like the Mummies are less ancient and enduring, more hapless stooges that got suddenly dropped into a world they don't understand. Contrary to this allowing an excuse for metaknowledge, I think it discourages it if a Mummy wakes up in 2019 and has no idea what a car is or, indeed, even a horse is or how to work one. To me, this was kind of the core of Mummy's appeal - this sense of age, like everything has been done before and will be done again, of being so used to everything, being so bored of humanity and their temporary little creations even as you try to hold on to it, or even get it back in Akenakhi's case. Making that into prophecy of what is yet to come utterly changes the dynamic of Mummy in, I think, a less interesting way.<br /> I never felt like there was any issue with starting experience not making sense. It's generally assumed that you've earned experience to get to the starting point, after all - that's why Werewolves start at 7 Harmony and not 10 like it says new-changes are. It just represents more time here. Likewise, I felt like not quite having all of Arisen cosmology down the first time you play makes sense and works with the idea of poor memory.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also concerned with the idea of Judges being statted beings that show up in-game. I liked it best when I could only splutter uselessly at my Judge and have no actual chance at hurting them in any meaningful way. Facing the inevitable seemed like a core theme of 1e Mummy, and making Judges something you can overcome, no matter how difficult, I think takes away from that. That and the Gentleman Gamer mentioning that serving your Judge can increase your Memory. I don't like that at all.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely sorry to say it, but I've come out of this teaser a lot less enthused about Mummy than I was going in. I'm still excited about what it ends up being, but now I'm considering it may well just not be something I enjoy as much as first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T05:32:59-07:00","id":1308284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308281#post1308281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like the idea of Mummies being unstuck in time, the idea of the current Descent being the player's first Descent is immensely disappointing to me. I loved the idea of Mummies being these ancient beings with huge, sprawling, half-remembered histories that shaped them into who they are, I thought that was a fantastic niche that nothing else really filled, and I loved coming up with and playing a character like that. The first Descent being the 'now' Descent takes away from that, making it seem like the Mummies are less ancient and enduring, more hapless stooges that got suddenly dropped into a world they don't understand. Contrary to this allowing an excuse for metaknowledge, I think it discourages it if a Mummy wakes up in 2019 and has no idea what a car is or, indeed, even a horse is or how to work one. To me, this was kind of the core of Mummy's appeal - this sense of age, like everything has been done before and will be done again, of being so used to everything, being so bored of humanity and their temporary little creations even as you try to hold on to it, or even get it back in Akenakhi's case. Making that into prophecy of what is yet to come utterly changes the dynamic of Mummy in, I think, a less interesting way.<br /> I never felt like there was any issue with starting experience not making sense. It's generally assumed that you've earned experience to get to the starting point, after all - that's why Werewolves start at 7 Harmony and not 10 like it says new-changes are. It just represents more time here. Likewise, I felt like not quite having all of Arisen cosmology down the first time you play makes sense and works with the idea of poor memory.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm also concerned with the idea of Judges being statted beings that show up in-game. I liked it best when I could only splutter uselessly at my Judge and have no actual chance at hurting them in any meaningful way. Facing the inevitable seemed like a core theme of 1e Mummy, and making Judges something you can overcome, no matter how difficult, I think takes away from that. That and the Gentleman Gamer mentioning that serving your Judge can increase your Memory. I don't like that at all.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely sorry to say it, but I've come out of this teaser a lot less enthused about Mummy than I was going in. I'm still excited about what it ends up being, but now I'm considering it may well just not be something I enjoy as much as first edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can always play Mummy the Curse 2nd Edition linearly using Dark Eras. 1st Descent in modern day seems to be the default, but Storytellers and players can always play as they like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T06:16:46-07:00","id":1308292,"title":"","content":"True enough, but it being the default assumption still doesn't sit right with me, partly because it being a default assumption may well effect other parts of the game, and partly because &quot;you can houserule it away&quot; doesn't really change it from the default. If I want to play, rather than run, then I can assume most Storytellers are going to run it using the default assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T09:50:56-07:00","id":1308317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1307864#post1307864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, not! Last time I spoke to Malcolm (who is now very busy at Green Ronin: they just announced the setting for the gameline he's Developer of) he was of the same opinion as me; Mummy was something we greatly enjoyed working on, and have no desire to work on again. It'd be <i>weird</i>.<br /> <br /> Personally, the changes Matthew and his team have teased to the gameline sound brilliant, and I hope the game becomes as popular as it deserves to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>The changes do sound good. I'm a big fan of the non-linear experience Arisen are going to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T04:14:10-07:00","id":1308455,"title":"","content":"Finally got round to watching it. I think the XP problem is a red herring. It only appears an issue because RPGs tend to quantify skills into a linear progression. If the result is odd, that's because the XP mechanic is inherently kinda dodgy. It comes across as trying to fit the setting to a mechanic rather than the other way around.<br /> <br /> Also, I think expecting adding non-linear time to the game to not radically alter the feel of the game is unlikely to succeed.<br /> <br /> That being said, I actually really like the ideas themselves, and honestly I'd rather the new writers do something interesting and break with the previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T13:16:30-07:00","id":1308516,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see more development on Twilight, locations that can be found there and the &quot;society&quot; of the ghosts who linger there. Maybe start with expanding the &quot;pits&quot; leading to the realm of the devourer alluded to in Book of the Deceived, where they can be found and what might cause them to open in this modern age. Since a mummy can theoretically spend a good portion of its existence in Neter Khertet we should have it fully fleshed out and made more interesting than it currently is. Likewise I hope ghosts continue to play a significant part in the story and some exploration on how their interactions differ from say Sin Eaters or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T16:11:33-07:00","id":1308541,"title":"","content":"I gotta say, now that I've actually had a few moments to really think about it, there's an enormous onus of responsibility on the GM all of a sudden that wasn't there (to the same degree) in the first edition of Mummy. When a player makes a character in Mummy first edition, they know who their character is in the present day. That gives the GM a pretty reasonable starting point to work from when creating flashback scenes, because they can imagine the story a character could have gone on to get to where they are today. But by making the &quot;flashbacks&quot; actually reveal elements of that character's future, that puts everyone involved in an awkward position. If you show an Arisen as a particular kind of character in a future Descent, that can create some real cognitive dissonance if the players take their character in a very different direction in play. Even creating playable flashbacks just shifts the onus of responsibility onto the player, and they may feel constrained in their future roleplaying decisions by how they played themselves as future characters.<br /> <br /> Can't say I disagree with Michael's point that it's a problem that isn't really a problem. I don't recall anyone seriously complaining that Arisen only started with 20 experience in first edition, especially given that the game explicitly makes them amnesiacs. I mean, it's not like every roleplay game ever hasn't had to grapple with this same issue to some degree (i.e. &quot;Why is my 40 year old character at the same experience as the 16 year old, when they've both gained in skill at the same speed for the last six months of game time?&quot;). Arguably, Mummy had a better explanation than most games in just going, &quot;Well, you forgot most of what you spent you experience on previously&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'll be interested to see how the game addresses those problems, because I can't imagine they've gone unaddressed. The only one I can think of is if any flashforward style segments are meant to still be the present day Arisen's mind suddenly being projected into their future (past?) self, which actually eats away at a good bit of the fun of Mummy (remembering who you were, or I guess will be in this scenario). The non-linear approach to time is still interesting, and I hope it's executed well, but it seems to throw up a lot of roleplay hurdles just to fix a minor mechanical one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T17:22:55-07:00","id":1308548,"title":"","content":"The modern day does not have to be your first Descent. Just putting it out there.<br /> The non-linear stuff is an option and one you can make use of to great effect but we aren't bound by it at any particular point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T17:26:15-07:00","id":1308550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308548#post1308548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The modern day does not have to be your first Descent. Just putting it out there.<br /> The non-linear stuff is an option and one you can make use of to great effect but we aren't bound by it at any particular point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder how much this will have to be repeated throughout the road to 2nd edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T18:35:01-07:00","id":1308561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308548#post1308548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The modern day does not have to be your first Descent. Just putting it out there.<br /> The non-linear stuff is an option and one you can make use of to great effect but we aren't bound by it at any particular point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chronicles of Darkness is a toolbox by nature, and I'm always cognizant of my ability to mod games or just use 1st edition setting with 2nd edition mechanics for that matter. I do find the non-linear approach to time interesting, but the modern day not being your first descent doesn't actually address the issue of how to handle &quot;flashforwards&quot; to your future self in a way that feels respectful to player agency and non-limiting to roleplaying character arcs.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just don't use X&quot; is the least interesting solution to handling problems with any mechanic, and one I hope the Mummy team doesn't default to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T18:59:33-07:00","id":1308564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308561#post1308561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness is a toolbox by nature, and I'm always cognizant of my ability to mod games or just use 1st edition setting with 2nd edition mechanics for that matter. I do find the non-linear approach to time interesting, but the modern day not being your first descent doesn't actually address the issue of how to handle &quot;flashforwards&quot; to your future self in a way that feels respectful to player agency and non-limiting to roleplaying character arcs.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just don't use X&quot; is the least interesting solution to handling problems with any mechanic, and one I hope the Mummy team doesn't default to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure they will address how to handle flash-forwards along with flash-backs. if they dont, well that's a HUGE oversight<br /> <br /> EDIT: I wouldn't be surprised if one of the devs for the game are looking at this thread right now and taking this concern into account","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T16:53:12-07:00","id":1308825,"title":"","content":"Additional, I fully expect you can mix and match.<br /> I doubt there will be any issue with a modern Descent having flashbacks to the first Sothic turn or the Reign of Terror and a flashforward to the fall of Isireion.<br /> Nonlinar time can do that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T09:52:30-07:00","id":1308945,"title":"","content":"Look! Minor Guilds are a thing now <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/maar-kherit-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/maar-kherit-m...e-2nd-edition/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T09:56:07-07:00","id":1308947,"title":"","content":"Wut.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">words words words</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:14:18-07:00","id":1308951,"title":"","content":"Not my writing, but I am so glad this got un-[REDACTED] so early. The Maar-Kherit are awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:17:19-07:00","id":1308952,"title":"","content":"so are minor guilds unplayable? these poor medicine men seem to live quite a horrible iteration of life magic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:27:45-07:00","id":1308962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308281#post1308281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also concerned with the idea of Judges being statted beings that show up in-game. <b>I liked it best when I could only splutter uselessly at my Judge and have no actual chance at hurting them in any meaningful way.</b> Facing the inevitable seemed like a core theme of 1e Mummy, and making Judges something you can overcome, no matter how difficult, I think takes away from that. That and the Gentleman Gamer mentioning that serving your Judge can increase your Memory. I don't like that at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry to say this, but your rulebook seems to be missing several pages. Specifically, the part about Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> Yeah, you may not have <i>directly injured </i>your Judge, but condemning him to an eternity of screaming uselessly after being put on perma-mute is roughly like mooning Zeus and forcing him to send you to Elysium. You have just upended an entire cosmological view and proven the Judge isn't actually that powerful.<br /> <br /> That, and this philosophy is boring. Even Call of Cthulhu understands that; you may have to lower your expectations a bit, but knocking out Nyarlathotep for another few generations is not &quot;powerless.&quot; Beyond that, in Mummy, you are playing a god. No, there is not &quot;but&quot; here, you are playing a human who was remade into a god, however minor. And the thing about gods is that they often have a talent for overcoming older gods, especially in the myths of Egyptian culture and its Middle Eastern peers; Ra and Apep, Marduk and Tiamat, Gabriel and Rahab. Being the eternal toady of a completely inhuman god just isn't accurate to the culture.<br /> <br /> Besides, I've read the Storyteller's Vault writing guide; if anything, 2E is more fatalistic about the Arisen role in the world, explicitly so. It's far more humanistic, because it embraces art as a fundamental expression of humanity, but it's also made in the recognition that Irem and its influence is eternal; you will never <i>not </i>be a child of the Nameless Empire, and that includes its cosmology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T10:43:52-07:00","id":1308967,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the likelihood of any mummy to be able to just throw down with a Judge is slim. These entities are gods. Opposing them is a chronicle arc lasting multiple Descents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:41:39-07:00","id":1309038,"title":"","content":"My thoughts on the changes to second edition have been pretty cautious and wary so far. I feel like I've spent so much time defending Mummy and explaining why it not only works but it works <i>well</i> that I've entrenched myself in 1e so hard that I can't budge and now I'm just a grognard about it.<br /> <br /> With that all said, I really like the Malignant, and I'm curious about other minor Guilds and their role. I hope it doesn't come across <i>too </i>contrived now if there's all these additional setting elements that <i>all</i> come from Irem, but it was the greatest magical empire ever I suppose. I do wonder if something like the Malignant couldn't have just been wrapped up in with the Deceived or Shuankhsen but those two are so full of their own beauty and tragedies that maybe the Malignant do deserve to be their own thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T16:47:00-07:00","id":1309040,"title":"","content":"I loved the Blight! I wonder if there is a minor guild linked to all five of the main guilds, some as antagonists like Blight, some who have sought immortality through other means, or some surviving only as ghosts drawing essence form the eternal influence of Irem on the art of the humanity....<br /> <br /> Separate question: Is Apotheosis going to continue as a possible endgame in Mummy the Curse 2nd edition? I was always intrigued by it as a concept and the idea of giving up the full potential of power in exchange for freedom to choose your own path always resonated strongly with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T17:06:39-07:00","id":1309043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308962#post1308962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry to say this, but your rulebook seems to be missing several pages. Specifically, the part about Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the core details of Apotheosis and what it actually <i>means</i> aren't actually immediately accessible to a player in 1E Mummy.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm confident MrBreaksIt is well acquainted with Apotheosis, seeing as the character he mentions spent a pretty sizable Chronicle trying to achieve it. Hence why he had to spit at his Judge so often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T18:34:19-07:00","id":1309065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1308962#post1308962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've read the Storyteller's Vault writing guide;</div> </div> </div> </div>Where could I find this? Is it actually in the Storyteller's Vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-30T18:37:28-07:00","id":1309066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1309065#post1309065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where could I find this? Is it actually in the Storyteller's Vault?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. There's <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1281365#post1281365\">a link</a> earlier in the thread, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T07:03:21-07:00","id":1309429,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Deceived have in minor guilds associated with them? Maybe those poor Iremite Pharaohs who were basically chosen as sacrifices to honor Azar by being sliced to pieces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T12:59:49-07:00","id":1309493,"title":"","content":"so are these minor guilds playable? the Blights seem to only be tragic antagonists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-02T16:43:47-07:00","id":1309537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1309493#post1309493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so are these minor guilds playable? the Blights seem to only be tragic antagonists</div> </div> </div> </div>Unknown, but I'd say it is unlikely.<br /> Minor guilds are a new thing and I am under the impression that the &quot;Blight&quot; preview is the only example we have.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also note that the Maar-Kherit and the Shuankshen share a lot thematically, though the latter do appear trapped forever at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":1624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","user":"FallenEco","date":". 05-02-2019, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T12:09:31-07:00","id":1309716,"title":"","content":"Huh, I guess <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> is pre-empting the MMN a bit. Since according to a post in the OPP Facebook group, MtC2e just got out of Redlines and is now in Second Drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-03T12:26:14-07:00","id":1309722,"title":"","content":"Keep making the game awesome, writers! Ganbatte!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:31:07-07:00","id":1310862,"title":"","content":"Okay. This? This right here actually gets me more excited for 2nd edition than I have been in a long time. Not the cult itself, which sounds interesting but probably would not be of much use in my own games. <br /> <br /> Its the format, ya'll. Its all about the format.<br /> <br /> What we are given here is a very short but succinct look at an arisen cult, this particular one combining Scandinavian Christian traditions with Iremite customs. They are given a short history, goals, and induction ceremonies about a paragraph long. This excites me because it implies something the 1e lacked. Direct examples of what kinds of scorpion cults there are and what they do. Yeah, we had nice descriptions of one or two in books like Guildehalls, but most of them were dominated by a singular mummy. This entry indicates, at least I hope it indicates, that we will receive many examples of cults big and small, with lots of arisen or just one, with unique histories and goals.<br /> <br /> But the next sections are what really really get me excited. We have Judge Worship, Guild relations, and Rituals. <br /> <br /> If I am not reading too much into this, that means that any examples of Guilds the new edition will discuss will talk briefly about which Judges they serve and HOW and WHY they serve those judges, taking something I always struggled with making interesting and hammering out concrete examples of who serves the will of certain Judges and how they please them. I thrive on examples in the setting when looking for inspiration on building my own cults. So this is perfect.<br /> <br /> Guild relationship is straight forward, but gives a solid example of how a cult might interact with a guild and thus helps establish to look of a Nome in which the cult operates. <br /> <br /> Rituals appears to be a refinement of the sorcerer rules from Dark Eras companion Iserion. Basically, it implies sorcerous rites are a part of the Cult, perhaps as well a part of the Cult Merit. Each cult may in fact have rituals unique to that cult if I can read into the implications of the text. Which, frankly? Perfections. Excellent way to intergrate good ideas and make them specific to Mummy. <br /> <br /> Definitely getting second edition now. I was on the fence, but this clenches it.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2/posts/2489551\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects.../posts/2489551</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:40:38-07:00","id":1310864,"title":"","content":"My guess is the Minor Guilds are actually the Immortals, with this being one example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:44:39-07:00","id":1310867,"title":"","content":"I can't imagine all the immortals being Iremite in origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:56:34-07:00","id":1310868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1310867#post1310867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't imagine all the immortals being Iremite in origin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To be brutally honest, I'd be disappointed if they were. Unless one can be considered a &quot;minor guild&quot; in the sense that the Arisen guilds make a habit of &quot;adopting&quot; immortal traditions into the larger network as a kind of honorary mummy or something. Which...I would have mixed feelings about as well, but as one of the apparently few people who misses non egyptian mummies from Resurrections days I'd be okay with it. Mostly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T03:25:25-07:00","id":1311191,"title":"","content":"Non-Arisen Immortals are not Iremite in origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T04:25:06-07:00","id":1311194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1311191#post1311191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Arisen Immortals are not Iremite in origin.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Allows for awesome moments of &quot;What the Heck??!!&quot; as Immortals; Iremites and non-Iremites; discover or rediscover each other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T07:06:11-07:00","id":1312079,"title":"","content":"The preview of one of the main Guilds is up for everyone to see, folks. Here you go: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/maa-kep-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/\" target=\"_blank\">the 2nd Edition Maa-Kep</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T07:52:41-07:00","id":1312094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312079#post1312079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The preview of one of the main Guilds is up for everyone to see, folks. Here you go: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/maa-kep-mummy-the-curse-2nd-edition/&amp;quot;]the</a> 2nd Edition Maa-Kep[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Also,the reveal of the Wadjet-Itja!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T07:53:43-07:00","id":1312095,"title":"","content":"Wadjet-Itja is a new Guild, perhaps a minor Guild or a new major one as it was listed with the other major guilds. <br /> <br /> Wadjet-Itja means Green One Thief. Wadjet was a Goddess of Lower Egypt, Synchronized with Bast at times, who was originally the Protector of Lower Egypt. <br /> <br /> Could these be beings who found a way to steal Immortality from other Mummies, or an Iremite Thieves Guild? Could it be a reference to Body Thieves from Immortals?<br /> <br /> That would explain the hatred they recieve from the Iremite secret police because Body Thieves could spy on the cults and mess with the intelligence gathering with ease. They are immortal rivals (or perfect servants) for the Maa-Kep. <br /> <br /> Yeah the more I think on it, the more convinced I become that the minor Guilds are various kinds of Immortals, with the Wadjet-Itja being Body Thieves. <br /> <br /> Minor Guilds (Immortals) seem to be rivals and servants to the Mummies, a mix of allies and antagonists for Mummies the way Hobgoblins and Hedge Ghosts are for Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 05-14-2019, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T08:17:00-07:00","id":1312098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1311191#post1311191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-Arisen Immortals are not Iremite in origin.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, perhaps that undermines my theory of Minor Guilds = None Arisen Immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T09:42:17-07:00","id":1312111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312095#post1312095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wadjet-Itja is a new Guild, perhaps a minor Guild or a new major one as it was listed with the other major guilds.<br /> <br /> Wadjet-Itja means Green One Thief. Wadjet was a Goddess of Lower Egypt, Synchronized with Bast at times, who was originally the Protector of Lower Egypt.<br /> <br /> Could these be beings who found a way to steal Immortality from other Mummies, or an Iremite Thieves Guild? Could it be a reference to Body Thieves from Immortals?<br /> <br /> That would explain the hatred they recieve from the Iremite secret police because Body Thieves could spy on the cults and mess with the intelligence gathering with ease. They are immortal rivals (or perfect servants) for the Maa-Kep.<br /> <br /> Yeah the more I think on it, the more convinced I become that the minor Guilds are various kinds of Immortals, with the Wadjet-Itja being Body Thieves.<br /> <br /> Minor Guilds (Immortals) seem to be rivals and servants to the Mummies, a mix of allies and antagonists for Mummies the way Hobgoblins and Hedge Ghosts are for Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wadjet is also used as an alternate name for the Eye of Horus, the symbol that often pops up in regard to ancient Egypt (including the very eye that peeks out from underneath the sand on the cover of the 1e Core book for Mummy: the Curse). Mythology says Horus and Set fought over the throne of Osiris, and Set clawed out Horus' eye. Isis later restored the eye, and Horus tried to use its magic to resurrect Osiris. For this reason it symbolizes healing, sacrifice, resurrection and protection.<br /> <br /> &quot;Itja&quot;, according to the internet, means &quot;thief&quot; Thus- Thieves of Wadjet, or Thieves of the Eye of Horus. Since the myth involves Set this group could represent Apotheosis or something similar.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, since both Set and Horus are gods of war, this mysterious 7th Guild comes from the ranks of the army...or that failed rebellion mentioned in Book of the Deceived?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T09:42:32-07:00","id":1312112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312095#post1312095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wadjet-Itja is a new Guild, perhaps a minor Guild or a new major one as it was listed with the other major guilds.<br /> <br /> Yeah the more I think on it, the more convinced I become that the minor Guilds are various kinds of Immortals, with the Wadjet-Itja being Body Thieves.<br /> <br /> Minor Guilds (Immortals) seem to be rivals and servants to the Mummies, a mix of allies and antagonists for Mummies the way Hobgoblins and Hedge Ghosts are for Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of the Iremites giving non-Iremite immortals the name as a group label does sound pretty awesome! I like your logic here. Fits well with the concepts of Immortal Iremite pride and superiority that citizens of the Nameless Empire might largely share and the disdain they may have for 'pretenders' to their timeless nature.<br /> <br /> AND HOLY COW THAT PREVIEW OF THE MAA-KEP WAS AWESOME!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T10:33:10-07:00","id":1312121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312112#post1312112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea of the Iremites giving non-Iremite immortals the name as a group label does sound pretty awesome! I like your logic here. Fits well with the concepts of Immortal Iremite pride and superiority that citizens of the Nameless Empire might largely share and the disdain they may have for 'pretenders' to their timeless nature.<br /> <br /> AND HOLY COW THAT PREVIEW OF THE MAA-KEP WAS AWESOME!</div> </div> </div> </div>All credit goes to Meghan for her fantastic writing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T11:04:52-07:00","id":1312128,"title":"","content":"God, I love the Maa-Kep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T12:37:57-07:00","id":1312143,"title":"","content":"Does anyone else think that Junta and Dapifers are odd choices for nicknames? Usually in WoD/CofD games, the uncommon name is the splat name, and the nickname is something more informal and familiar. Like Nosferatu and Haunts or Mastigos and Warlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T12:50:58-07:00","id":1312144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312143#post1312143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone else think that Junta and Dapifers are odd choices for nicknames? Usually in WoD/CofD games, the uncommon name is the splat name, and the nickname is something more informal and familiar. Like Nosferatu and Haunts or Mastigos and Warlocks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought about it but yeah they kinda are. Like, calling the Maa-Kep as a whole The Junta sounds good, but A Junta is a bit odd.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe it's just me, but I had to look up Dapifers, so if the idea is to give them nicknames to help players round the unusual terminology, I don't think that does that.<br /> <br /> I guess we'll see if there's an explanation of the nicknames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-14T13:06:41-07:00","id":1312145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312144#post1312144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I hadn't thought about it but yeah they kinda are. Like, calling the Maa-Kep as a whole The Junta sounds good, but A Junta is a bit odd.<br /> <br /> Also, maybe it's just me, but I had to look up Dapifers, so if the idea is to give them nicknames to help players round the unusual terminology, I don't think that does that.<br /> <br /> I guess we'll see if there's an explanation of the nicknames.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. I see why they call themselves that (it's essentially Egyptian for &quot;steward&quot;), but &quot;junta&quot; is a term for a group of people, you sit on a Junta, you aren't one. (personal note), &quot;dapifier&quot; makes me think &quot;dapper&quot;, which makes me think that the Maa-Kep are a bunch of highly competent tailors and male politeness coaches).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T06:38:01-07:00","id":1312279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312121#post1312121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All credit goes to Meghan for her fantastic writing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is that confirmation that the Minor Guilds are just the Mummy given names for none Iremite Immortals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T07:07:19-07:00","id":1312285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312279#post1312279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is that confirmation that the Minor Guilds are just the Mummy given names for none Iremite Immortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It\u2019s giving credit where credit is due for the compliment given about the preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T08:02:34-07:00","id":1312293,"title":"","content":"It's already been said they are not called minor guilds if non iremite immortals. Minor guilds are iremite guilds who were deemed too unimportant to become mummies (I think)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T09:09:57-07:00","id":1312307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312293#post1312293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's already been said they are not called minor guilds if non iremite immortals. Minor guilds are iremite guilds who were deemed too unimportant to become mummies (I think)</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be better put as &quot;Iremite guilds who were not included in the Rite of Return, but still attained some form of immortality&quot; (the Maar-Kherit, for example, were eliminated for not going along with the Rite).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T09:21:28-07:00","id":1312311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312307#post1312307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Might be better put as &amp;quot;Iremite guilds who were not included in the Rite of Return, but still attained some form of immortality&amp;quot; (the Maar-Kherit, for example, were eliminated for not going along with the Rite).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T09:34:04-07:00","id":1312317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312095#post1312095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wadjet-Itja is a new Guild, perhaps a minor Guild or a new major one as it was listed with the other major guilds. <br /> <br /> Wadjet-Itja means Green One Thief. Wadjet was a Goddess of Lower Egypt, Synchronized with Bast at times, who was originally the Protector of Lower Egypt. <br /> <br /> Could these be beings who found a way to steal Immortality from other Mummies, or an Iremite Thieves Guild? Could it be a reference to Body Thieves from Immortals?<br /> <br /> That would explain the hatred they recieve from the Iremite secret police because Body Thieves could spy on the cults and mess with the intelligence gathering with ease. They are immortal rivals (or perfect servants) for the Maa-Kep. <br /> <br /> Yeah the more I think on it, the more convinced I become that the minor Guilds are various kinds of Immortals, with the Wadjet-Itja being Body Thieves. <br /> <br /> Minor Guilds (Immortals) seem to be rivals and servants to the Mummies, a mix of allies and antagonists for Mummies the way Hobgoblins and Hedge Ghosts are for Changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like how the Maar-Kherit was a sister Guild to the Su-Menent, the Wadjet-Itja could serve as a counter or even a mirror to the engravers- except where as the Physics fell and were swept aside, this Guild remained complicit and so underwent the Rite as normal. <br /> <br /> Perhaps this guild specialized in intelligence gathering and infiltration; but rather than maintaining order and acting as watchdogs within the Nameless Empire the Wadjet-Itja focused on perpetuating and expanding the Empire\u2019s influence and borders to other lands?<br /> <br /> <br /> A guild that trained people in magic and mundane skills to intergate, study, and undermine rival cultures in preparation for the hammer blow of Irem\u2019s armies: a guild that produced saboteurs and assassins to act as the vanguard wave of Iremite invasions? <br /> <br /> And now after it\u2019s fall, they continue on much as before, only now they are doing so according to a more personal agenda; subverting resources, mortals, and even magical power to forever expand their own influence within the world, sometimes alongside the Maa-Kep in order to perpetuate Iremite\u2019s values farther afield, most times in direct opposition in a sort of Spy Vs Spy kind of rivalry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 05-15-2019, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T11:23:18-07:00","id":1312346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312317#post1312317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much like how the Maar-Kherit was a sister Guild to the Su-Menent, the Wadjet-Itja could serve as a counter or even a mirror to the engravers- except where as the Physics fell and were swept aside, this Guild remained complicit and so underwent the Rite as normal.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this guild specialized in intelligence gathering and infiltration; but rather than maintaining order and acting as watchdogs within the Nameless Empire the Wadjet-Itja focused on perpetuating and expanding the Empire\u2019s influence and borders to other lands?<br /> <br /> <br /> A guild that trained people in magic and mundane skills to intergate, study, and undermine rival cultures in preparation for the hammer blow of Irem\u2019s armies: a guild that produced saboteurs and assassins to act as the vanguard wave of Iremite invasions?<br /> <br /> And now after it\u2019s fall, they continue on much as before, only now they are doing so according to a more personal agenda; subverting resources, mortals, and even magical power to forever expand their own influence within the world, sometimes alongside the Maa-Kep in order to perpetuate Iremite\u2019s values farther afield, most times in direct opposition in a sort of Spy Vs Spy kind of rivalry.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the idea that Wadjet-Itja is a minor Guild is unlikely for the simple fact that they are being mentioned alongside the established &quot;main&quot; guilds while the one minor guild we know about is unremarked upon. That implies to me that whatever the WI is is considered more important or at least distinguishable enough from other groups to be spoken of alongside them all.<br /> <br /> Also, my reading of minor guilds is that they were specialized groups overseen by the larger, broader Guild. Their area of expertise is finer than the main guilds but ultimately they are overseen by the larger guild who in turn reported to the six Shan'iatu of that Guild. I dunno if all members of a given minor guild are another form of immortal altogether or not. I suspect not, since it would make sense to me that the minor guilds would fall under the auspices of the major ones when it came time to pick for the Rite of Return. E.G.- nobody much cared if you were &quot;just&quot; a part of the major guild or specialized in a minor guild within the hierarchy of that major one. If you were a good servant, you made the cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T11:47:28-07:00","id":1312353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312346#post1312346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the idea that Wadjet-Itja is a minor Guild is unlikely for the simple fact that they are being mentioned alongside the established &quot;main&quot; guilds while the one minor guild we know about is unremarked upon. That implies to me that whatever the WI is is considered more important or at least distinguishable enough from other groups to be spoken of alongside them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, they're the Maa-Kep's associated minor Guild, as the Maar-Kherit are the Su-Menent's, and that's why they show up in their stereotypes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T13:32:56-07:00","id":1312393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312346#post1312346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say the idea that Wadjet-Itja is a minor Guild is unlikely for the simple fact that they are being mentioned alongside the established &amp;quot;main&amp;quot; guilds while the one minor guild we know about is unremarked upon. That implies to me that whatever the WI is is considered more important or at least distinguishable enough from other groups to be spoken of alongside them all.<br /> <br /> Also, my reading of minor guilds is that they were specialized groups overseen by the larger, broader Guild. Their area of expertise is finer than the main guilds but ultimately they are overseen by the larger guild who in turn reported to the six Shan'iatu of that Guild. I dunno if all members of a given minor guild are another form of immortal altogether or not. I suspect not, since it would make sense to me that the minor guilds would fall under the auspices of the major ones when it came time to pick for the Rite of Return. E.G.- nobody much cared if you were &amp;quot;just&amp;quot; a part of the major guild or specialized in a minor guild within the hierarchy of that major one. If you were a good servant, you made the cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize, I thought my mention of them undergoing the Rite solidified the notion that I was considering them to be a Fully established post Irem Guild that operated along with their peers. ^^;<br /> <br /> I do not think they are a Minor Guild, no. I used the term Sister Guild to convey commonality with the Maa-Kep, sorry to be confusing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T13:35:50-07:00","id":1312394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1312353#post1312353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, they're the Maa-Kep's associated minor Guild, as the Maar-Kherit are the Su-Menent's, and that's why they show up in their stereotypes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is admittedly a possibility, I guess we will all have to see when another guild preview happens to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-16T05:12:00-07:00","id":1312537,"title":"","content":"So they are likely a new major Guild, cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T13:49:40-07:00","id":1314158,"title":"","content":"So if the new Guild is a catch all for &quot;fake&quot; immortals, they logically wouldn't have their own version of a relic they specialized in. But who cares! Are there any forms of Egyptian magic or relics you can think of that are &quot;missing&quot; from the first edition that might pop up as a sixth ite