divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:31:48-07:00","id":1325565,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m curious if there is any non-spoilers y\u2019all can talk about in the meantime. For instance on the decrees- since talking about what\u2019s gonna be different is probably a no fly zone I\u2019m curious if there is anything from the old edition you felt strongly about carrying over into the new one. What about the decrees appealed to you and made you excited to be working on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T07:46:28-07:00","id":1325611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1130275-it-s-coming?p=1325565#post1325565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m curious if there is any non-spoilers y\u2019all can talk about in the meantime. For instance on the decrees- since talking about what\u2019s gonna be different is probably a no fly zone I\u2019m curious if there is anything from the old edition you felt strongly about carrying over into the new one. What about the decrees appealed to you and made you excited to be working on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s tricky to say much without getting into spoiler territory. Talking much about what\u2019s the same would also give an indication of what has changed by default, even if it doesn\u2019t say how or why. Saying things that haven\u2019t changed that wouldn\u2019t point to potential spoilers wouldn\u2019t be interesting enough to be worth it. <br /> Now, as to why I was excited to work on decrees? For one thing, writing up an official splat was high up on my freelancing bucket list. High enough up on it that I cheerfully traded my setting section to Chris for the opportunity, which was a win/win because he had some awesome ideas for one all set to go. It also allowed Chris and I a chance to work together on another part of the book (the two of us are also responsible for many of the new Conditions), and I\u2019d like to think that we make a pretty good team. One of our goals was to work together closely enough that they seemed to have been written by a single author, which is why I\u2019m looking forward to seeing how well we pulled that off. We also wanted to make each one fun and interesting to play, and I\u2019m happy to state that I\u2019d be delighted to play any of them in the new edition, so I\u2019d like to think we accomplished that as well. Time will tell.<br /> I do believe I just managed to ramble on without dropping any spoilers or even a [REDACTED]. The ninjas are eyeing me suspiciously, but they haven\u2019t attacked yet, so I might be in the clear here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-22T20:42:42-07:00","id":1326868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without obviously going into redacted territory. Can any of the freelancers talk about what drew them to write for the 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummies have always fascinated me. When I was a kid, the Mummy was my Universal monster of choice. I adored the Fruity Yummy Mummy cereal mascot, to the point that I dressed up as him for Halloween the year the cereal was released. To this day, there\u2019s an ancient My Pet Monster wearing the shirt from that costume. I also bitch about them not bringing back Fruity Yummy Mummy every year. When I would go to the museum, the Egyptian exhibits were the only thing that contended with the dinosaurs in my priorities. To be perfectly honest, it\u2019s surprising that I didn\u2019t end up becoming Kemetic with as much as I\u2019d loved Egypt. <br /> Years later, I would discover the glory of White Wolf role playing games. The first supplement I snagged for Vampire: The Masquerade was Mummy. The first antagonist I created for the game was a mummy (with the clever name of \u201cCleo\u201d, which took my friend\u2019s character all of half a second to declare was short for \u201cCleopatra\u201d). I was ecstatic when the next edition of Mummy came out, and grabbed it as soon as I could get my grubby little paws on it. I would be even more delighted when Mummy: The Resurrection was released. Could my beloved mummies finally be getting their own game? Sure, it was a \u201cmini game line\u201d, but they got one! But that would be nothing compared to my excitement when I learned of Mummy: The Curse, and I backed its Kickstarter in a heartbeat. By this point, the \u201cNew World of Darkness\u201d had already long won me over, so to see mummies getting their own game line was incredible. I loved it, and if I started dropping mummies into most of my nWoD games at this point, I could be forgiven. To be fair, I\u2019d been worse about dropping changelings into them. I loved MtC, despite aspects I considered flaws. Nothing\u2019s perfect, after all, and in general, it was all I could have hoped for. When I learned a second edition was planned, the possibilities seemed endless. I made a pitch for a new antagonist to Dixie and Matthew (no, it\u2019s not in there), and mentioned my interest in it. When the email came offering me a spot on the team, it was like my dream had come true. This project checks off several boxes on my freelancing bucket list, and I seriously can\u2019t wait to see what everyone thinks of the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-19T22:57:05-07:00","id":1331719,"title":"","content":"Art notes have been assembled!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blan